,"html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/37e2d59db994cb62bed14670563eaa34ecae9f6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:31:50Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:31:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sweeps on by default; SealPackage expired lease -> not-claimed (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#163)\n\n* feat(chart): sweep CronJobs on by default (ADR-0037)\n\nsweeps.enabled now defaults to true: expire-leases every minute,\nsweep-cpt-misses every 5 minutes, concurrencyPolicy Forbid, both schedules\nand the history limits configurable. The wget --post-data= invocation is\ncorrect for the two handlers (no body, no Content-Type, no Idempotency-Key);\nthe chart test now renders and asserts the command and the defaults.\n\nDocs: ADR-0037 + index, README, task-lifecycle, ddd pack hotspot rows and\nthe eventstorming diagram (decided 2026-10-06).\n\n* feat(task): SealPackage with a missing/expired lease returns not-claimed (ADR-0038)\n\nTask.VerifyHeldBy now returns ErrNotClaimed (409 task-not-claimed) for a\nmissing or expired lease, like Complete and RenewLease; an active lease held\nby another station stays ErrNotOwner (409 task-not-owner). Both errors were\nalready mapped to 409 with their own problem types, so errors.go is unchanged.\n\nTests: domain (expired / missing / other-station / parity with Complete and\nRenewLease), use case (TestSealPackage_RejectsExpiredLease etc.) and an HTTP\ntest asserting the problem types. OpenAPI 409 text updated and the API\nreference regenerated (docs-api-drift). Docs pack, sequence diagram and\nADR-0038 + index updated; domain_events documented as KEEP (legacy, unused).","tree":{"sha":"16f245a385cf6af0c52a60750d2d6589488a341e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/16f245a385cf6af0c52a60750d2d6589488a341e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/37e2d59db994cb62bed14670563eaa34ecae9f6e","verification":{"payload":"tree 16f245a385cf6af0c52a60750d2d6589488a341e\nparent d35d2449ac5e501b3b16127a5a6250aaffc25b00\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791329510 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791329510 -0300\n\nfeat: sweeps on by default; SealPackage expired lease -> not-claimed (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#163)\n\n* feat(chart): sweep CronJobs on by default (ADR-0037)\n\nsweeps.enabled now defaults to true: expire-leases every minute,\nsweep-cpt-misses every 5 minutes, concurrencyPolicy Forbid, both schedules\nand the history limits configurable. The wget --post-data= invocation is\ncorrect for the two handlers (no body, no Content-Type, no Idempotency-Key);\nthe chart test now renders and asserts the command and the defaults.\n\nDocs: ADR-0037 + index, README, task-lifecycle, ddd pack hotspot rows and\nthe eventstorming diagram (decided 2026-10-06).\n\n* feat(task): SealPackage with a missing/expired lease returns not-claimed (ADR-0038)\n\nTask.VerifyHeldBy now returns ErrNotClaimed (409 task-not-claimed) for a\nmissing or expired lease, like Complete and RenewLease; an active lease held\nby another station stays ErrNotOwner (409 task-not-owner). Both errors were\nalready mapped to 409 with their own problem types, so errors.go is unchanged.\n\nTests: domain (expired / missing / other-station / parity with Complete and\nRenewLease), use case (TestSealPackage_RejectsExpiredLease etc.) and an HTTP\ntest asserting the problem types. OpenAPI 409 text updated and the API\nreference regenerated (docs-api-drift). Docs pack, sequence diagram and\nADR-0038 + index updated; domain_events documented as KEEP (legacy, unused).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxYTmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXEYQAF09pdsNq2gkqTh4Qz/HYGrA\n4H6iKHZpSYzww2LNhIwmoxjWFtrHIguDHDsDHwPwKqmnj76i6+fByoCFIPlu+Tkt\nt1fZbhBRnEY/tWelhry+GslJwjKVhNitX54uiN7uy7ANjEeIREN7k5pz+SbCYGcU\nNcrdOZDvNaFoaqFNKlSIUhg6aca6Bx5+EGVXvqldjXdaWh8TWOacJwlTX4TFxIqT\ngL7+sv8bZlKvay/Qy1ieyIw7AybaeNI3JDXJPhX71D7IDpcfL0l2Xssa9d4DarhQ\npqPQmjS+ws+LwPYbS8wjkxRDK4BzFk1CRhJdHg96bx8Iv2Fo8AvOcPxCUw0kAbTK\nuoGdj9FDDNp/jY235M9dnE+Q4DpfyeAOZX3LsjFTh0FBEqsTSj0YRDetbbcAkb88\notX4KWFRMoFAkHb4S6BfTbbN2CDJyOK08Mp7V8nin8KrcARy7cbMZ6R7KfFgh8PZ\nuYjOj634JA3NtsKrJbJem3xsd52Kyj0XUIoZ8z8BxYPTZ28yvy4NeGQVeYFsFRKO\n94gHZIzH+IpQkn6Yym/XHpFKtD1Z95SipU/c/eXbcpbGVO8gNiPkm0EKj99r1S9y\nmZjT8ImIK40KuNb0lQUzULcENRJuvxbJOozCt3FagQluL0t1uwuES/M4ivs3d4UT\nJlBnoxArJ3VBNYUOU+d2\n=HELw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T23:31:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/37e2d59db994cb62bed14670563eaa34ecae9f6e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjB-doAKDM3ZTJkNTlkYjk5NGNiNjJiZWQxNDY3MDU2M2VhYTM0ZWNhZTlmNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/d35d2449ac5e501b3b16127a5a6250aaffc25b00","sha":"d35d2449ac5e501b3b16127a5a6250aaffc25b00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/d35d2449ac5e501b3b16127a5a6250aaffc25b00"}],"sha":"37e2d59db994cb62bed14670563eaa34ecae9f6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/37e2d59db994cb62bed14670563eaa34ecae9f6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/d35d2449ac5e501b3b16127a5a6250aaffc25b00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:56:56Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:56:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(transfer): DISPATCH/ARRIVAL task types, transfer completion facts, atomic WorkReleased consumption (#162)\n\n* feat(transfer): task types DISPATCH/ARRIVAL, transfer facts, atomic WorkReleased consumption (ADR-0036)\n\nInter-warehouse-transfer work enters through the existing single door:\nWorkReleased gains a strictly-additive optional correlation block\n(transfer_ref, work_kind, site_id, sku, quantity), work_unit_id stays\nthe Task''s OrderRef, and the block rides the Task as pure payload that\nnever affects claiming or leasing. New task types DISPATCH and ARRIVAL\njoin the catalogue-driven type set.\n\nFixes the pre-existing lost-WorkReleased bug first: the consumer claimed\nthe CloudEvents id BEFORE the catalogue lookup/CreateTask and OUTSIDE\ntheir UnitOfWork, so a failed create permanently suppressed redelivery.\nNew ApplyWorkReleased use case claims the id, validates the path_id,\nsaves the Task and publishes TaskCreated in ONE UnitOfWork (nested\nCreateTask joins it) — a port of wes-work-planning''s onceAtomically\n(ADR-0028); without a UnitOfWork the claim is undone via the new\noptional ports.ProcessedEventReleaser.\n\nCompletion of a task carrying transfer_ref raises exactly ONE fact\nselected by work_kind — TransferPicked | TransferDispatched |\nTransferArrived — alongside the unchanged TaskCompleted, committing with\nthe Completed state in the same outbox transaction. Type\ncom.warehouse.wes.fulfillment-execution.transfer.<Fact>, dataschema\nurn:warehouse:fulfillment-execution:events:<Fact>:v1, subject/key =\ntask_id, time = completion time. Non-transfer tasks emit no fact.\n\nStorage: migration 0014 adds six nullable correlation columns to tasks;\nNULL transfer_ref = not transfer work (legacy rows unchanged).\nContracts: asyncapi messages+schemas for the three facts, WorkReleased\noptional fields, task_type enums gain DISPATCH/ARRIVAL (asyncapi,\nopenapi, HTTP DTO, web console). Docs: ADR-0036, ADR-0032 type catalogue,\nintegration-contracts, process-paths, DDD diagrams.\n\nTests: unit (decode->persist->reload->completion field survival,\nper-work_kind fact selection, non-transfer no fact, unknown work_kind\nrejected, atomicity regression proving a failed create leaves no\nprocessed marker and redelivery creates exactly one task), golden wire\ntests per fact, and testcontainers e2e: WorkReleased with transfer\nfields -> DISPATCH task -> complete -> TaskCompleted + TransferDispatched\non the wire via the real outbox+relay; replay creates no dup.\n\n* docs(api): regenerate REST reference for DISPATCH/ARRIVAL task types","tree":{"sha":"83ed6bdbe906b9785e321755b82fc3ac4832a4c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/83ed6bdbe906b9785e321755b82fc3ac4832a4c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/d35d2449ac5e501b3b16127a5a6250aaffc25b00","verification":{"payload":"tree 83ed6bdbe906b9785e321755b82fc3ac4832a4c8\nparent fef3e15d04faae6e07df0d8472c82402abcf9082\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791327416 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791327416 -0300\n\nfeat(transfer): DISPATCH/ARRIVAL task types, transfer completion facts, atomic WorkReleased consumption (#162)\n\n* feat(transfer): task types DISPATCH/ARRIVAL, transfer facts, atomic WorkReleased consumption (ADR-0036)\n\nInter-warehouse-transfer work enters through the existing single door:\nWorkReleased gains a strictly-additive optional correlation block\n(transfer_ref, work_kind, site_id, sku, quantity), work_unit_id stays\nthe Task''s OrderRef, and the block rides the Task as pure payload that\nnever affects claiming or leasing. New task types DISPATCH and ARRIVAL\njoin the catalogue-driven type set.\n\nFixes the pre-existing lost-WorkReleased bug first: the consumer claimed\nthe CloudEvents id BEFORE the catalogue lookup/CreateTask and OUTSIDE\ntheir UnitOfWork, so a failed create permanently suppressed redelivery.\nNew ApplyWorkReleased use case claims the id, validates the path_id,\nsaves the Task and publishes TaskCreated in ONE UnitOfWork (nested\nCreateTask joins it) — a port of wes-work-planning''s onceAtomically\n(ADR-0028); without a UnitOfWork the claim is undone via the new\noptional ports.ProcessedEventReleaser.\n\nCompletion of a task carrying transfer_ref raises exactly ONE fact\nselected by work_kind — TransferPicked | TransferDispatched |\nTransferArrived — alongside the unchanged TaskCompleted, committing with\nthe Completed state in the same outbox transaction. Type\ncom.warehouse.wes.fulfillment-execution.transfer.<Fact>, dataschema\nurn:warehouse:fulfillment-execution:events:<Fact>:v1, subject/key =\ntask_id, time = completion time. Non-transfer tasks emit no fact.\n\nStorage: migration 0014 adds six nullable correlation columns to tasks;\nNULL transfer_ref = not transfer work (legacy rows unchanged).\nContracts: asyncapi messages+schemas for the three facts, WorkReleased\noptional fields, task_type enums gain DISPATCH/ARRIVAL (asyncapi,\nopenapi, HTTP DTO, web console). Docs: ADR-0036, ADR-0032 type catalogue,\nintegration-contracts, process-paths, DDD diagrams.\n\nTests: unit (decode->persist->reload->completion field survival,\nper-work_kind fact selection, non-transfer no fact, unknown work_kind\nrejected, atomicity regression proving a failed create leaves no\nprocessed marker and redelivery creates exactly one task), golden wire\ntests per fact, and testcontainers e2e: WorkReleased with transfer\nfields -> DISPATCH task -> complete -> TaskCompleted + TransferDispatched\non the wire via the real outbox+relay; replay creates no dup.\n\n* docs(api): regenerate REST reference for DISPATCH/ARRIVAL task types","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxXy4CRC1aQ7