kwDOUAjB-doAKDVhNzA1M2Y1OTg3NmU1MjNlZTRhZDczZWFiNjc3NmNmZjlhNmUyNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/eec428a7060450d0ea46c916ad52935bef6ed707","sha":"eec428a7060450d0ea46c916ad52935bef6ed707","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/eec428a7060450d0ea46c916ad52935bef6ed707"}],"sha":"5a7053f59876e523ee4ad73eab6776cff9a6e25f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/5a7053f59876e523ee4ad73eab6776cff9a6e25f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/eec428a7060450d0ea46c916ad52935bef6ed707/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:24:38Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:24:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#158)\n\n* fix(task): reject SealPackage when the caller''s lease has expired\n\nSealPackage compared only the lease''s station id, so a station whose lease\nhad lapsed (task still CLAIMED because no sweep ran) could still seal a\npackage. Add the read-only Task.VerifyHeldBy(stationId, now), which requires\na lease held by the caller that has not expired (inclusive boundary, same as\nComplete/RenewLease), and use it in SealPackage. Failure stays task.ErrNotOwner\n(409 task-not-owner), the contract openapi.yaml already documents, so there\nis no REST contract change.\n\nTests: Task.VerifyHeldBy domain tests; SealPackage rejects an expired lease\nand saves no package. Sequence diagram, aggregate canvas, use-cases and\ninvariants docs updated.\n\n* docs(api): expand CPT as Critical Pull Time in openapi.yaml\n\nFour openapi.yaml descriptions (info, createTask, CreateTaskRequest.cpt,\nArriveAtRebinRequest.cpt) expanded CPT as \"Committed Processing Time\"; the\ndomain (shared.CPT) and every other doc say \"Critical Pull Time\". Prose\nonly, no schema or behaviour change. Regenerated the docs API reference\n(clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs fulfillment) and updated the ubiquitous\nlanguage row that recorded the discrepancy.\n\n* docs(chart): correct what config.eventPublisher gates\n\nThe values.yaml comment said eventPublisher gates the TaskCompleted publisher\nonly. EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka selects both outbox encoders (integration and\nanalytics topics, composition.BuildEventPublisher) and the WorkReleased\nconsumer''s dead-letter writer (cmd/execution maybeWireDeadLetter). Comment\nonly; no value or template change.\n\n* feat(chart): opt-in CronJobs for the lease and CPT sweeps\n\nPOST /tasks/expire-leases and POST /tasks/sweep-cpt-misses have no\nin-process scheduler by design (ADR-0003 names a Kubernetes CronJob as the\nexternal scheduler; ADR-0025 rejected a ticker). Add sweeps.enabled (default\nfalse, so rendered output and behaviour are unchanged) which renders one\nCronJob per sweep that POSTs to the release''s own Service with busybox wget\nfrom the service image. Each sweep and its schedule can be toggled\nindependently; concurrencyPolicy is Forbid.\n\nTest: charts/fulfillment-execution/tests/test_sweeps_cronjob.py (default\nrenders nothing; enabled renders both with the right URLs; per-sweep toggle,\nschedule override, pods not matched by any Service). Docs that listed\n\"nothing schedules the sweeps\" updated; no endpoint, event or ADR body\nchanged.","tree":{"sha":"d28e984c87bdd93dd90a95f9d27d1c791c8fc4ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/d28e984c87bdd93dd90a95f9d27d1c791c8fc4ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/eec428a7060450d0ea46c916ad52935bef6ed707","verification":{"payload":"tree d28e984c87bdd93dd90a95f9d27d1c791c8fc4ee\nparent 1d18f3214774fd9b4db80c4918fd08c099c9f2d2\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791285878 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791285878 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#158)\n\n* fix(task): reject SealPackage when the caller''s lease has expired\n\nSealPackage compared only the lease''s station id, so a station whose lease\nhad lapsed (task still CLAIMED because no sweep ran) could still seal a\npackage. Add the read-only Task.VerifyHeldBy(stationId, now), which requires\na lease held by the caller that has not expired (inclusive boundary, same as\nComplete/RenewLease), and use it in SealPackage. Failure stays task.ErrNotOwner\n(409 task-not-owner), the contract openapi.yaml already documents, so there\nis no REST contract change.\n\nTests: Task.VerifyHeldBy domain tests; SealPackage rejects an expired lease\nand saves no package. Sequence diagram, aggregate canvas, use-cases and\ninvariants docs updated.\n\n* docs(api): expand CPT as Critical Pull Time in openapi.yaml\n\nFour openapi.yaml descriptions (info, createTask, CreateTaskRequest.cpt,\nArriveAtRebinRequest.cpt) expanded CPT as \"Committed Processing Time\"; the\ndomain (shared.CPT) and every other doc say \"Critical Pull Time\". Prose\nonly, no schema or behaviour change. Regenerated the docs API reference\n(clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs fulfillment) and updated the ubiquitous\nlanguage row that recorded the discrepancy.\n\n* docs(chart): correct what config.eventPublisher gates\n\nThe values.yaml comment said eventPublisher gates the TaskCompleted publisher\nonly. EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka selects both outbox encoders (integration and\nanalytics topics, composition.BuildEventPublisher) and the WorkReleased\nconsumer''s dead-letter writer (cmd/execution maybeWireDeadLetter). Comment\nonly; no value or template change.\n\n* feat(chart): opt-in CronJobs for the lease and CPT sweeps\n\nPOST /tasks/expire-leases and POST /tasks/sweep-cpt-misses have no\nin-process scheduler by design (ADR-0003 names a Kubernetes CronJob as the\nexternal scheduler; ADR-0025 rejected a ticker). Add sweeps.enabled (default\nfalse, so rendered output and behaviour are unchanged) which renders one\nCronJob per sweep that POSTs to the release''s own Service with busybox wget\nfrom the service image. Each sweep and its schedule can be toggled\nindependently; concurrencyPolicy is Forbid.\n\nTest: charts/fulfillment-execution/tests/test_sweeps_cronjob.py (default\nrenders nothing; enabled renders both with the right URLs; per-sweep toggle,\nschedule override, pods not matched by any Service). Docs that listed\n\"nothing schedules the sweeps\" updated; no endpoint, event or ADR body\nchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNp2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACu8QACbjdONdn2N5gQv6Jg8OUDJI\nCF5YZUXLNr7vqKzvIFFqFKli+PKmiTf8rMxJKLkYeH3NPxLWWtibNzb3fta0dnV4\n+BGUVcy3GQiFxYyyB9zChABVtAC37NhCCQSuwgi4wOTTV5nvGETJ6G1G5riWLj/p\n8Qzqwg+eyalOqiBRcSDt/sKhWKHIwFTjstsMqxSyenz3np4ygkH00rD7DYUbQrNN\nNmDsqusaPLXI/fqOb85mPvIxmX+ZvS+nS4X2VXbf6W9dNj+YDQctuOlvA8jIKYe1\nOpYnri9cINFcEQ4gmp1FgN9xSUritAiwF/2tg9NnLcrP7bSPf9j5X2ULTqLlJF65\nGUXUUT+QfQsjbRwQPzAcdyst0q2WRmvhiWnHv