MTE4OWNlYTdjYzc0OGQ3NTE5ZDBhOTQyMWY3ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/ba62e1804577a235a1633e1144a230bd654382ff","sha":"ba62e1804577a235a1633e1144a230bd654382ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/ba62e1804577a235a1633e1144a230bd654382ff"}],"sha":"d04ca261d8a1189cea7cc748d7519d0a9421f7ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/d04ca261d8a1189cea7cc748d7519d0a9421f7ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/ba62e1804577a235a1633e1144a230bd654382ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:51:57Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:51:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#153)\n\n* docs: refresh product docs against develop\n\nPart A of the docs refresh. Every change was checked against the code on\norigin/develop:\n\n- README and overview: Rebin as a first-class path, the IQVO docs URL,\n  all 19 routes with the router/OpenAPI parity test, readyz (ADR-0029),\n  Idempotency-Key (ADR-0028), the outbox and catalogue-source wiring,\n  and the arch-go subtests.\n- running-locally: the full env var set, including\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL,\n  WORK_RELEASED_CONSUMER_GROUP, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS and LOG_LEVEL, plus\n  the env vars of the other binaries.\n- ddd pages:\n  - Four aggregates, and station check-in/out is now exposed.\n  - SLAM returns 204, with the package read model (ADR-0033).\n  - 17 use cases, with the SaveClaim compare-and-set (ADR-0034) and the\n    full port method sets.\n  - Domain events give full CE types, both encoders, partition keys and\n    consumers.\n- Context map rewritten in ddd-crew notation with U/D and patterns.\n  Adds the process-path-management and warehouse-ops-agent edges.\n- Ubiquitous language: every term is mapped to its code identifier, and\n  terms whose code name differs are flagged.\n- API reference: 19/19 routes and the idempotency problem types.\n- ADR index: the ADR-0008 status note. The docs-api-drift rule now says\n  the job only gates PRs into main.\n- Admonitions use the bracket title form.\n- Stale claudioed org links changed to IQVO in .claude docs.\n\n* docs(ddd): add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack\n\nPart B. Adds the ddd-crew pack under docs/docs/ddd, wired into the\nsidebar as a \"DDD artifacts (ddd-crew)\" category:\n\n- ddd-artifacts: the index page, plus the sources of truth.\n- core-domain-chart: a quadrantChart and the evolution note.\n- bounded-context-canvas: canvas v5. Every message maps to a real route,\n  MCP tool or CloudEvents type.\n- aggregate-design-canvas: Task, Station, Package and\n  OrderConsolidation, each with a stateDiagram.\n- domain-message-flow: four scenarios using cmd/evt/qry arrows.\n- eventstorming: three design-level boards with a sticky inventory.\n- class-diagram: domain model, domain events, and the hexagonal view.\n- entity-relationship: the OLTP and analytics schemas. Neither has any\n  foreign keys.\n- sequence-diagrams: nine use-case flows, including the idempotency\n  middleware, the claim compare-and-set and the outbox relay.\n\nThe context map, ubiquitous language and domain events pages are linked\nfrom the index and are not duplicated.\n\nMermaid validator: 35/35 diagrams render, 0 failed.\n\n* docs: fix CI-gating claims and remaining stale org links\n\n- subdomain-classification: mutation-fast runs on every push and PR. Only\n  the full mutation job runs on schedule or dispatch.\n- api-reference/index: the docs-api-drift job runs on every push and PR.\n- docs/README: the published site is now the IQVO URL. The API reference\n  is generated by gen-api-docs and committed, not built at build time.\n- SECURITY.md: the advisory link now points to the IQVO org.","tree":{"sha":"c94fd7f5530a4ba30ad3f319bb4e54ad5cfe7f26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/c94fd7f5530a4ba30ad3f319bb4e54ad5cfe7f26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/ba62e1804577a235a1633e1144a230bd654382ff","verification":{"payload":"tree c94fd7f5530a4ba30ad3f319bb4e54ad5cfe7f26\nparent bd007158ee2a10ddc337a091f4545efc19d53eff\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791255117 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791255117 -0300\n\ndocs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#153)\n\n* docs: refresh product docs against develop\n\nPart A of the docs refresh. Every change was checked against the code on\norigin/develop:\n\n- README and overview: Rebin as a first-class path, the IQVO docs URL,\n  all 19 routes with the router/OpenAPI parity test, readyz (ADR-0029),\n  Idempotency-Key (ADR-0028), the outbox and catalogue-source wiring,\n  and the arch-go subtests.\n- running-locally: the full env var set, including\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL,\n  WORK_RELEASED_CONSUMER_GROUP, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS and LOG_LEVEL, plus\n  the env vars of the other binaries.\n- ddd pages:\n  - Four aggregates, and station check-in/out is now exposed.\n  - SLAM returns 204, with the package read model (ADR-0033).\n  - 17 use cases, with the SaveClaim compare-and-set (ADR-0034) and the\n    full port method sets.\n  - Domain events give full CE types, both encoders, partition keys and\n    consumers.\n- Context map rewritten in ddd-crew notation with U/D and patterns.\n  Adds the process-path-management and warehouse-ops-agent edges.\n- Ubiquitous language: every term is mapped to its code identifier, and\n  terms whose code name differs are flagged.\n- API reference: 19/19 routes and the idempotency problem types.\n- ADR index: the ADR-0008 status note. The docs-api-drift rule now says\n  the job only gates PRs into main.\n- Admonitions use the bracket title form.\n- Stale claudioed org links changed to IQVO in .claude docs.\n\n* docs(ddd): add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack\n\nPart B. Adds the ddd-crew pack under docs/docs/ddd, wired into the\nsidebar as a \"DDD artifacts (ddd-crew)\" category:\n\n- ddd-artifacts: the index page, plus the sources of truth.\n- core-domain-chart: a quadrantChart and the evolution note.\n- bounded-context-canvas: canvas v5. Every message maps to a real route,\n  MCP tool or CloudEvents type.\n- aggregate-design-canvas: Task, Station, Package and\n  OrderConsolidation, each with a stateDiagram.\n- domain-message-flow: four scenarios using cmd/evt/qry arrows.\n- eventstorming: three design-level boards with a sticky inventory.\n- class-diagram: domain model, domain events, and the hexagonal view.\n- entity-relationship: the OLTP and analytics schemas. Neither has any\n  foreign keys.\n- sequence-diagrams: nine use-case flows, including the idempotency\n  middleware, the claim compare-and-set and the outbox relay.\n\nThe context map, ubiquitous language and domain events pages are linked\nfrom the index and are not duplicated.\n\nMermaid validator: 35/35 diagrams render, 0 failed.\n\n* docs: fix CI-gating claims and remaining stale org links\n\n- subdomain-classification: mutation-fast runs on every push and PR. Only\n  the full mutation job runs on schedule or dispatch.\n- api-reference/index: the docs-api-drift job runs on every push and PR.\n- docs/README: the published site is now the IQVO URL. The API reference\n  is generated by gen-api-docs and committed, not built at build time.\n- SECURITY.md: the advisory link now points to the IQVO org.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxGJNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyKAQAAIFhopvb2BA54cxjUPk06Bv\ne2cdF8huxpVLEXdgF6mmwGmAKMpjj/oP+H+Hs82cKhKRJ2h/47n7XN2cAFfHVCrG\nU0aYCmhlFt3OYYSc5WNCICwFCnn/7Zao76ZjNQ0Ah0KJ6EPe9362qC4SPbEH9DUf\neWOq/T5haGk4XicwWuItMukfKeuHf0ul4dEptjVj7b9RPzfp2KWk5UkFdsM8XUMf\ng4J/ujpLIMK5a8x0fsKy8Lie5KCSW6SNGfE/3CZP8g0Vgkj2YJGwAB7gGc112QRX\nWqP5H8SpB/qTVaIaZ6V1tE2mxfd6m6X9DFM3CCSrKLc8fzkRb0yoQxqbbtvrB+3t\nmSwhabh3UmAf+w7HEC/B9LzS62DXYMV5tio3iVyuZJ01qEa+WZQyEwwELLt3ztUL\nVVQkfChQFdzSE6LE7BCtX/MoKJLFODIdYxH6m7j1Eke6VooUY9HhSprXW93B8XVR\nGah5GCUgBRRzzHRkXT5b0LjDkgSVWPQmUDH5xy83DtqxNgB+W/CcKHPpU4ydFxqj\n16MYPrX0WgsNAep5kc4cUGdrOjjiQ6mBN9skyib0JzpTIgOHWJJ+6cvdMA5mrAaj\nWjCzuyhz+V9SZyGzc3TkVkrHxrJszy4leJVSGUUkotFYPwQXb1bQSZbGhc7pShD5\n4n0qDLiYAEMfxyiDpb0j\n=nVf7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T02:51:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3",