on/commit/0ecb052348bad3186bbac31bc11d7f8260a22ee2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjB-doAKDBlY2IwNTIzNDhiYWQzMTg2YmJhYzMxYmMxMWQ3ZjgyNjBhMjJlZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/59d7af37c9d604fd4e8d2ac84ad0bc3e1122c3dd","sha":"59d7af37c9d604fd4e8d2ac84ad0bc3e1122c3dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/59d7af37c9d604fd4e8d2ac84ad0bc3e1122c3dd"}],"sha":"0ecb052348bad3186bbac31bc11d7f8260a22ee2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/0ecb052348bad3186bbac31bc11d7f8260a22ee2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/59d7af37c9d604fd4e8d2ac84ad0bc3e1122c3dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:57:37Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:57:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ADR-conformance audit fixes (MCP outbox, probes, otelchimetric, consolidation lock, docs) (#148)\n\n* fix: MCP complete_task publishes via the shared outbox; readyz probe; otelchimetric on all routers; Idempotency-Key CORS\n\n- internal/composition.BuildEventPublisher shared by cmd/execution and cmd/mcp (relay only in cmd/execution); cmd/mcp builds CompleteTask with publisher + UnitOfWork (ADR-0008/0020)\n- chart: mcp EVENT_PUBLISHER/KAFKA_BROKERS; readinessProbe -> /readyz (ADR-0029)\n- replace hand-rolled httpmetrics with otelchi+otelchimetric on main, reports and MCP routers (ADR-0019)\n- CORS AllowedHeaders includes Idempotency-Key (ADR-0028)\n- tests: testcontainers MCP complete_task outbox test, chart probe test, router metric tests\n\n* fix: serialize concurrent rebin arrivals per order; ADR-0034 records consolidation lock and claim CAS\n\nArriveAtRebin now does its read-modify-write inside the UnitOfWork via FindByOrderRefForUpdate (pg_advisory_xact_lock + SELECT FOR UPDATE), so concurrent arrivals no longer overwrite each other (last-writer-wins) and the PACK task is created once. Adds a testcontainers race test (8 goroutines, one order). ADR-0034 also documents SaveClaim''s compare-and-set; fixes ADR-0002/0003 text.\n\n* fix: deterministic SLAM task pick for on-time KPI; test: enforce analytics isolation\n\n- AnalyticsPublisher.pickSlamTask: with a retried SLAM leg, prefer a worked task over an abandoned Pending one (then latest claim, then lowest id). Package.TaskId is the PACK task, so correlation stays on OrderRef; ADR-0026 corrected accordingly.\n- arch-go rules: internal/analytics/** imports nothing internal; domain/application do not import analytics (ADR-0012).\n\n* fix: align DLQ writer with fleet writer config; docs: Idempotency-Key in OpenAPI, ADR drift fixes, ADR-0035\n\n- DLQ writer: Hash balancer, RequireAll, 10ms batch via outboundkafka.NewDeadLetterWriter (ADR-0035)\n- openapi: POST /tasks Idempotency-Key header, 400 idempotency-key-required, 422 idempotency-key-reused; docs regenerated (clean-api-docs then gen-api-docs)\n- ADR-0008: auth/scope/rate-limit text superseded by ADR-0022, spans-only observability, dangling ADR-0009 ref\n- ADR-0001/0004/0005/0007/0012/0013/0015/0017/0019/0029 count/title/historical-text fixes\n- new ADR-0035 (Kafka hash partition key); index + sidebar updated\n\n* fix: declare Idempotency-Key optional in the OpenAPI schema (in-memory contract-test config does not enforce it)\n\nSchemathesis runs against the in-memory server, where RequireIdempotencyKey is skipped, so a required header made the contract job fail. The description still tells clients to always send it and documents the 400/422 behaviour of Postgres-backed deployments. Docs regenerated.\n\n* fix: drop minLength from the Idempotency-Key schema (in-memory contract config accepts empty keys)\n\nDocs regenerated.","tree":{"sha":"62cb0ef89e07986a698efddd8443ceb1b84093c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/62cb0ef89e07986a698efddd8443ceb1b84093c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/59d7af37c9d604fd4e8d2ac84ad0bc3e1122c3dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 62cb0ef89e07986a698efddd8443ceb1b84093c9\nparent f1f2ef01fe2ebda55680b4b91f6d63c36ec02669\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791154657 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791154657 -0300\n\nfix: ADR-conformance audit fixes (MCP outbox, probes, otelchimetric, consolidation lock, docs) (#148)\n\n* fix: MCP complete_task publishes via the shared outbox; readyz probe; otelchimetric on all routers; Idempotency-Key CORS\n\n- internal/composition.BuildEventPublisher shared by cmd/execution and cmd/mcp (relay only in cmd/execution); cmd/mcp builds CompleteTask with publisher + UnitOfWork (ADR-0008/0020)\n- chart: mcp EVENT_PUBLISHER/KAFKA_BROKERS; readinessProbe -> /readyz (ADR-0029)\n- replace hand-rolled httpmetrics with otelchi+otelchimetric on main, reports and MCP routers (ADR-0019)\n- CORS AllowedHeaders includes Idempotency-Key (ADR-0028)\n- tests: testcontainers MCP complete_task outbox test, chart probe test, router metric tests\n\n* fix: serialize concurrent rebin arrivals per order; ADR-0034 records consolidation lock and claim CAS\n\nArriveAtRebin now does its read-modify-write inside the UnitOfWork via FindByOrderRefForUpdate (pg_advisory_xact_lock + SELECT FOR UPDATE), so concurrent arrivals no longer overwrite each other (last-writer-wins) and the PACK task is created once. Adds a testcontainers race test (8 goroutines, one order). ADR-0034 also documents SaveClaim''s compare-and-set; fixes ADR-0002/0003 text.\n\n* fix: deterministic SLAM task pick for on-time KPI; test: enforce analytics isolation\n\n- AnalyticsPublisher.pickSlamTask: with a retried SLAM leg, prefer a worked task over an abandoned Pending one (then latest claim, then lowest id). Package.TaskId is the PACK task, so correlation stays on OrderRef; ADR-0026 corrected accordingly.\n- arch-go rules: internal/analytics/** imports nothing internal; domain/application do not import analytics (ADR-0012).\n\n* fix: align DLQ writer with fleet writer config; docs: Idempotency-Key in OpenAPI, ADR drift fixes, ADR-0035\n\n- DLQ writer: Hash balancer, RequireAll, 10ms batch via outboundkafka.NewDeadLetterWriter (ADR-0035)\n- openapi: POST /tasks Idempotency-Key header, 400 idempotency-key-required, 422 idempotency-key-reused; docs regenerated (clean-api-docs then gen-api-docs)\n- ADR-0008: auth/scope/rate-limit text superseded by ADR-0022, spans-only observability, dangling ADR-0009 ref\n- ADR-0001/0004/0005/0007/0012/0013/0015/0017/0019/0029 count/title/historical-text fixes\n- new ADR-0035 (Kafka hash partition key); index + sidebar updated\n\n* fix: declare Idempotency-Key optional in the OpenAPI schema (in-memory contract-test config does not enforce it)\n\nSchemathesis runs against the in-memory server, where RequireIdempotencyKey is skipped, so a required header made the contract job fail. The description still tells clients to always send it and documents the 400/422 behaviour of Postgres-backed deployments. Docs regenerated.\n\n* fix: drop minLength from the Idempotency-Key schema (in-memory contract config accepts empty keys)\n\nDocs regenerated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtnhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtCgQABcBA8MU2k5q4CWizRo9ojR4\nVsfMw1qJc2T/3OtNLFvtSXOQobqpSB985A0CxK/7FdIuXFKAY6N/ohvJl9yBFuYP\nt7EuRxYPn0h9n8H+37PdbIZfVslyAPael26+pdjLPy2X4PbDTSLCOtxJXRUYSonO\nFacyRQtdSlS9OYEbyfUcQahN2pdFJwlXjXodFqdj/ImVLkF5KdTor3IjTzD3hi25\nzYju2Uj4jTCwwGMJtVLlgoLqlLIzc9V0TdbYAm75JKr7pVNmI2RdpQR+bVDx6gBC\nOctKSYbobBkQcRb8uzaXv3mNQO9Q3I6d+lYBVfiheOLiRcXRVzoWO1kzTyLH0kgx\nNAm2Je5SSHYJ9TShAR58Q/Gh7uiLJ54CwEtTgNakb0pAUk+D65qb7tE4pjnHhl57\nfYpJdxdlYc3cB0Osp3ksnBKkBdpWYEd/CyEKS+psOnX4RGo1G0QXi2iI5dsNsl8j\nGGJLe5jRFAjPOGVxcqIQetRSySreBP4bY801BIyWT7Y+e2WAhtvl2c+3gfuOPZnv\n8hQ3NAg6kn7wJlKUmtzXjZrtau05NaJvhcABoyYxbc5/7/ImMbbQQy79cBoS7D5/\nZCOMUq9JetqfCm6OuZVFldx5MpgBNoNYbLLxPQEtu0m4ph142Tk2ikrPnAd8naRX\n5GzvSA4Y58SYD/ooAx7o\n=on5M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T22:57:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"