bscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/e18d9bbad92f53fee3fd88b74fbbec3ad993ab5a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjB-doAKGUxOGQ5YmJhZDkyZjUzZmVlM2ZkODhiNzRmYmJlYzNhZDk5M2FiNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/1bcae2c251162eb9de7ac5ab915ded98ddf59cb4","sha":"1bcae2c251162eb9de7ac5ab915ded98ddf59cb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/1bcae2c251162eb9de7ac5ab915ded98ddf59cb4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/8b7113f9fb8e3b0a78f8e529b34765a78d5c208c","sha":"8b7113f9fb8e3b0a78f8e529b34765a78d5c208c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/8b7113f9fb8e3b0a78f8e529b34765a78d5c208c"}],"sha":"e18d9bbad92f53fee3fd88b74fbbec3ad993ab5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/e18d9bbad92f53fee3fd88b74fbbec3ad993ab5a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/1bcae2c251162eb9de7ac5ab915ded98ddf59cb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:21:55Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:21:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#124)\n\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver uses a session-scoped pg_advisory_lock\nto serialize concurrent migration runs. PgBouncer''s transaction-pooling\nmode (warehouse-infra PR #43) does not preserve session state across\nstatements, so any 2+ replicas of cmd/execution or cmd/mcp starting\nconcurrently (HPA scale-out per ADR-0030, or an ordinary multi-replica\nrolling deploy) crash-loop for 1-2 minutes with ''pq: unnamed prepared\nstatement does not exist'' before one wins the lock race.\n\ncmd/execution/main.go''s openStorage and cmd/mcp/main.go''s new\nbuildTaskRepo now read MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL for the migration step\nonly, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset so local dev and CI\nintegration tests keep working unchanged. The pgxpool built right after\nmigrations complete still uses DATABASE_URL/PgBouncer, unchanged.\n\ncharts/fulfillment-execution: new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey\nvalue renders MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL in the api and mcp Deployments\n(the two that run migrations), sourced from the same existingSecret,\nwith optional: true so a secret predating this key still starts the\npod. warehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions the secret key for all\n9 OLTP services, including this one -- no infra changes needed here.\n\nDirect port of order-management PR #115 / ADR-0029, this fleet''s Phase\n4 reference implementation. New ADR-0031 documents the rationale and\ncross-references order-management ADR-0029 and warehouse-infra PR\n#43/#44.\n\nTests added:\n- cmd/execution/migrations_test.go: TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback,\n  TestOpenStorage_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations\n- cmd/mcp/migrations_test.go: TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback,\n  TestBuildTaskRepo_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations\n\nmake check, make check-all, go test -tags=integration ./... (real\nPostgres), and helm lint all green.","tree":{"sha":"ca3ae3b74f09086fa5eb858a3fd4e2dcbe7a8825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/ca3ae3b74f09086fa5eb858a3fd4e2dcbe7a8825"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/1bcae2c251162eb9de7ac5ab915ded98ddf59cb4","verification":{"payload":"tree ca3ae3b74f09086fa5eb858a3fd4e2dcbe7a8825\nparent b3af40ae45317954b4acc3213d33046877197ebd\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790601715 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790601715 -0300\n\nfix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#124)\n\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver uses a session-scoped pg_advisory_lock\nto serialize concurrent migration runs. PgBouncer''s transaction-pooling\nmode (warehouse-infra PR #43) does not preserve session state across\nstatements, so any 2+ replicas of cmd/execution or cmd/mcp starting\nconcurrently (HPA scale-out per ADR-0030, or an ordinary multi-replica\nrolling deploy) crash-loop for 1-2 minutes with ''pq: unnamed prepared\nstatement does not exist'' before one wins the lock race.\n\ncmd/execution/main.go''s openStorage and cmd/mcp/main.go''s new\nbuildTaskRepo now read MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL for the migration step\nonly, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset so local dev and CI\nintegration tests keep working unchanged. The pgxpool built right after\nmigrations complete still uses DATABASE_URL/PgBouncer, unchanged.\n\ncharts/fulfillment-execution: new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey\nvalue renders MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL in the api and mcp Deployments\n(the two that run migrations), sourced from the same existingSecret,\nwith optional: true so a secret predating this key still starts the\npod. warehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions the secret key for all\n9 OLTP services, including this one -- no infra changes needed here.\n\nDirect port of order-management PR #115 / ADR-0029, this fleet''s Phase\n4 reference implementation. New ADR-0031 documents the rationale and\ncross-references order-management ADR-0029 and warehouse-infra PR\n#43/#44.\n\nTests added:\n- cmd/execution/migrations_test.go: TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback,\n  TestOpenStorage_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations\n- cmd/mcp/migrations_test.go: TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback,\n  TestBuildTaskRepo_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations\n\nmake check, make check-all, go test -tags=integration ./... (real\nPostgres), and helm lint all green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumnzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ7sQAK+FgdxDjbCM07V68vhiwb1S\nKg69erQDTBY5dqs7IdphF0HEKAQEzEDIVkt/bW2Ny7gXO+tdyfNuVubhryOeqDr/\n0K9BX1DQsfpzz1H9BEOR0jrGYN/QExKKttbetJ/F3jnUhnQx4ZaGB6MjWFPYAh1D\nEimzHuG7AD620lknby9fwCKOzv7BF8BPBkoY40qz6Vj/UGFLt2lFZVfKC5YzItAN\nvb+gZ3B6boV3H7Zui9Ci8hIVdCRO7f3csVap4uNoaplKS7oVTox3V4rrYozrSb8J\ntDayOVdqOCoHQnUxR8sTPJXNbOsF/EcRd2zNcTg9G5wzj8E0/v7UX6lfeUJfe88j\nBUub/LZIUgU5tkOIRgOkSCuz6helzmtY5sb6QMWfO0WfzqbQGVTx0OzhH0DOrrgj\nJz25k2ajYswPtWK65XyA7dLnPJXae4Znz/lVBvurl30xOLiiVVzGfZlfhgvHIfWZ\nrtYLiqwZ25avTIm/Ukr5Y1LOLGDIxxfEbjK6l9D+gHX69fXiypqyViVgLuIFvuUb\nroXqbv5iwkP2/StzkGwa7HTs90ytvyefe9CA6FCtxcF7O9zkVY669wD0+3OQooEU\nbdVGORRhFPX+TFQROfivzqsYyzzc1z2zORF1mp9Xjuam7w9Hq8EjNRS8AKWamn4g\nN3f1mmlsVw3b5v7RVQ03\n=V18i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T13:21:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/follo