tps://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/bd664a28661ac427f557c228b9b86c8134c098a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:42Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0030) (#121)\n\nPhase 3 scalability fan-out for fulfillment-execution, a direct port of\norder-management ADR-0026 (PR #110).\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed Deployment, every\nblock default-disabled via values.yaml so this PR changes nothing on\nmerge:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP; its WorkReleased consumer\n  uses a stable shared consumer group, verified safe at N>1.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 (not 4) / 70% CPU. Its Kafka consumer\n  group (fulfillment-analytics) is stable/shared and the analytics\n  publisher always sets a partition Key, verified in source, so N>1 is\n  safe; capped low since every write is already idempotent on event_id\n  but wide fan-out buys little for this workload.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Stateless read-only reader.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Static asset serving.\n- mcp: deliberately NO autoscaling block. Verified in\n  internal/adapters/inbound/mcp/server.go that the SDK''s\n  StreamableHTTPHandler keeps in-memory per-process session state keyed by\n  Mcp-Session-Id, with no session affinity on mcp-service.yaml -- unsafe\n  to scale without a real code change (out of scope here).\n\nEach Deployment template guards its static replicas: field with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so a hardcoded replica\ncount never fights an active HPA. Verified via helm template with every\ncombination (default off: 0 HPAs, every static replicas: present; all on:\n4 HPAs, only mcp keeps replicas:; api-only: only api HPA renders and only\napi''s replicas: is removed).\n\npgxpool tuning, matching order-management''s numbers exactly (same chart\nshape):\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool): MaxConns=10, statement_timeout=5s. Shared\n  by cmd/execution and cmd/mcp. Now flows through PgBouncer\n  (warehouse-infra PR #43, already live), so the 40-connection worst case\n  at api''s HPA ceiling is bounded by PgBouncer''s own pool_size=12, not a\n  direct multiplier against Postgres''s shared max_connections=100.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool): MaxConns=5,\n  statement_timeout=10s. Fixed at 1 replica, direct to Postgres per\n  PgBouncer PR #43''s documented analytics-DSN exception.\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool): MaxConns=5\n  (ReportsMaxConns), statement_timeout=15s (ReportsStatementTimeout).\n  HPA-scalable to 3, direct to Postgres.\n\nProven with a real Postgres via testcontainers\n(pool_limits_integration_test.go, -tags=integration): statement_timeout\ngenuinely cancels a pg_sleep past the configured timeout (SQLSTATE\n57014), and MaxConns genuinely blocks a further Acquire once the ceiling\nis held.\n\nADR-0030 documents the full decision, the connection-budget math, and the\nmcp exclusion; registered in docs/docs/adr/index.md.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean, make\ncheck, make arch-test, go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1\n(full suite green, real Postgres/Kafka testcontainers), make coverage\n(99.3%, gate 90%), helm lint, helm template (default off / all on /\napi-only, each independently confirmed).","tree":{"sha":"b0e2d4352826750b8882862afc5fd1c3b723242b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/b0e2d4352826750b8882862afc5fd1c3b723242b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/bd664a28661ac427f557c228b9b86c8134c098a8","verification":{"payload":"tree b0e2d4352826750b8882862afc5fd1c3b723242b\nparent 8b1b4a6118317491e837f4e012a5cfb641dc06a5\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790567982 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790567982 -0300\n\nfeat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0030) (#121)\n\nPhase 3 scalability fan-out for fulfillment-execution, a direct port of\norder-management ADR-0026 (PR #110).\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed Deployment, every\nblock default-disabled via values.yaml so this PR changes nothing on\nmerge:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP; its WorkReleased consumer\n  uses a stable shared consumer group, verified safe at N>1.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 (not 4) / 70% CPU. Its Kafka consumer\n  group (fulfillment-analytics) is stable/shared and the analytics\n  publisher always sets a partition Key, verified in source, so N>1 is\n  safe; capped low since every write is already idempotent on event_id\n  but wide fan-out buys little for this workload.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Stateless read-only reader.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Static asset serving.\n- mcp: deliberately NO autoscaling block. Verified in\n  internal/adapters/inbound/mcp/server.go that the SDK''s\n  StreamableHTTPHandler keeps in-memory per-process session state keyed by\n  Mcp-Session-Id, with no session affinity on mcp-service.yaml -- unsafe\n  to scale without a real code change (out of scope here).\n\nEach Deployment template guards its static replicas: field with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so a hardcoded replica\ncount never fights an active HPA. Verified via helm template with every\ncombination (default off: 0 HPAs, every static replicas: present; all on:\n4 HPAs, only mcp keeps replicas:; api-only: only api HPA renders and only\napi''s replicas: is removed).\n\npgxpool tuning, matching order-management''s numbers exactly (same chart\nshape):\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool): MaxConns=10, statement_timeout=5s. Shared\n  by cmd/execution and cmd/mcp. Now flows through PgBouncer\n  (warehouse-infra PR #43, already live), so the 40-connection worst case\n  at api''s HPA ceiling is bounded by PgBouncer''s own pool_size=12, not a\n  direct multiplier against Postgres''s shared max_connections=100.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool): MaxConns=5,\n  statement_timeout=10s. Fixed at 1 replica, direct to Postgres per\n  PgBouncer PR #43''s documented analytics-DSN exception.\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool): MaxConns=5\n  (ReportsMaxConns), statement_timeout=15s (ReportsStatementTimeout).\n  HPA-scalable to 3, direct to Postgres.\n\nProven with a real Postgres via testcontainers\n(pool_limits_integration_test.go, -tags=integration): statement_timeout\ngenuinely cancels a pg_sleep past the configured timeout (SQLSTATE\n57014), and MaxConns genuinely blocks a further Acquire once the ceiling\nis held.\n\nADR-0030 documents the full decision, the connection-budget math, and the\nmcp exclusion; registered in docs/docs/adr/index.md.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean, make\ncheck, make arch-test, go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1\n(full suite green, real Postgres/Kafka testcontainers), make coverage\n(99.3%, gate 90%), helm lint, helm template (default off / all on /\napi-only, each independently confirmed).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueYuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASlgQAArA0u3TwjV7mmWhjQsTuxdI\nyYrlgYbSrllbhwwXGf5dwrR5fg5Jhf0Mp2t6/y+yCbnTLJpeDFQwVZHsRYhmX7AH\nTR7LM3aUMuamVtkSJLD6eE5WSG4Yl56/G3/56VrlOpFln/sldMGMQHg29NCTvDY+\n8DoGXe5faLkk/8u2I6AawEFIGNF8tAPjGKmif7ZGrmjlnh56m9Xs55dxchcfzQn6\nQE6kL2CD52XunSNkx+xhMqdcmKKN1xRX4jYEDnYPy+Kl/mMvWsb9N72PrusYjMo8\n3WakBOsla3BApxxtPhOMvgXaOKCOPllz/OOd6ru/isGQV5jy9XwPEbU3Q+7yJfdu\nILAKNuBZtT159isYHjDQ7jzR1G/JaTsXZHbHjoGOre6kitOxnq50BRqnM36okzRg\nDVx9lIHzHeozIR/Qtoys0rXpihky+6EN3xFbrSSST7Q/cL+8vF88xppfKlHKopZo\nSH/oVoKcgtAQYFmJcYGEAZBDnjtLv3aqgKIz4sTAAhuDt/mVoANmqhH/1Zqp4owz\n1enoCXw2y73HuqIImu5Fy+OSp2vlc3wOO7vI+yTRrpx/YrmGSZhOwF954UDP4Wxa\nNiivqwZlplj4/fXpyeJmi+IQ5VH08BfK6gWFTvBYamtJuTVK+7Ul6MYe0IL+4/Eg\nJn+4V2loEGMV/n/ZelFs\n=B1nK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:59:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/bd664a28661ac427f557c228b9b86c8134c098a8","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjB-doAKGJkNjY0YTI4NjYxYWM0MjdmNTU3YzIyOGI5Yjg2YzgxMzRjMDk4YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/8b1b4a6118317491e837f4e012a5cfb641dc06a5","sha":"8b1b4a6118317491e837f4e012a5cfb641dc06a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/8b1b4a6118317491e837f4e012a5cfb641dc06a5"}],"sha":"bd664a28661ac427f557c228b9b86c8134c098a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/bd664a28661ac427f557c228b9b86c8134c098a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/8b1b4a6118317491e837f4e012a5cfb641dc06a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:42Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): switch outbound writers from LeastBytes to Hash balancer (#120)\n\nEvery outbound Kafka writer in this package (Publisher, AnalyticsPublisher,\nRelaySink) was built with Balancer: &kafkago.LeastBytes{}. LeastBytes picks\na partition purely by cumulative byte volume and never reads Message.Key,\nso the correct, non-nil, per-aggregate Key already set on every message\n(TaskId/PackageId) was silently a no-op for partition placement. Since\nwarehouse-infra PR #42 bumped every business topic from 1->8 partitions,\nthis meant per-aggregate event ordering was NOT actually guaranteed\ndespite the code looking correct.\n\nSwitches all three writers to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a over Message.Key),\nmatching order-management''s reference fix (PR #111, merged into develop)\nand the fleet-ops skill''s kafka-go-key-balancer-mismatch.md writeup.\n\nAdds partition_key_integration_test.go: three real-broker Testcontainers\ntests (Publisher, AnalyticsPublisher, RelaySink) against an 8-partition\ntopic proving same-key messages land on the same partition. Verified\nlocally that these tests FAIL under LeastBytes (same key scattered across\n2 partitions) and PASS under Hash -- a fake-Writer unit test alone would\nnot catch this class of bug, since the fake writer never simulates\npartition routing.","tree":{"sha":"e8ffd96cbe005b7b83bd1bc7784237a923cd65f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/e8ffd96cbe005b7b83bd1bc7784237a923cd65f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/8b1b4a6118317491e837f4e012a5cfb641dc06a5","verification":{"payload":"tree e8ffd96cbe005b7b83bd1bc7784237a923cd65f0\nparent 2b3340c9c7aeaa3434a0f02167966a37bb7dc9bc\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790566482 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790566482 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): switch outbound writers from LeastBytes to Hash balancer (#120)\n\nEvery outbound Kafka writer in this package (Publisher, AnalyticsPublisher,\nRelaySink) was built with Balancer: &kafkago.LeastBytes{}. LeastBytes picks\na partition purely by cumulative byte volume and never reads Message.Key,\nso the correct, non-nil, per-aggregate Key already set on every message\n(TaskId/PackageId) was silently a no-op for partition placement. Since\nwarehouse-infra PR #42 bumped every business topic from 1->8 partitions,\nthis meant per-aggregate event ordering was NOT actually guaranteed\ndespite the code looking correct.\n\nSwitches all three writers to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a over Message.Key),\nmatching order-management''s reference fix (PR #111, merged into develop)\nand the fleet-ops skill''s kafka-go-key-balancer-mismatch.md writeup.\n\nAdds partition_key_integration_test.go: three real-broker Testcontainers\ntests (Publisher, AnalyticsPublisher, RelaySink) against an 8-partition\ntopic proving same-key messages land on the same partition. Verified\nlocally that these tests FAIL under LeastBytes (same key scattered across\n2 partitions) and PASS under Hash -- a fake-Writer unit test alone would\nnot catch this class of bug, since the fake writer never simulates\npartition routing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueBSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEDsQAF6IMx1bsG0KQppaU9pMsSyC\ng/gdXCsXjX7vT0NffgNSYpv9OmcKn6RIdm2kT3s4Zgwgd0j7NikBbO0ApFRJ9kZi\nj1VkHcNR0Z8HmoTJW/WH7NoTnmmWjq/mWkne5gZilUbgy+q3yIHhX8S/B6gOQxOB\nIRspi5udzIGT6avlQEQwcy0y/3sNFWYMfhvhctd2BA9aZ8tpfHFoPCk0ozEULT93\n62Ed1dhP+psgTBa6+TwSDT7P8c7EwhbhBlmGjVAB83fu9tRYYJSb3jrX/ZasOaXP\nh20Uk/Si5MNvXXEeF1ykuZ+5GfzTKbB4MqlxNz4dVJlfzoc2f9LqqZ/nZNhaDEzr\nHwPGHJ1OtzY8rqmlHzFfDb3FnfWm71a6pPG4wAsLqAEeT9N8h4a3XO2CIB4TMJRq\nvCA9iJPJkf390l0KcLkLuuQ9q20QxM8Hi8Wf4DtND4ewLFrAt1pUJfVVN8S7BQZS\n+SZ2aTEtd4WZYklLa6w1CePwubblZMVXA8SlmG/IF+U31MmAL6/iEgOJTWWbvimj\nunRsb1Egde3lnrHO/vti1/PygMwDdHB6t/pOrbMjmIvd0Q0i5FQTLU6kcmSA0f0p\n03QI7Sj1PEET6RHLe2MlB9bjCI1Rl3KiGqLAVc7mdm8u8NwFGxklg1fKlBQ7A2VE\n4S6NIbcl6RC3w0X9tsjQ\n=fjdo\n-----END PG