thub.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/8b7113f9fb8e3b0a78f8e529b34765a78d5c208c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjB-doAKDhiNzExM2Y5ZmI4ZTNiMGE3OGY4ZTUyOWIzNDc2NWE3OGQ1YzIwOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/78bbbcb1c16ce52c90064ca90090483d4bae58e2","sha":"78bbbcb1c16ce52c90064ca90090483d4bae58e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/78bbbcb1c16ce52c90064ca90090483d4bae58e2"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/f602ec7f43e0d537b7775e16e5b9f8725741cc51","sha":"f602ec7f43e0d537b7775e16e5b9f8725741cc51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/f602ec7f43e0d537b7775e16e5b9f8725741cc51"}],"sha":"8b7113f9fb8e3b0a78f8e529b34765a78d5c208c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/8b7113f9fb8e3b0a78f8e529b34765a78d5c208c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/f602ec7f43e0d537b7775e16e5b9f8725741cc51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:51:32Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:51:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resilience): per-dependency circuit breakers, read-only retry, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (#117)\n\nPorts order-management''s resilience reference design (PR #107, ADR-0025)\nto fulfillment-execution.\n\n- Per-dependency sony/gobreaker circuit breakers for facilitylayout and\n  productclassification clients (never one global breaker), each falling\n  back to its existing fail-open PermissiveLookup behavior on OPEN.\n- cenkalti/backoff/v4 jittered retry (max 3) on both clients'' read-only\n  calls only.\n- internal/observability.CircuitBreakerMetrics gauge on the existing OTel\n  meter.\n- Kafka consumer: bounded in-process retry before the existing DLQ\n  publish; fixed a correctness issue where the idempotency claim was\n  inside the retry loop (see ADR-0029).\n- Graceful shutdown hardening: readiness-flip-first via new GET /readyz,\n  bounded drain, cmd/execution/main.go shutdown-order fix.\n- apis/openapi.yaml + regenerated docs/docs/api-reference for /readyz.\n- ADR-0029 documents the design; also fixes a pre-existing ADR-0028\n  sidebar omission found while updating the index.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration) clean, gofmt clean,\ngolangci-lint 0 issues, go test ./... -race green (all packages incl.\ninternal/architecture), go mod tidy -diff clean, coverage 99.3% (gate\n90%), docs typecheck/build clean.","tree":{"sha":"af4c6fd3feae4258228f273f7ae1a3eed392908a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/af4c6fd3feae4258228f273f7ae1a3eed392908a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/f602ec7f43e0d537b7775e16e5b9f8725741cc51","verification":{"payload":"tree af4c6fd3feae4258228f273f7ae1a3eed392908a\nparent 7d635c44c9cb9ff0427ca9a807e133934e11610e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790545892 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790545892 -0300\n\nfeat(resilience): per-dependency circuit breakers, read-only retry, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (#117)\n\nPorts order-management''s resilience reference design (PR #107, ADR-0025)\nto fulfillment-execution.\n\n- Per-dependency sony/gobreaker circuit breakers for facilitylayout and\n  productclassification clients (never one global breaker), each falling\n  back to its existing fail-open PermissiveLookup behavior on OPEN.\n- cenkalti/backoff/v4 jittered retry (max 3) on both clients'' read-only\n  calls only.\n- internal/observability.CircuitBreakerMetrics gauge on the existing OTel\n  meter.\n- Kafka consumer: bounded in-process retry before the existing DLQ\n  publish; fixed a correctness issue where the idempotency claim was\n  inside the retry loop (see ADR-0029).\n- Graceful shutdown hardening: readiness-flip-first via new GET /readyz,\n  bounded drain, cmd/execution/main.go shutdown-order fix.\n- apis/openapi.yaml + regenerated docs/docs/api-reference for /readyz.\n- ADR-0029 documents the design; also fixes a pre-existing ADR-0028\n  sidebar omission found while updating the index.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration) clean, gofmt clean,\ngolangci-lint 0 issues, go test ./... -race green (all packages incl.\ninternal/architecture), go mod tidy -diff clean, coverage 99.3% (gate\n90%), docs typecheck/build clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquY/lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHHIQAISEYWScyRU6fsGXzpK+FtHd\nWhcWxNqqALVKkgbKF9BCOjp5+8f+ZlYs1I4eyFA+zgjCuHBpkhDYnnTvPDRAffsf\nHHMuyt9QEPzVBybhEJm4TBC8G6ZSNDpfBqMlXRS61MEwBxjDNZ9xkpp32InH172G\ncvLiaW2+HaDOJaKv+cTNZe6oL9Z6UuJcu34RyKSQ6cqwVSyP+srSmI8tcFTiUjTW\nxSF5dnmdokHrzoZ6GXFf00MCe00DaQ6vApki4QQ3TEXPE6NqdMKcuX1fdN1sTO5K\nk/NFSEyzX7xaIkqg2xhi77ygyOK8mYIHb59rSNJxe4aicZ7HsGAS2DafV+vdve/C\naZMvqxPtFKdnrl8boEX9ejkVP65EZWtXJedUVWdcjIlBVOZ7zrhWc82+