://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/7d635c44c9cb9ff0427ca9a807e133934e11610e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:48:02Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:48:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kafka): EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE for the integration publisher (ADR-0027 Phase 4) (#116)\n\nAdds EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE (flat|cloudevents|dual, default flat) to the\nintegration Kafka publisher (internal/adapters/outbound/kafka), splitting\nEncode to build either envelope shape per ADR-0027 Phase 4:\n\n- flat (default, unset): today''s Envelope/TaskCPTMissedEnvelope/\n  PackageManifestedEnvelope shapes, byte-identical JSON output. A\n  golden-file test pins the exact pre-migration wire bytes for\n  TaskCompleted, TaskCPTMissed, and PackageManifested as the regression\n  gate.\n- cloudevents: one CloudEvents 1.0 structured-mode message per event,\n  using the reverse-DNS `type` convention and `/warehouse/...` `source`\n  already specified in apis/asyncapi.yaml (com.warehouse.wes.\n  fulfillment-execution.<entity>.<EventName>; entity is \"task\" for\n  TaskCompleted/TaskCPTMissed, \"package\" for PackageManifested). `id`\n  carries the same value as today''s event_id, `time` the same value as\n  today''s occurred_at, `subject` the raising aggregate''s instance id\n  (task id / package id, already available at each call site). `data` is\n  byte-identical to the flat envelope''s own Data payload.\n- dual: both shapes, two physical Kafka messages per domain event, same\n  topic, same key (== today''s event_id).\n\nNew small pure helper `cloudEventsType(entity, eventName string) string`\nbuilds the type string from the wes/fulfillment-execution constants\nalready used verbatim in apis/asyncapi.yaml.\n\ncmd/execution/main.go reads EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE via the existing\ngetenv/ParseEnvelopeMode pattern and logs \"event envelope mode\"\nmode=flat|cloudevents|dual once at publisher construction, mirroring this\nrepo''s existing MODE-flag logging convention (buildClassificationLookup /\nbuildLocationRoleLookup).\n\nTests (internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/envelope_mode_test.go), all run\nlocally:\n- flat mode: byte-identical golden JSON for TaskCompleted, TaskCPTMissed,\n  PackageManifested, plus the unset/zero-value Mode case.\n- ParseEnvelopeMode: case-insensitive parsing, unrecognized values default\n  to flat.\n- cloudevents mode: schema-field assertions (specversion, id==event_id,\n  the real reverse-DNS type string, source, subject, time==occurred_at,\n  datacontenttype, unchanged data) for all three event types.\n- dual mode: exactly 2 messages per domain event, shared key, message 0\n  structurally flat (no specversion key) and byte-identical to flat-only\n  output, message 1 structurally CloudEvents-shaped, for all three event\n  types.\n\nEvery pre-existing Encode/Publish test in this package (publisher_test.go,\nencoded_test.go) is unmodified and still passes — the zero-value Mode on\na bare Publisher{} literal behaves as flat.\n\nScope: only the integration publisher/topic (warehouse.fulfillment.events)\ntouched, per ADR-0027. The separate analytics publisher/topic\n(warehouse.fulfillment.analytics, internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/\nanalytics_publisher.go) is untouched — out of scope.\n\nLocal verification: `make check` (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test -race)\nand `make check-all` (+ coverage gate, arch-test, bdd) both green.\nCoverage: 99.3% (gate: 90%).\n\nZero production behavior change: EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE is not set anywhere\nin warehouse-infra Terraform/Helm values today, so every deployed instance\nof this service keeps running the same flat, byte-identical envelope it\nwrites today. This PR is a no-op merge; a later, separate infra phase sets\nthe var per ADR-0027''s phase sequence.\n\nCites: ADR-0027 (CloudEvents 1.0 envelope migration for the integration\ntopics), Phase 4 — Publishers grow EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE, default flat\n(non-breaking merge).","tree":{"sha":"b627f71f4dfa6b6d3f1209eaa65ee3c13f932d36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/b627f71f4dfa6b6d3f1209eaa65ee3c13f932d36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/7d635c44c9cb9ff0427ca9a807e133934e11610e","verification":{"payload":"tree b627f71f4dfa6b6d3f1209eaa65ee3c13f932d36\nparent 7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790520482 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790520482 -0300\n\nfeat(kafka): EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE for the integration publisher (ADR-0027 Phase 4) (#116)\n\nAdds EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE (flat|cloudevents|dual, default flat) to the\nintegration Kafka publisher (internal/adapters/outbound/kafka), splitting\nEncode to build either envelope shape per ADR-0027 Phase 4:\n\n- flat (default, unset): today''s Envelope/TaskCPTMissedEnvelope/\n  PackageManifestedEnvelope shapes, byte-identical JSON output. A\n  golden-file test pins the exact pre-migration wire bytes for\n  TaskCompleted, TaskCPTMissed, and PackageManifested as the regression\n  gate.\n- cloudevents: one CloudEvents 1.0 structured-mode message per event,\n  using the reverse-DNS `type` convention and `/warehouse/...` `source`\n  already specified in apis/asyncapi.yaml (com.warehouse.wes.\n  fulfillment-execution.<entity>.<EventName>; entity is \"task\" for\n  TaskCompleted/TaskCPTMissed, \"package\" for PackageManifested). `id`\n  carries the same value as today''s event_id, `time` the same value as\n  today''s occurred_at, `subject` the raising aggregate''s instance id\n  (task id / package id, already available at each call site). `data` is\n  byte-identical to the flat envelope''s own Data payload.\n- dual: both shapes, two physical Kafka messages per domain event, same\n  topic, same key (== today''s event_id).\n\nNew small pure helper `cloudEventsType(entity, eventName string) string`\nbuilds the type string from the wes/fulfillment-execution constants\nalready used verbatim in apis/asyncapi.yaml.\n\ncmd/execution/main.go reads EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE via the existing\ngetenv/ParseEnvelopeMode pattern and logs \"event envelope mode\"\nmode=flat|cloudevents|dual once at publisher construction, mirroring this\nrepo''s existing MODE-flag logging convention (buildClassificationLookup /\nbuildLocationRoleLookup).\n\nTests (internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/envelope_mode_test.go), all run\nlocally:\n- flat mode: byte-identical golden JSON for TaskCompleted, TaskCPTMissed,\n  PackageManifested, plus the unset/zero-value Mode case.\n- ParseEnvelopeMode: case-insensitive parsing, unrecognized values default\n  to flat.\n- cloudevents mode: schema-field assertions (specversion, id==event_id,\n  the real reverse-DNS type string, source, subject, time==occurred_at,\n  datacontenttype, unchanged data) for all three event types.\n- dual mode: exactly 2 messages per domain event, shared key, message 0\n  structurally flat (no specversion key) and byte-identical to flat-only\n  output, message 1 structurally CloudEvents-shaped, for all three event\n  types.\n\nEvery pre-existing Encode/Publish test in this package (publisher_test.go,\nencoded_test.go) is unmodified and still passes — the zero-value Mode on\na bare Publisher{} literal behaves as flat.\n\nScope: only the integration publisher/topic (warehouse.fulfillment.events)\ntouched, per ADR-0027. The separate analytics publisher/topic\n(warehouse.fulfillment.analytics, internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/\nanalytics_publisher.go) is untouched — out of scope.\n\nLocal verification: `make check` (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test -race)\nand `make check-all` (+ coverage gate, arch-test, bdd) both green.\nCoverage: 99.3% (gate: 90%).\n\nZero production behavior change: EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE is not set anywhere\nin warehouse-infra Terraform/Helm values today, so every deployed instance\nof this service keeps running the same flat, byte-identical envelope it\nwrites today. This PR is a no-op merge; a later, separate infra phase sets\nthe var per ADR-0027''s phase sequence.\n\nCites: ADR-0027 (CloudEvents 1.0 envelope migration for the integration\ntopics), Phase 4 — Publishers grow EVENT_ENVELOPE_MODE, default flat\n(non-breaking merge).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquSyiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGz4QAHy83/KDYcTFFVJQ7CsVYm8B\n32SUbD2eL75qvKMCLauxLfQ/utbs2zGBaEPpr4sYOJEviK4aaLb0+hPvge+sWowm\nvbvEg41n2MdLS9VO13Wo1TDehiJBD7urfrAKu8DTDcenJRTIT9O9Doq1MRmK/mxu\nyX4I94hZlUifk5rSHHnyOAc0uBMEJXf/3Q92dVOtcURKsTzbR+mkJU/H6M8Uh8sP\neriUTqbmM7yGNSFqDY23PdUTwkbvUlkx8yjyRgPJK1aAF/pru5rT6+V0JMvC0xp6\nmvusrkGpm9t72QHtaC5hmbIYpLuLdLLr8LQpmzfyZi7PSM28rJFJZjKayF9c+yWM\ne7FBfryI/RWgLmo5Q9GQnTjaEfBWrDCAWsQyqjgxz6j7b+LvmYOlXmGTgyI3d6zn\nrLmP8doY513EIfTiCBfK7IgnDjtN6wkz1PidGoEKgzLaPqQY+CmwvPdbBjHDfmp/\nfcPUZ1hb+rfRNC952Qyl8VBbO7sLAXg5taqeyLlFy07Qscs8bIB3TTDZ149WxSVv\nrfjKaXcVcvtI/Sow8DIv4C9b3ENnBCXAIEsVoe74LJBp9nESGJxi1Psg9VFW4JN9\nJnQ5jRBT8/PO+I9VManDCNoTxmuQe02PJcd7L9pc5SPig1HikwY5dN5v4zm6taNd\nxqSvETiWZVtjbc91ZuBs\n=FqWI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T14:48:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/7d635c44c9cb9ff0427ca9a807e133934e11610e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjB-doAKDdkNjM1YzQ0YzljYjlmZjA0MjdjYTlhODA3ZTEzMzkzNGUxMTYxMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b","sha":"7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b"}],"sha":"7d635c44c9cb9ff0427ca9a807e133934e11610e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/7d635c44c9cb9ff0427ca9a807e133934e11610e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:19:58Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:19:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(http): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /tasks (#115)\n\nPorts order-management''s ADR-0023 reference design (PR #105) to\nfulfillment-execution''s one true resource-creation POST endpoint,\nPOST /tasks (server-generated TaskId). POST /stations is deliberately\nleft unprotected — RegisterStation already treats a caller-supplied\nstationId as idempotent by construction (re-registration overwrites\nthe capability set rather than erroring), so it needs no middleware.\n\n- internal/pgtx: new tiny package extracted from unit_of_work.go''s\n  previously-unexported txKey/withTx/txFrom, so the inbound HTTP\n  middleware and the outbound postgres.UnitOfWork can bind/read the\n  same transaction-in-context without crossing the inbound/outbound\n  architecture boundary. unit_of_work.go now delegates to it; zero\n  behavior change for any existing caller.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go: RequireIdempotencyKey,\n  route-scoped via chi''s r.With(...) onto POST /tasks only (never\n  r.Use on the whole router). Missing header -> 400. Fresh key begins\n  a pgx transaction, INSERTs a bare idempotency_keys row, runs the\n  wrapped handler against a recorder inside that same transaction\n  (joined by CreateTask''s existing atomically()/UnitOfWork.Execute via\n  pgtx), then UPDATEs the outcome and commits before writing to the\n  real ResponseWriter. Same key + matching body replays the cached\n  response verbatim, including a cached business-validation error.\n  Same key + different body -> 422. A panic rolls back and re-panics\n  without caching anything.\n- migrations/0012_idempotency_keys.{up,down}.sql: same table shape as\n  order-management''s (key PK, method, path, request_hash,\n  status_code, response_body, response_headers, created_at,\n  completed_at, plus the created_at index for a future TTL job).\n- router.go: new WithIdempotencyPool RouterOption; a nil pool (the\n  in-memory dev/test composition root) leaves POST /tasks\n  unprotected, mirroring this repo''s existing nil-pool convention for\n  other optional Postgres-backed capabilities. cmd/execution/main.go\n  wires the real pool in.\n- idempotency_integration_test.go: the same six scenarios as the\n  reference, against a real testcontainers Postgres through the real\n  chi router (fresh key creates the task; replay returns an identical\n  response with exactly one task row; mismatched body -> 422; missing\n  header -> 400; five concurrent goroutines with the same key create\n  exactly one task; a cached business-validation error is replayed\n  verbatim on retry).\n- docs/docs/adr/0028-idempotency-key-middleware.md: this repo''s ADR,\n  including the confirmed survey of every mutating POST route and why\n  only /tasks needed this.\n\nCreateTask.Execute already wrapped Tasks.Save + Publisher.Publish in\natomically()/UnitOfWork.Execute from the earlier transactional-outbox\nrollout, so no use-case change was needed for the join to work.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain and -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\nmake check, make arch-test, make coverage (99.3%, gate 90%), and\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 all green, including\nthe six new integration scenarios against real testcontainers\nPostgres.","tree":{"sha":"b9864f95b7fc00cc4cbb242ba0b54c00e5fa89c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/b9864f95b7fc00cc4cbb242ba0b54c00e5fa89c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b","verification":{"payload":"tree b9864f95b7fc00cc4cbb242ba0b54c00e5fa89c8\nparent c1bf77b958b01ac244f74fcfd967b91ec98e61bf\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790515198 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790515198 -0300\n\nfeat(http): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /tasks (#115)\n\nPorts order-management''s ADR-0023 reference design (PR #105) to\nfulfillment-execution''s one true resource-creation POST endpoint,\nPOST /tasks (server-generated TaskId). POST /stations is deliberately\nleft unprotected — RegisterStation already treats a caller-supplied\nstationId as idempotent by construction (re-registration overwrites\nthe capability set rather than erroring), so it needs no middleware.\n\n- internal/pgtx: new tiny package extracted from unit_of_work.go''s\n  previously-unexported txKey/withTx/txFrom, so the inbound HTTP\n  middleware and the outbound postgres.UnitOfWork can bind/read the\n  same transaction-in-context without crossing the inbound/outbound\n  architecture boundary. unit_of_work.go now delegates to it; zero\n  behavior change for any existing caller.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go: RequireIdempotencyKey,\n  route-scoped via chi''s r.With(...) onto POST /tasks only (never\n  r.Use on the whole router). Missing header -> 400. Fresh key begins\n  a pgx transaction, INSERTs a bare idempotency_keys row, runs the\n  wrapped handler against a recorder inside that same transaction\n  (joined by CreateTask''s existing atomically()/UnitOfWork.Execute via\n  pgtx), then UPDATEs the outcome and commits before writing to the\n  real ResponseWriter. Same key + matching body replays the cached\n  response verbatim, including a cached business-validation error.\n  Same key + different body -> 422. A panic rolls back and re-panics\n  without caching anything.\n- migrations/0012_idempotency_keys.{up,down}.sql: same table shape as\n  order-management''s (key PK, method, path, request_hash,\n  status_code, response_body, response_headers, created_at,\n  completed_at, plus the created_at index for a future TTL job).\n- router.go: new WithIdempotencyPool RouterOption; a nil pool (the\n  in-memory dev/test composition root) leaves POST /tasks\n  unprotected, mirroring this repo''s existing nil-pool convention for\n  other optional Postgres-backed capabilities. cmd/execution/main.go\n  wires the real pool in.\n- idempotency_integration_test.go: the same six scenarios as the\n  reference, against a real testcontainers Postgres through the real\n  chi router (fresh key creates the task; replay returns an identical\n  response with exactly one task row; mismatched body -> 422; missing\n  header -> 400; five concurrent goroutines with the same key create\n  exactly one task; a cached business-validation error is replayed\n  verbatim on retry).\n- docs/docs/adr/0028-idempotency-key-middleware.md: this repo''s ADR,\n  including the confirmed survey of every mutating POST route and why\n  only /tasks needed this.\n\nCreateTask.Execute already wrapped Tasks.Save + Publisher.Publish in\natomically()/UnitOfWork.Execute from the earlier transactional-outbox\nrollout, so no use-case change was needed for the join to work.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain and -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\nmake check, make arch-test, make coverage (99.3%, gate 90%), and\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 all green, including\nthe six new integration scenarios against real testcontainers\nPostgres.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRf+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkt0QACr5HK542RWa50it47BBNu3u\n/lrHAo5qSiJTEbxgxfUk3q75B8Xyzgqpr1eiCSYycxP4jJEHErvoo6Od1bFykVJT\njJoZpzIXZob0t+7FuvU2LDxPoPLkjtHcMQuLgB8p0hz5fdxWol7e+SYm7dc5c3qv\nJR20CCvcqaibXJAzyOG9y0ndO0tfEJnOVGG1UcbRI8Yv11f7U66e4qpRRSYLUZYJ\nfnTkCse8Syy39GuPTHl+GOD8E2/1tbP15q9tR/47fAmbTWVIEsh4U4QIG6J1VH87\nZM3RHBamQBA4w0qHjxz2UdtFf4wKzE2o0hVF5T7ZkMQeNu8Lqt6gYdhmAfaH40yP\ncbt8HPBcJxfksfXVEoTe8XI+rlzOGeAfZbE7XASvhxis4v27LqOgSgI07htOwjyh\nj+1VCK5GFipfepVcXbIEUW8OARQ/hDoA4EuSxxoXRxMmid9wiNrOGFhtZylq31Ba\nmk9Rqt/SnkUPPijriRbYJMAudm3e7VMSyUlNoGOoBMnHqbFKMdbLJXQBCvsmbtXF\nUGe8XIjdLCu2i9prfRBgy/xKZdhzpq0qsemYM3AoR4LIUNSuKVLBAj+HEKB7EZ7R\nSgr1H3IlxBwfV7bExLLXeVgW6Rma61q0Yclp22oRl7iIvjQCviW2fUaNdDbovAzG\nT+YfHp8VqkQa16fdjzHc\n=N0LN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T13:19:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjB-doAKDdjZTFlNmY3NzMzODNhNmNmNTFiMGY2ZTNjMWYzN2YyZWM5NzQxMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commit/c1bf77b958b01ac244f74fcfd967b91ec98e61bf","sha":"c1bf77b958b01ac244f74fcfd967b91ec98e61bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/c1bf77b958b01ac244f74fcfd967b91ec98e61bf"}],"sha":"7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/7ce1e6f773383a6cf51b0f6e3c1f37f2ec97412b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/commits/c1bf77b958b01ac244f74fcfd967b91ec98e61bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:09:57Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:09:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kafka): dual-read WorkReleased envelope (ADR-0027 Phase 2 Task 2a) (#114)\n\nUpgrade this repo''s inbound consumer of wes-work-planning''s WorkReleased\nevent (internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go, off\nwarehouse.work-planning.events) to accept EITHER the existing flat\nplatform envelope or the new CloudEvents 1.0 structured envelope on the\nSAME topic, discriminated by the presence of a specversion field.\n\n- Add decodeEnvelope: probes for specversion, then decodes the flat or\n  CloudEvents shape and normalizes both to the existing Envelope struct\n  (event_id/event_type/occurred_at/source/data) HandleMessage already\n  consumes. WorkReleasedData is unchanged.\n- CloudEvents id -> event_id, time -> occurred_at, source -> source\n  (cosmetic), data -> data unchanged. type is stripped back from the\n  reverse-DNS form (com.warehouse.wes.work-planning.workunit.WorkReleased)\n  to the bare \"WorkReleased\" the existing switch/case dispatch already\n  keys on, via bareEventType.\n- An unrecognized specversion value fails soft: HandleMessage returns an\n  error, mirroring this consumer''s existing malformed-message posture\n  (Run logs it and routes it to the configured dead-letter sink; no\n  panic, no silent Task creation).\n- No env var, no behavior change for existing flat traffic — purely\n  additive read-side capability, per the ADR''s phase-ordering rationale\n  (publishers do not start dual-writing until every consumer here is\n  proven dual-read first).\n\nTests (all real, run locally):\n- Flat-envelope regression test (unchanged behavior).\n- CloudEvents-envelope test using the ADR''s exact schema, asserting the\n  same normalized result (task type, OrderRef) as the flat path.\n- Explicit flat-vs-CloudEvents same-result comparison test.\n- Malformed/unsupported specversion fails soft without creating a Task.\n- New testcontainers Kafka integration test\n  (dualread_integration_test.go): publishes one flat-shaped and one\n  CloudEvents-shaped message sharing the same event_id/id onto a real\n  broker, asserts CreateTask fires exactly once — the idempotency-safety\n  property ADR-0027 calls out as load-bearing for the later dual-write\n  phase.\n\nVerified locally: make check, make check-all (fmt, vet, build, lint,\ntest, 90% coverage gate, arch-test, bdd) and\n`go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1` (the same command CI''s\nintegration job runs) all green, including the new testcontainers test\nagainst a real Kafka broker.\n\nPer ADR-0027 Phase 2 Task 2a\n(docs/docs/adr/0027-cloudevents-envelope-migration.md).","tree":{"sha":"a9c71518f8cdf912c19ef97a279598d53f8b1203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/trees/a9c71518f8cdf912c19ef97a279598d53f8b1203"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/fulfillment-execution/git/commits/c1bf77b958b01ac244f74fcfd967b91ec98e61bf","verification":{"payload":"tree a9c71518f8cdf912c19ef97a279598d53f8b1203\nparent 73962da3b705792ad0da888dbbe1b0fbc40d370b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790514597 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790514597 -0300\n\nfeat(kafka): dual-read WorkReleased envelope (ADR-0027 Phase 2 Task 2a) (#114)\n\nUpgrade this repo''s inbound consumer of wes-work-planning''s WorkReleased\nevent (internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/consumer.go, off\nwarehouse.work-planning.events) to accept EITHER the existing flat\nplatform envelope or the new CloudEvents 1.0 structured envelope on the\nSAME topic, discriminated by the presence of a specversion field.\n\n- Add decodeEnvelope: probes for specversion, then decodes the flat or\n  CloudEvents shape and normalizes both to the existing Envelope struct\n  (event_id/event_type/occurred_at/source/data) HandleMessage already\n  consumes. WorkReleasedData is unchanged.\n- CloudEvents id -> event_id, time -> occurred_at, source -> source\n  (cosmetic), data -> data unchanged. type is stripped back from the\n  reverse-DNS form (com.warehouse.wes.work-planning.workunit.WorkReleased)\n  to the bare \"WorkReleased\" the existing switch/case dispatch already\n  keys on, via bareEventType.\n- An unrecognized specversion value fails soft: HandleMessage returns an\n  error, mirroring this consumer''s existing malformed-message posture\n  (Run logs it and routes it to the configured dead-letter sink; no\n  panic, no silent Task creation).\n- No env var, no behavior change for existing flat traffic — purely\n  additive read-side capability, per the ADR''s phase-ordering rationale\n  (publishers do not start dual-writing until every consumer here is\n  proven dual-read first).\n\nTests (all real, run locally):\n- Flat-envelope regression test (unchanged behavior).\n- CloudEvents-envelope test using the ADR''s exact schema, asserting the\n  same normalized result (task type, OrderRef) as the flat path.\n- Explicit flat-vs-CloudEvents same-result comparison test.\n- Malformed/unsupported specversion fails soft without creating a Task.\n- New testcontainers Kafka integration test\n  (dualread_integration_test.go): publishes one flat-shaped and one\n  CloudEvents-shaped message sharing the same event_id/id onto a real\n  broker, asserts CreateTask fires exactly once — the idempotency-safety\n  property ADR-0027 calls out as load-bearing for the later dual-write\n  phase.\n\nVerified locally: make check, make check-all (fmt, vet, build, lint,\ntest, 90% coverage gate, arch-test, bdd) and\n`go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1` (the same command CI''s\nintegration job runs) all green, including the new testcontainers test\nagainst a real Kafka broker.\n\nPer ADR-0027 Phase 2 Task 2a\n(docs/docs/adr/0027-cloudevents-envelope-migration.md).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRWlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApFUQAE7KK2qVNS631giaCBYixRzB\nit2skNMb6FzUGgH96O4hJBLtsqpLXtZchhJnu2MDmBpODBQ/D1zXJUsBYRkFlrbR\nY3st/5AzcYt3YYA53er48EPjPDqCbie6zz0Hezm9Qq6X3zXdGRII44Y2nyrMNt9p\n6Fl3Bjstl13nIfQFx6vP08