":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/7ac4d786f9e0c17846c4343343dde3fefd150267"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/12c22202221f084bb0eb5c544cb98bee3ad83ff2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:59:55Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:59:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: siteCode is the canonical name for the shift-plan key; buildingId deprecated (decision 19) (#147)\n\n* feat(siteCode): REST and MCP accept siteCode as the canonical ShiftPlan key; buildingId is a deprecated alias\n\nDecision 19 (additive step). ProposePathPlan and CommitShiftPlan accept\nsiteCode OR buildingId (same value, same building_id column); both present and\ndifferent is 422 conflicting-site-and-building; neither is 400\nmissing-building-id (slug kept). ShiftPlan responses carry siteCode and\nbuildingId (same value). GET /sites/{siteCode}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap is\nthe canonical route; the buildings route keeps working and answers\nDeprecation: true. The by-path staffing gap takes siteCode as plan key and\nscope; buildingId-only calls stay unscoped. MCP tools take siteCode with\nbuildingId as a deprecated alias; staffing resource gains the\nstaffing://sites/... template.\n\nThe 422 for a differing pair is NOT applied to staffing-gap reads: ADR 0034''s\nown tests and docs use bldg-1 + WH1 as the supported pair (see ADR 0035).\n\n* feat(events): ShiftPlanProposed and ShiftPlanCommitted carry site_code (same value as building_id)\n\nAdditive on v1, no .v2: the integration ShiftPlanCommitted line message and the\nanalytics ShiftPlanProposed / ShiftPlanCommitted payloads gain site_code, the\ncanonical name of the plan key, with the same value as the (now deprecated,\nnot removed) building_id. Kafka key and CloudEvents subject are unchanged. The\nAsyncAPI declares site_code as not-required (pre-existing outbox rows lack it)\nand building_id as deprecated; validated with the asyncapi CLI (0 errors).\nGoldens change only by adding the field.\n\n* test(siteCode): Postgres round trip proves buildingId and siteCode are one stored key\n\nTestcontainers Postgres through the real router: a plan committed via the\ndeprecated buildingId is readable via siteCode (canonical /sites route and the\nlegacy /buildings route) and the reverse; both live in shift_plan.building_id\n(no migration); the outbox ShiftPlanCommitted message carries site_code and\nbuilding_id with one value and the unchanged <site>/<shift> key and subject; a\nconflicting pair is a 422 that writes nothing.\n\n* docs: siteCode convergence (ADR 0035): ADR, docs pack, regenerated API reference\n\n- ADR 0035: siteCode is canonical, buildingId a deprecated alias; the differing pair stays valid on staffing-gap reads during the deprecation window\n- docs pack, README, INTEGRATION and the MCP governance charter use Site as the term\n- API reference regenerated, including the new /sites/{siteCode}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap route\n\n* test: split three siteCode tests under the complexity gates\n\nCI lint and complexity flagged TestStaffingGapForShift_CanonicalSitesRouteAndDeprecatedBuildingsRoute (cyclomatic 16 > 15), TestTools_DescribeBuildingIdAsDeprecatedInFavourOfSiteCode (cognitive 21 > 20) and TestAsyncAPI_PlanEventsDeclareSiteCodeAndDeprecateBuildingId (cognitive 26 > 20). Extract named helpers; every assertion is preserved. Reproduced locally with golangci-lint (3 issues before, 0 after).","tree":{"sha":"78669859103717446f0f635148880b37c04ea858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/78669859103717446f0f635148880b37c04ea858"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/12c22202221f084bb0eb5c544cb98bee3ad83ff2","verification":{"payload":"tree 78669859103717446f0f635148880b37c04ea858\nparent d39f8932f0d85232f70f2dc951dd8af4a43d60a3\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791449995 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791449995 -0300\n\nfeat: siteCode is the canonical name for the shift-plan key; buildingId deprecated (decision 19) (#147)\n\n* feat(siteCode): REST and MCP accept siteCode as the canonical ShiftPlan key; buildingId is a deprecated alias\n\nDecision 19 (additive step). ProposePathPlan and CommitShiftPlan accept\nsiteCode OR buildingId (same value, same building_id column); both present and\ndifferent is 422 conflicting-site-and-building; neither is 400\nmissing-building-id (slug kept). ShiftPlan responses carry siteCode and\nbuildingId (same value). GET /sites/{siteCode}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap is\nthe canonical route; the buildings route keeps working and answers\nDeprecation: true. The by-path staffing gap takes siteCode as plan key and\nscope; buildingId-only calls stay unscoped. MCP tools take siteCode with\nbuildingId as a deprecated alias; staffing resource gains the\nstaffing://sites/... template.\n\nThe 422 for a differing pair is NOT applied to staffing-gap reads: ADR 0034''s\nown tests and docs use bldg-1 + WH1 as the supported pair (see ADR 0035).\n\n* feat(events): ShiftPlanProposed and ShiftPlanCommitted carry site_code (same value as building_id)\n\nAdditive on v1, no .v2: the integration ShiftPlanCommitted line message and the\nanalytics ShiftPlanProposed / ShiftPlanCommitted payloads gain site_code, the\ncanonical name of the plan key, with the same value as the (now deprecated,\nnot removed) building_id. Kafka key and CloudEvents subject are unchanged. The\nAsyncAPI declares site_code as not-required (pre-existing outbox rows lack it)\nand building_id as deprecated; validated with the asyncapi CLI (0 errors).\nGoldens change only by adding the field.\n\n* test(siteCode): Postgres round trip proves buildingId and siteCode are one stored key\n\nTestcontainers Postgres through the real router: a plan committed via the\ndeprecated buildingId is readable via siteCode (canonical /sites route and the\nlegacy /buildings route) and the reverse; both live in shift_plan.building_id\n(no migration); the outbox ShiftPlanCommitted message carries site_code and\nbuilding_id with one value and the unchanged <site>/<shift> key and subject; a\nconflicting pair is a 422 that writes nothing.\n\n* docs: siteCode convergence (ADR 0035): ADR, docs pack, regenerated API reference\n\n- ADR 0035: siteCode is canonical, buildingId a deprecated alias; the differing pair stays valid on staffing-gap reads during the deprecation window\n- docs pack, README, INTEGRATION and the MCP governance charter use Site as the term\n- API reference regenerated, including the new /sites/{siteCode}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap route\n\n* test: split three siteCode tests under the complexity gates\n\nCI lint and complexity flagged TestStaffingGapForShift_CanonicalSitesRouteAndDeprecatedBuildingsRoute (cyclomatic 16 > 15), TestTools_DescribeBuildingIdAsDeprecatedInFavourOfSiteCode