claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/12de6871a790aab3d0e4aedb7bfb5ce22ab8a10a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:38:16Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:38:16Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"docs(executive): add executive briefing deck\n\nAdds `executive/index.html`: a self-contained reveal.js executive deck covering strategy, architecture, observability, competitive position and next steps for this repo. Open it in a browser (loads reveal.js 6.0.0 from jsDelivr, pinned with an SRI hash; no vendored library code in this repo); no build step. Full source text is in the speaker notes (press S).\n\nNo code, config, workflow or chart changes; the folder is outside `.github/`, `charts/` and the docs site, so `repo_lint` and the docs build are unaffected. Fleet-wide gap analysis lives in `warehouse-docs/executive/competitive-gaps.html`.","tree":{"sha":"a91d3b7f1163259d1e2051291ddb8e4fc4e92fe6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/a91d3b7f1163259d1e2051291ddb8e4fc4e92fe6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/12de6871a790aab3d0e4aedb7bfb5ce22ab8a10a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/12de6871a790aab3d0e4aedb7bfb5ce22ab8a10a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjCLdoAKDEyZGU2ODcxYTc5MGFhYjNkMGU0YWVkYjdiZmI1Y2UyMmFiOGExMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/26b124c351b47bb5a7afa1c1ce063967d9dc0f00","sha":"26b124c351b47bb5a7afa1c1ce063967d9dc0f00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/26b124c351b47bb5a7afa1c1ce063967d9dc0f00"}],"sha":"12de6871a790aab3d0e4aedb7bfb5ce22ab8a10a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/12de6871a790aab3d0e4aedb7bfb5ce22ab8a10a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/26b124c351b47bb5a7afa1c1ce063967d9dc0f00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:09:46Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:09:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: site-scoped staffing gap, verified unit of charge (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#141)\n\n* feat: site-scope the staffing gap with an optional canonical siteCode\n\nStartAssociateShift accepts an optional siteCode (the facility-layout Site\ncode) persisted on associate_shift.site_code (nullable, additive migration\n000005). The single and list staffing-gap queries (REST and the MCP\nget_staffing_gap tool) accept an optional siteCode filter that counts only\nassignments whose associate has a not-ended shift at that site. Without it\nnothing changes (fleet-wide count). Legacy NULL-site rows count only in\nunscoped queries. PathUnderstaffed gains an optional site_code on the\nanalytics payload, omitted when unscoped (additive, still v1).\n\nNo live lookup/validation against facility-layout: the code is accepted as\ngiven.\n\nTests: unit (scoped vs unscoped, legacy NULL, blank), HTTP, MCP, BDD,\nanalytics golden + projector tolerance, testcontainers Postgres (two sites,\nsame path; legacy NULL; ended shift; restart moves site).\n\n* docs: ADR 0034 + OpenAPI/AsyncAPI for the site-scoped staffing gap\n\nNew ADR 0034 (accepted) records the scoping rule. apis/openapi.yaml gains the\noptional siteCode on StartShiftRequest, the staffing-gap query parameter and\nthe response echo; apis/asyncapi.yaml gains the optional site_code on the\nPathUnderstaffed analytics payload (absence = unscoped). The generated REST\nAPI reference is regenerated exactly like ci.yml''s docs-api-drift job.\n\n* docs: resolve the staffing-gap hotspot and record the other decided items\n\nDDD pack (docs/docs/ddd/*): ER diagram (associate_shift.site_code, migration\n000005), class diagrams (SiteCode, NewAssociateShiftAtSite,\nCountActiveByPathAtSite, PathUnderstaffed.siteCode), sequence diagrams\n(StartAssociateShift, GetStaffingGap scoped/unscoped), domain events (additive\nsite_code, absence = unscoped), aggregate design canvas, aggregates, message\nflow, bounded-context canvas. The \"counts across buildings\" hotspot is now\n\"Decided 2026-10-06 ... (ADR 0034)\".\n\nUnit of charge (decision 7): \"Verified 2026-10-06\" note in the\nubiquitous-language and bounded-context-canvas pages (1 work unit = 1 task = 1\nunit of charge; 3600 / MeanActualSeconds is correct). ADR 0033 untouched.\n\ndomain_event table (decision 8): documented as legacy, unused; retained\n(additive migrations only).\n\nAlso README curl examples, integration.md and the MCP governance charter.\n\n* fix: declare siteCode nullable in the OpenAPI StartShiftRequest\n\nThe CI `contract` job (Schemathesis, negative-data phase) sent\n{\"siteCode\": null} and the API accepted it (201) while the spec declared\nsiteCode as a non-nullable string. The behaviour is intended and matches\n`certifications` (null == omitted, site stays unknown), so the spec now says\nso (nullable: true) instead of the handler rejecting null. Adds an HTTP test\npinning null == omitted and regenerates the REST API reference.\n\nVerified locally: `make contract` (Schemathesis 4.28.0, all four phases pass).","tree":{"sha":"941d86c2d622676e19c55f53ea1ad751f56a7d93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/941d86c2d622676e19c55f53ea1ad751f56a7d93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/26b124c351b47bb5a7afa1c1ce063967d9dc0f00","verification":{"payload":"tree 941d86c2d622676e19c55f53ea1ad751f56a7d93\nparent 0df3efa830bdb28035e881684a4d4e882859cdc6\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791328186 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791328186 -0300\n\nfeat: site-scoped staffing gap, verified unit of charge (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#141)\n\n* feat: site-scope the staffing gap with an optional canonical siteCode\n\nStartAssociateShift accepts an optional siteCode (the facility-layout Site\ncode) persisted on associate_shift.site_code (nullable, additive migration\n000005). The single and list staffing-gap queries (REST and the MCP\nget_staffing_gap tool) accept an optional siteCode filter that counts only\nassignments whose associate has a not-ended shift at that site. Without it\nnothing changes (fleet-wide count). Legacy NULL-site rows count only in\nunscoped queries. PathUnderstaffed gains an optional site_code on the\nanalytics payload, omitted when unscoped (additive, still v1).\n\nNo live lookup/validation against facility-layout: the code is accepted as\ngiven.\n\nTests: unit (scoped vs unscoped, legacy NULL, blank), HTTP, MCP, BDD,\nanalytics golden + projector tolerance, testcontainers Postgres (two sites,\nsame path; legacy NULL; ended shift; restart moves site).\n\n* docs: ADR 0034 + OpenAPI/AsyncAPI for the site-scoped staffing gap\n\nNew ADR 0034 (accepted) records the scoping rule. apis/openapi.yaml gains the\noptional siteCode on StartShiftRequest, the staffing-gap query parameter and\nthe response echo; apis/asyncapi.yaml gains the optional site_code on the\nPathUnderstaffed analytics payload (absence = unscoped). The generated REST\nAPI reference is regenerated exactly like ci.yml''s docs-api-drift job.\n\n* docs: resolve the staffing-gap hotspot and record the other decided items\n\nDDD pack (docs/docs/ddd/*): ER diagram (associate_shift.site_code, migration\n000005), class diagrams (SiteCode, NewAssociateShiftAtSite,\nCountActiveByPathAtSite, PathUnderstaffed.siteCode), sequence diagrams\n(StartAssociateShift, GetStaffingGap scoped/unscoped), domain events (additive\nsite_code, absence = unscoped), aggregate design canvas, aggregates, message\nflow, bounded-context canvas. The \"counts across buildings\" hotspot is now\n\"Decided 2026-10-06 ... (ADR 0034)\".\n\nUnit of charge (decision 7): \"Verified 2026-10-06\" note in the\nubiquitous-language and bounded-context-canvas pages (1 work unit = 1 task = 1\nunit of charge; 3600 / MeanActualSeconds is correct). ADR 0033 untouched.\n\ndomain_event table (decision 8): documented as legacy, unused; retained\n(additive migrations only).\n\nAlso README curl examples, integration.md and the MCP governance charter.\n\n* fix: declare siteCode nullable in the OpenAPI StartShiftRequest\n\nThe CI `contract` job (Schemathesis, negative-data phase) sent\n{\"siteCode\": null} and the API accepted it (201) while the spec declared\nsiteCode as a non-nullable string. The behaviour is intended and matches\n`certifications` (null == omitted, site stays unknown), so the spec now says\nso (nullable: true) instead of the handler rejecting null. Adds an HTTP test\npinning null == omitted and regenerates the REST API reference.\n\nVerified locally: `make contract` (Schemathesis 4.28.0, all four phases pass).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxX+6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfCYQAElS3zKzjegEznaimmBVFS3S\n4xDmFIpP3ygQtTfiTJmFqwj2j1+55ROTgqdQXZ5jjd9mRAb1vaNJoapTXYzsXliq\n9p/qdOFM5DblP2tLrOup94XdtAHrDemfup7VciD9/p6tfcNlUXGyL3qahIehEJOI\n+ellQbdwdbOW67fj+irXcf0sZtFultDIHqQ+zj1DO63Pp0koJimZ34G3xi7EyQEy\nev+odHQ4/vY2HOw87ZglDO54idVTTAZTAW0Ny2feuM94rZo