"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/26b124c351b47bb5a7afa1c1ce063967d9dc0f00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/0df3efa830bdb28035e881684a4d4e882859cdc6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:59:48Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:59:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#139)\n\n* fix(http): roll back domain writes of a non-2xx idempotent request\n\nRequireIdempotencyKey committed the shared transaction for any non-panic\nresponse. A late failure (409 concurrent-modification on the assignment\nSave after the associate hours Save of the same request) therefore\npersisted the earlier write. The wrapped handler now runs in a savepoint:\n2xx releases it, any other status rolls back to it, while the idempotency\nrow (inserted before the savepoint) still stores the failed response, so\nreplay semantics are unchanged.\n\nIntegration test (testcontainers) forces a real optimistic-concurrency\nconflict and asserts associate_shift, outbox and the stored 409 replay.\n\n* fix(usecases): convert measured seconds-per-task to a per-head hourly rate\n\nProposePathPlan divided the charge by labor-performance''s\nmeanActualSeconds (a duration per task) where a per-head hourly rate\n(units per head per hour, like plannedRate) is expected: a 36 s task\nproposed 100 heads for 3600 units instead of 36. The measured rate is now\n3600 / meanActualSeconds; a non-positive or non-finite duration is treated\nas ErrMeasuredRateUnavailable (fail-open, 0 heads).\n\nTests pin the conversion at several magnitudes and the degenerate inputs.\n\n* fix(api): declare /readyz, add observedIdleShare, record ADR-0033\n\n- apis/openapi.yaml: GET /readyz (200 ready / 503 not_ready) was served but\n  undeclared; a router-vs-spec drift test now guards every route.\n- staffing-gap responses gain observedIdleShare (a 0..1 fraction, the name\n  matches the value); observedIdlePct is kept with the unchanged value and\n  marked deprecated, so no consumer breaks (additive).\n- resolvedRate / plannedRate descriptions state the per-head hourly unit.\n- ADR-0033 records the idempotent-request atomicity fix, the measured-rate\n  unit conversion, the idle-share naming and /readyz; ADR index + sidebar.\n- docs: regenerated REST API reference (clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs),\n  sequence diagrams, glossary, bounded-context canvas, quickstart, README.\n\n* style: gofmt idempotency integration test","tree":{"sha":"3fd7a6b6233274b1d8215d511596cd34803f94c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/3fd7a6b6233274b1d8215d511596cd34803f94c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/0df3efa830bdb28035e881684a4d4e882859cdc6","verification":{"payload":"tree 3fd7a6b6233274b1d8215d511596cd34803f94c4\nparent bdc5a37f38e2adc71389a2dd7b73e420f8967c9f\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791284388 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791284388 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#139)\n\n* fix(http): roll back domain writes of a non-2xx idempotent request\n\nRequireIdempotencyKey committed the shared transaction for any non-panic\nresponse. A late failure (409 concurrent-modification on the assignment\nSave after the associate hours Save of the same request) therefore\npersisted the earlier write. The wrapped handler now runs in a savepoint:\n2xx releases it, any other status rolls back to it, while the idempotency\nrow (inserted before the savepoint) still stores the failed response, so\nreplay semantics are unchanged.\n\nIntegration test (testcontainers) forces a real optimistic-concurrency\nconflict and asserts associate_shift, outbox and the stored 409 replay.\n\n* fix(usecases): convert measured seconds-per-task to a per-head hourly rate\n\nProposePathPlan divided the charge by labor-performance''s\nmeanActualSeconds (a duration per task) where a per-head hourly rate\n(units per head per hour, like plannedRate) is expected: a 36 s task\nproposed 100 heads for 3600 units instead of 36. The measured rate is now\n3600 / meanActualSeconds; a non-positive or non-finite duration is treated\nas ErrMeasuredRateUnavailable (fail-open, 0 heads).\n\nTests pin the conversion at several magnitudes and the degenerate inputs.\n\n* fix(api): declare /readyz, add observedIdleShare, record ADR-0033\n\n- apis/openapi.yaml: GET /readyz (200 ready / 503 not_ready) was served but\n  undeclared; a router-vs-spec drift test now guards every route.\n- staffing-gap responses gain observedIdleShare (a 0..1 fraction, the name\n  matches the value); observedIdlePct is kept with the unchanged value and\n  marked deprecated, so no consumer breaks (additive).\n- resolvedRate / plannedRate descriptions state the per-head hourly unit.\n- ADR-0033 records the idempotent-request atomicity fix, the measured-rate\n  unit conversion, the idle-share naming and /readyz; ADR index + sidebar.\n- docs: regenerated REST API reference (clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs),\n  sequence diagrams, glossary, bounded-context canvas, quickstart, README.\n\n* style: gofmt idempotency integration test","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNSkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApAgQAHcAb7atQTJYSoafrkizIuzn\n3lGNwe7aydLtzcwWcVaqeLR8Xyk7m0usErEMPhgpGAwNjJdLHnorBGvuHd+mdkBK\nd515996zfwGfVTRjffFdU23ScaVmsz0KFaVkWSsKQep7SEEDqFmC542itREjtnJo\nIyyjD3sA8a/XmfeGdBl013rixw8wTokWNUyR7lEiLhf6QYYlEZQk9xvy0df8fOd2\nE+mFXqyV3MajOpYizWfy7Y0JTQaZEgOLxo4abnun4nm2Lyyi64mD1tGL4/AV8gma\nqZUY5qnMoeQg+lyXZtBlBgzWbLviAIMzGnkE4ZF81wHoL/5YeIgwslexRpV25iuu\nPmPIgNuWA+jSvCiUBS1ESl9J8KWDG/Axliu58mwzZpNJhH3kEhBd1dlhMY5ty1eJ\n8Q7TbEHS7Pap7FOS2wnk1hQUtKC5/VlF1nA3uB3cM2p/68FmmTXDRyR9KD/V0ycr\nVU3nr/3z95jVMS2s+qs/UQ/INwm9jffgCNqlR93v6igm0lJSDxhFqJXw6lweD9UP\nlxfpWKjCMbcuoGVu1Skddu6TKmN8dSClMIh3Y47FX7vCfsvLQqQ8nn67FJ+xhH8P\nZaTWh1OBZSBMZMlyhCglhilWgUEi26LPjAGQmF8ldjeyRfMFl8ox1jjDiNs/Fmjx\nmHCJ8taWRFBUw8RxCije\n=JPPJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T10:59:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/0df3efa830bdb28035e881684a4d4e882859cdc6","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjCLdoAKDBkZjNlZmE4MzBiZGIyODAzNWU4ODE2ODRhNGQ0ZTg4Mjg1OWNkYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/bdc5a37f38e2adc71389a2dd7b73e420f8967c9f","sha":"bdc5a37f38e2adc71389a2dd7b73e420f8967c9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/bdc5a37f38e2adc71389a2dd7b73e420f8967c9f"}],"sha":"0df3efa830bdb28035e881684a4d4e882859cdc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/0df3efa830bdb28035e881684a4d4e882859cdc6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/bdc5a37f38e2adc71389a2dd7b73e420f8967c9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:54:16Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:54:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#137)\n\n* docs: refresh product docs against origin/develop\n\nGround every stale fact in the code on origin/develop:\n\n- README: IQVO Pages URL; env table gains MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL,\n  HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL, IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL, OUTBOX_RETENTION and\n  SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_DELAY; curl examples send the Idempotency-Key header the\n  two creation POSTs require (ADR-0027); add the all-paths staffing-gap\n  route (ADR-0029) and GET /readyz (ADR-0022); warehouse-planning is a\n  second ShiftPlanCommitted consumer; integration tests are all\n  testcontainers now; BDD table lists all nine feature files.\n- overview: eleven backend contexts (not five), nine use-case structs,\n  CI quality-gate table matches ci.yml (complexity, guide-lint, contract,\n  evals-tests, blocking mutation-fast, web), quickstart curls send\n  Idempotency-Key.\n- api-reference/index: 12 router routes, 11 in openapi.yaml (/readyz is\n  missing from the spec), Staffing tag has 2 operations.\n- adr/index: Status column for 0008, 0009 and 0011 now matches the ADR\n  bodies.\n- ddd: live installed-capacity invariant (ADR-0014) and the ADR-0021\n  version guard documented in invariants; catalogue-resolved certification\n  name; counts in subdomain-classification; warehouse-planning,\n  warehouse-ops-agent and warehouse-console rows in context-relationships.\n- ecosystem: warehouse-planning consumes ShiftPlanCommitted.\n- Old-org github.com/claudioed and claudioed.github.io links in prose docs\n  and .claude skills point at IQVO.\n- .claude/rules: REST table gains the all-paths route, /readyz and the\n  Idempotency-Key requirement; integrations names both consumers.\n\n* docs: WIP DDD artifact pack (agent interrupted by rate limit)\n\nPartial, unverified work committed to preserve it; the resume run reviews,\ncompletes and validates it.\n\n* docs: complete ddd-crew DDD artifact pack and refresh event, context-map and glossary pages\n\nAdds bounded-context-canvas, aggregate-design-canvas, domain-message-flow,\neventstorming, class-diagram, entity-relationship and sequence-diagrams\nunder docs/docs/ddd, all derived from internal/domain, the use cases,\nadapters and migrations. Refreshes domain-events (full CloudEvents types,\ntopics, keys, payloads, consumers), ecosystem/context-map (U/D + pattern\nlabelled flowchart LR with an evidence table) and the ubiquitous-language\nglossary (code mapping, terms whose code name differs). Wires the pack into\nsidebars.ts under \"DDD artifacts (ddd-crew)\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(claude): docs site moved to iqvo.github.io\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70534b153415a16c4ab90afacf7362277ff99d1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/70534b153415a16c4ab90afacf7362277ff99d1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/bdc5a37f38e2adc71389a2dd7b73e420f8967c9f","verification":{"payload":"tree 70534b153415a16c4ab90afacf7362277ff99d1f\nparent 02d801b61dbcf4ed64aa173a4a4cc079f358ef5b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791269656 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791269656 -0300\n\ndocs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#137)\n\n* docs: refresh product docs against origin/develop\n\nGround every stale fact in the code on origin/develop:\n\n- README: IQVO Pages URL; env table gains MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL,\n  HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL, IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL, OUTBOX_RETENTION and\n  SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_DELAY; curl examples send the Idempotency-Key header the\n  two creation POSTs require (ADR-0027); add the all-paths staffing-gap\n  route (ADR-0029) and GET /readyz (ADR-0022); warehouse-planning is a\n  second ShiftPlanCommitted con