de_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/3fb63be645ca1b3144b09dcf505d7cc8d573954d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjCLdoAKDNmYjYzYmU2NDVjYTFiMzE0NGIwOWRjZjUwNWQ3Y2M4ZDU3Mzk1NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/25058ba064a470d2e41108f2a121d41920424d9c","sha":"25058ba064a470d2e41108f2a121d41920424d9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/25058ba064a470d2e41108f2a121d41920424d9c"}],"sha":"3fb63be645ca1b3144b09dcf505d7cc8d573954d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/3fb63be645ca1b3144b09dcf505d7cc8d573954d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/25058ba064a470d2e41108f2a121d41920424d9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:47:56Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:47:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ADR-conformance gaps (MCP outbox, Idempotency-Key, shutdown, metrics, docs) (#132)\n\n* fix(mcp): publish assign_labor events through the transactional outbox and validate path ids (ADR-0008/0013/0016)\n\ncmd/mcp used LogPublisher and no UnitOfWork, so MCP-triggered LaborAssigned/LaborReassigned never reached Kafka or analytics. Extract internal/composition (BuildEventPublisher, BuildCatalogue) shared by cmd/workforce and cmd/mcp; MCP only inserts outbox rows (relay stays in cmd/workforce). Add Catalogue to MCP Deps so tool path ids get ADR-0013 validation; add otelchi/otelchimetric to the MCP router; wire EVENT_PUBLISHER, KAFKA_BROKERS and the path catalogue in the chart''s mcp-deployment.\n\n* fix(idempotency,shutdown): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware, housekeeping sweeper, ADR-0022 shutdown drain (ADR-0022/0021/0027/0028)\n\n- RequireIdempotencyKey route-scoped on POST /shift-plans and POST /associates/{id}/assignments when IdempotencyPool is wired; 400 idempotency-key-required, 422 idempotency-key-reused, byte-identical replay, panic rollback+repanic; shares its transaction with the use case via new internal/pgtx (idempotency row, aggregate save and outbox insert commit atomically)\n- migration 000004 idempotency_keys (+ created_at and published_at sweep indexes); CORS allows Idempotency-Key\n- housekeeping Sweeper (postgres) + cmd/workforce wiring: IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL 24h, OUTBOX_RETENTION 7d, HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL 1h, 0 disables\n- ADR-0022 section 8 shutdown order in cmd/workforce/serve.go: readiness flip -> SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_DELAY wait (default 10s = 2 probe periods, 0 in tests) -> HTTP Shutdown -> consumers -> sweeper -> relay -> pool last; unit-tested order incl. /readyz 503 during the drain window\n- ADR-0027 and ADR-0028 + index/sidebar entries; values.yaml/deployment.yaml env + terminationGracePeriod comment fix; OpenAPI header (optional, no minLength) + 400/422 + regenerated api-reference docs\n\n* fix(metrics): move workforce.labor_assignments behind ports.LaborMetrics with fleet attribute keys (ADR-0015)\n\nThe counter was created on the global otel.Meter inside the application layer and used workforce.assignment.outcome/reason attribute keys, violating Tier-2 placement and the fleet''s plain outcome/reason convention. The instrument now lives in internal/adapters/outbound/telemetry (LaborMetrics) behind a new ports.LaborMetrics port; AssignLabor takes it as an optional dependency; cmd/workforce and cmd/mcp both wire it so HTTP- and MCP-triggered assignments count on the identical instrument. Instrument name and workforce.path.id key unchanged (series-compatible); outcome/reason keys renamed. ADR-0015 status note + amended consequence added; reports router already had otelchi+otelchimetric (verified, no change needed).\n\n* fix(labor): normalise required certification through the path catalogue (ADR-0009/ADR-0013)\n\nAssignLabor matched the required certification against the RAW caller-supplied pathId while the catalogue (ADR-0013) recognises case-insensitive prefix families, so a certified associate was rejected over a case variant (PICK vs pick) or zone suffix (pick-zone-a). The required certification is now resolved through the catalogue''s canonical family prefix when one is wired (nil catalogue keeps the historical raw-id convention, i.e. the in-memory test configuration). Wired in cmd/workforce and cmd/mcp. ADR-0009 amended: hazmat is a station capability a declared family (hazmat-pick) requires, not a catalogue-declared path id — bare hazmat is 400 unknown-path-id; new tests: TestAssignLabor_CatalogueNormalisesRequiredCertification (use cases) and TestAssignLabor_HazmatPath_ThroughHTTP (catalogue-validating HTTP route, as the conformance pass requires).\n\n* feat(web): default the Workforce screen to the all-paths staffing-gap endpoint (ADR-0011)\n\nThe deferred GET /buildings/{buildingId}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap list endpoint shipped, but the MFE still did one-path-at-a-time lookups. The screen now defaults to the all-paths view for a building/shift (one request, every planned path, understaffed summary) and keeps the single-path lookup as an explicit ''By path'' mode. Endpoint URLs extracted into web/src/apiUrls.ts with vitest coverage (the suite has no jsdom, so the URL builders are the tested seam); ADR-0011 amended to record that the fast-follow shipped and the screen adopted it.\n\n* docs(adr): fix drift across 0004/0007/0008/0011/0013/0016/0025, dedupe sidebar positions, add short ADRs 0029-0032\n\n- 0004: ''zero in / no consumer group / no sync call'' amended to today''s reality (3 consumers, 2 sync clients, all cross-referenced); description no longer claims the catalog is ''ahead of'' the wire\n- 0007: CI job names corrected (api-lint, docs-api-drift; helm-lint is PRs-to-main only)\n- 0008: status notes auth superseded by ADR-0018; auth.go/key-Secret/rate-limit/scope-outcome-span claims removed or amended; dangling ''See ADR-0009'' OAuth pointer replaced\n- 0011: amended for ADR-0029 (all-paths endpoint shipped, screen adopted it)\n- 0013: documents the nil-catalogue decision (fail-closed at boot in composition.BuildCatalogue; handler nil branch is a test seam, panic-on-nil rejected)\n- 0016: outbox-lag follow-up recorded as shipped (workforce.outbox.lag_seconds) + ADR-0028 sweeper retention\n- 0025: reports-binary DSN statement corrected (no migrations; ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL fed from ANALYTICS_READER_DATABASE_URL key)\n- sidebar_position duplicates fixed (0006/0007/0008), missing positions added (0013-0018, 0021-0026); titles normalised to zero-padded numbering\n- pool.go comment: autoscaling.api.maxReplicas key\n- new short ADRs: 0029 all-paths staffing-gap endpoint, 0030 kafka-sourced catalogue, 0031 kafka writer durability, 0032 bootretry; index + sidebar updated; docs build passes\n\n* fix(mcp): use quietLogger() in the outbox integration test so the package compiles under -tags=integration\n\n* test(postgres): convert env-gated Postgres integration tests to testcontainers (ADR audit item 8)\n\n- postgres/integration_test.go: shared TestMain boots ONE testcontainers\n  postgres:16-alpine per package, migrates once, testPool cleans tables\n  between tests; the DATABASE_URL env gate and t.Skip are gone.\n- analyticsstore/postgres_integration_test.go: same shared-TestMain\n  pattern with its own container and migrations/analytics; the\n  ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL gate is gone; read-only-pool test builds its\n  own pool over the shared URL.\n- ci.yml integration job: drop the service containers and env vars -\n  every -tags=integration test is now self-sufficient (matches\n  order-management''s converted job).\n- Makefile: integration target no longer needs a running Postgres.","tree":{"sha":"14eec44ff6266bb8b5203787feb6f34c0a5fd8d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/14eec44ff6266bb8b5203787feb6f34c0a5fd8d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/25058ba064a470d2e41108f2a121d41920424d9c","verification":{"payload":"tree 14eec44ff6266bb8b5203787feb6f34c0a5fd8d4\nparent 9081d3cf636abae27a5c162c92563e97c57be086\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791168476 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791168476 -0300\n\nfix: ADR-conformance gaps (MCP outbox, Idempotency-Key, shutdown, metrics, docs) (#132)\n\n* fix(mcp): publish assign_labor events through the transactional outbox and validate path ids (ADR-0008/0013/0016)\n\ncmd/mcp used LogPublisher and no UnitOfWork, so MCP-triggered LaborAssigned/LaborReassigned never reached Kafka or analytics. Extract internal/composition (BuildEventPublisher, BuildCatalogue) shared by cmd/workforce and cmd/mcp; MCP only inserts outbox rows (relay stays in cmd/workforce). Add Catalogue to MCP Deps so tool path ids get ADR-0013 validation; add otelchi/otelchimetric to the MCP router; wire EVENT_PUBLISHER, KAFKA_BROKERS and the path catalogue in the chart''s mcp-deployment.\n\n* fix(idempotency,shutdown): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware, housekeeping sweeper, ADR-0022 shutdown drain (ADR-0022/0021/0027/0028)\n\n- RequireIdempotencyKey route-scoped on POST /shift-plans and POST /associates/{id}/assignments when IdempotencyPool is wired; 400 idempotency-key-required, 422 idempotency-key-reused, byte-identical replay, panic rollback+repanic; shares its transaction with the use case via new internal/pgtx (idempotency row, aggregate save and outbox insert commit atomically)\n- migration 000004 idempotency_keys (+ created_at and published_at sweep indexes); CORS allows Idempotency-Key\n- housekeeping Sweeper (postgres) + cmd/workforce wiring: IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL 24h, OUTBOX_RETENTION 7d, HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL 1h, 0 disables\n- ADR-0022 section 8 shutdown order in cmd/workforce/serve.go: readiness flip -> SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_DELAY wait (default 10s = 2 probe periods, 0 in tests) -> HTTP Shutdown -> consumers -> sweeper -> relay -> pool last; unit-tested order incl. /readyz 503 during the drain window\n- ADR-0027 and ADR-0028 + index/sidebar entries; values.yaml/deployment.yaml env + terminationGracePeriod comment fix; OpenAPI header (optional, no minLength) + 400/422 + regenerated api-reference docs\n\n* fix(metrics): move workforce.labor_assignments behind ports.LaborMetrics with fleet attribute keys (ADR-0015)\n\nThe counter was created on the global otel.Meter inside the application layer and used workforce.assignment.outcome/reason attribute keys, violating Tier-2 placement and the fleet''s plain outcome/reason convention. The instrument now lives in internal/adapters/outbound/telemetry (LaborMetrics) behind a new ports.LaborMetrics port; AssignLabor takes it as an optional dependency; cmd/workforce and cmd/mcp both wire it so HTTP- and MCP-triggered assignments count on the identical instrument. Instrument name and workforce.path.id key unchanged (series-compatible); outcome/reason keys renamed. ADR-0015 status note + amended consequence added; reports router already had otelchi+otelchimetric (verified, no change needed).\n\n* fix(labor): normalise required certification through the path catalogue (ADR-0009/ADR-0013)\n\nAssignLabor matched the required certification against the RAW caller-supplied pathId while the catalogue (ADR-0013) recognises case-insensitive prefix families, so a certified associate was rejected over a case variant (PICK vs pick) or zone suffix (pick-zone-a). The required certification is now resolved through the catalogue''s canonical family prefix when one is wired (nil catalogue keeps the historical raw-id convention, i.e. the in-memory test configuration). Wired in cmd/workforce and cmd/mcp. ADR-0009 amended: hazmat is a station capability a declared family (hazmat-pick) requires, not a catalogue-declared path id — bare hazmat is 400 unknown-path-id; new tests: TestAssignLabor_CatalogueNormalisesRequiredCertification (use cases) and TestAssignLabor_HazmatPath_ThroughHTTP (catalogue-validating HTTP route, as the conformance pass requires).\n\n* feat(web): default the Workforce screen to the all-paths staffing-gap endpoint (ADR-0011)\n\nThe deferred GET /buildings/{buildingId}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap list endpoint shipped, but the MFE still did one-path-at-a-time lookups. The screen now defaults to the all-paths view for a building/shift (one request, every planned path, understaffed summary) and keeps the single-path lookup as an explicit ''By path'' mode. Endpoint URLs extracted into web/src/apiUrls.ts with vitest coverage (the suite has no jsdom, so the URL builders are the tested seam); ADR-0011 amended to record that the fast-follow shipped and the screen adopted it.\n\n* docs(adr): fix drift across 0004/0007/0008/0011/0013/0016/0025, dedupe sidebar positions, add short ADRs 0029-0032\n\n- 0004: ''zero in / no consumer group / no sync call'' amended to today''s reality (3 consumers, 2 sync clients, all cross-referenced); description no longer claims the catalog is ''ahead of'' the wire\n- 0007: CI job names corrected (api-lint, docs-api-drift; helm-lint is PRs-to-main only)\n- 0008: status notes auth superseded by ADR-0018; auth.go/key-Secret/rate-limit/scope-outcome-span claims removed or amended; dangling ''See ADR-0009'' OAuth pointer replaced\n- 0011: amended for ADR-0029 (all-paths endpoint shipped, screen adopted it)\n- 0013: documents the nil-catalogue decision (fail-closed at boot in composition.BuildCatalogue; handler nil branch is a test seam, panic-on-nil rejected)\n- 0016: outbox-lag follow-up recorded as shipped (workforce.outbox.lag_seconds) + ADR-0028 sweeper retention\n- 0025: reports-binary DSN statement corrected (no migrations; ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL fed from ANALYTICS_READER_DATABASE_URL key)\n- sidebar_position duplicates fixed (0006/0007/0008), missing positions added (0013-0018, 0021-0026); titles normalised to zero-padded numbering\n- pool.go comment: autoscaling.api.maxReplicas key\n- new short ADRs: 0029 all-paths staffing-gap endpoint, 0030 kafka-sourced catalogue, 0031 kafka writer durability, 0032 bootretry; index + sidebar updated; docs build passes\n\n* fix(mcp): use quietLogger() in the outbox integration test so the package compiles under -tags=integration\n\n* test(postgres): convert env-gated Postgres integration tests to testcontainers (ADR audit item 8)\n\n- postgres/integration_test.go: shared TestMain boots ONE testcontainers\n  postgres:16-alpine per package, migrates once, testPool cleans tables\n  between tests; the DATABASE_URL env gate and t.Skip are gone.\n- analyticsstore/postgres_integration_test.go: same shared-TestMain\n  pattern with its own container and migrations/analytics; the\n  ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL gate is gone; read-only-pool test builds its\n  own pool over the shared URL.\n- ci.yml integration job: drop the service containers and env vars -\n  every -tags=integration test is now self-sufficient (matches\n  order-management''s converted job).\n- Makefile: integration target no longer needs a running Postgres.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqww/cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMXQQAEaLQBnuaT7ZrOszBa8ltTtF\nqTsvaOqpCTt+c5m5+gDOd/6lT9PsIjdSZNPK6K0rDBqxvEnyL0ByncDdXB+4NSqh\nZei1pRDM/hwt+vE7KVm0NN6SvEeAIATIw9Je8/hPh0hSziLcCf4NwMDKkB508392\nysp6EGnUkUTvWs1WGMEuDnyFiXVWA3Cf6hvz7VVKK5yVO/X3S9FDcYgQ47lHiPUJ\nnNkZhP0yr1GaBuV8JMLY/5otHfLCrm11fCa/Yog+0rlywCe6DeZ4ldw+4WvsT+sC\nhPADEOD/EZoVVEtEQVfwqN/DFt/uoMRR/uHdGuv7zFPHaw+PSPLlLNH6s5g/2kt0\n1EXIlYdG19YmpEOAst2DELerRe1etbk7zMr8yo+7tGq1oJQhOwyGT87YqwBD3VEM\n29vliUYAZWjhYQjvyg8x2rPSONBlUDWptV4XZS4mPF+ZNvuEAJg7lzQGQEqkfvOl\nFhKzB7Ia5gAfx595UEM5vlfsUPUNOVwwTdt2H9pvKZVHnenywfCfoh2tvEKS2Ntp\nONOnx9US3D99Yu72K9qd33BscLqHBr3FWDcHoZNZRD6DdIGxii9/TX7KbFYvVjT5\nZovpW4HHPRQnla2M9ldpiIMTm9Z7yK4okHN8Xc4wcPxFqqZvWATe5whe1GI+qMe8\npJq/RPmAZ0v4AeBRPl2f\n=Xoa0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T02:47:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api