s://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/0e2c2cee6d2914a98d86fa05ab27f35d8843ae31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T02:03:11Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T02:03:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(events)!: CloudEvents 1.0 mandatory envelope, remove flat/dual modes (#120)\n\n* feat(events)!: CloudEvents 1.0 mandatory envelope on every Kafka message\n\nEvery message workforce-management produces or consumes is now a\nCloudEvents 1.0 structured-mode event, built and validated with\ngithub.com/cloudevents/sdk-go/v2/event (v2.16.2) through the single\nhelper package internal/adapters/kafka/cloudevents (ADR-0026).\n\nPublishers (direct path AND outbox Encode path):\n- integration ShiftPlanCommitted keeps the one-message-per-PathPlan-line\n  fan-out; each line gets its own id, minted once in Encode and persisted\n  with the outbox row; subject = Kafka key = <buildingId>/<shiftId>;\n  dataschema urn:warehouse:workforce-management:events:ShiftPlanCommitted:v1\n- analytics publisher emits all ten events as CloudEvents with\n  dataschema ...:analytics:<Event>:v1; schema_version is removed\n- every message carries content-type: application/cloudevents+json;\n  charset=UTF-8 next to the trace headers; data payloads byte-identical\n- writers use kafkago.Hash{} so the existing keys actually route (they\n  were LeastBytes, which ignores the key, contrary to ADR-0023)\n\nConsumers decode with cloudevents.Decode and dispatch on the full type:\n- kafkacatalog: com.warehouse.wes.process-path-management.processpath.\n  ProcessPathCreated/Updated/Deactivated; invalid -> WARN + skip\n- laborperformancecache: com.warehouse.wes.labor-performance.performance.\n  TaskPerformanceRecorded; dedupes on (source,id); invalid -> WARN + skip\n- analytics projector: dedupes on id, time from the attribute; invalid\n  CloudEvents -> existing DLQ path\n\nRemoved: flat envelope structs, AnalyticsEnvelope, short-name dispatch\nconstants. Tests: golden exact-JSON per published type incl. header,\nlegacy-flat-message-rejected per consumer, testcontainers integration\ntests updated to the CloudEvents wire format.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the flat envelope is gone with no coexistence. Must\ndeploy together with the fleet cutover; see warehouse-infra\ndocs/cloudevents-cutover.md.\n\n* docs(events): ADR-0026 CloudEvents mandatory envelope; AsyncAPI matches the wire\n\n- new ADR-0026 \"CloudEvents 1.0 as the mandatory event envelope\",\n  registered in the ADR index and sidebars\n- ADR-0004 (envelope half) and ADR-0010 (Envelope v1) marked superseded\n- apis/asyncapi.yaml: all attributes required, exact type const and\n  dataschema const per message, analytics channel added, no\n  \"ahead of the wire\" caveats, examples match the real payloads\n- events/integration/labor-report/DDD pages, README, INTEGRATION.md,\n  .claude rules + skill and CLAUDE.md (AGENTS.md symlink) rewritten to\n  the CloudEvents shape","tree":{"sha":"1c0acfc91362790bd2ab1afd4027ea10a46f7c97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/1c0acfc91362790bd2ab1afd4027ea10a46f7c97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/0e2c2cee6d2914a98d86fa05ab27f35d8843ae31","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c0acfc91362790bd2ab1afd4027ea10a46f7c97\nparent 0e3834172dc4091bb34e36ed69242eb150b66a71\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790820191 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790820191 -0300\n\nfeat(events)!: CloudEvents 1.0 mandatory envelope, remove flat/dual modes (#120)\n\n* feat(events)!: CloudEvents 1.0 mandatory envelope on every Kafka message\n\nEvery message workforce-management produces or consumes is now a\nCloudEvents 1.0 structured-mode event, built and validated with\ngithub.com/cloudevents/sdk-go/v2/event (v2.16.2) through the single\nhelper package internal/adapters/kafka/cloudevents (ADR-0026).\n\nPublishers (direct path AND outbox Encode path):\n- integration ShiftPlanCommitted keeps the one-message-per-PathPlan-line\n  fan-out; each line gets its own id, minted once in Encode and persisted\n  with the outbox row; subject = Kafka key = <buildingId>/<shiftId>;\n  dataschema urn:warehouse:workforce-management:events:ShiftPlanCommitted:v1\n- analytics publisher emits all ten events as CloudEvents with\n  dataschema ...:analytics:<Event>:v1; schema_version is removed\n- every message carries content-type: application/cloudevents+json;\n  charset=UTF-8 next to the trace headers; data payloads byte-identical\n- writers use kafkago.Hash{} so the existing keys actually route (they\n  were LeastBytes, which ignores the key, contrary to ADR-0023)\n\nConsumers decode with cloudevents.Decode and dispatch on the full type:\n- kafkacatalog: com.warehouse.wes.process-path-management.processpath.\n  ProcessPathCreated/Updated/Deactivated; invalid -> WARN + skip\n- laborperformancecache: com.warehouse.wes.labor-performance.performance.\n  TaskPerformanceRecorded; dedupes on (source,id); invalid -> WARN + skip\n- analytics projector: dedupes on id, time from the attribute; invalid\n  CloudEvents -> existing DLQ path\n\nRemoved: flat envelope structs, AnalyticsEnvelope, short-name dispatch\nconstants. Tests: golden exact-JSON per published type incl. header,\nlegacy-flat-message-rejected per consumer, testcontainers integration\ntests updated to the CloudEvents wire format.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the flat envelope is gone with no coexistence. Must\ndeploy together with the fleet cutover; see warehouse-infra\ndocs/cloudevents-cutover.md.\n\n* docs(events): ADR-0026 CloudEvents mandatory envelope; AsyncAPI matches the wire\n\n- new ADR-0026 \"CloudEvents 1.0 as the mandatory event envelope\",\n  registered in the ADR index and sidebars\n- ADR-0004 (envelope half) and ADR-0010 (Envelope v1) marked superseded\n- apis/asyncapi.yaml: all attributes required, exact type const and\n  dataschema const per message, analytics channel added, no\n  \"ahead of the wire\" caveats, examples match the real payloads\n- events/integration/labor-report/DDD pages, README, INTEGRATION.md,\n  .claude rules + skill and CLAUDE.md (AGENTS.md symlink) rewritten to\n  the CloudEvents shape","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvb9fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+18QAJKDKsNObR+dRu9tQl1OD083\n/WSmxxhLoZuoxIwo5bl26mZ13hJ06tPMbzSi8sCuFzZua6X/ISPOIfl2UPcshKKV\n9IxmNijd+4A55nqYdxLF1r6nq0mw3qJNVPip5syDOIoU4YJaujJCDtpILYwGiRlI\nfjB5NGuVGroDDEO0oQFMYYvSADwKOzmFLfXbGv0I/CXsWZjRG5xyicO0vK1ueMRp\nSvfT2ADwTje0cWONVnSQYUHytPt/9D0eYHJjTP6aeLsw2fS8W7sEdp76LBZGUB4S\n17xoiFLZwfd8zB3v7g7HT0hXonZlbuCIz0a4/9peJMCuFwnapnG35pfEI3NHSppN\nDtgGKzgAsioBY8uzvy0S9AQYN5nMD473/ARDEbhP9Cu9NtFCGqaQzsqU78BHg+Yz\nNLN5b+EBtMK+VD9q9aqDBW40va6qyqYQ3x6uoPyJnbuLIedsGY5JwMhjCUAiSiWJ\nliOrXpQ7cs1imFFy2JuQ4WCfa9d4+uQGyUaujxYuWgRTIEtfcDtN8U3lg6wq6+HH\ng+WFZgDN9erQX6CqX7alutpQ6IqWLaEDw35NqbxVm1woGG3QiqsKlE