:{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/31ce9dd3a0422ab580c7674ff48ba82cff672028/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:46Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (#107)\n\nPhase 3 (scalability) fan-out, porting order-management''s reference PR\n#110 / ADR-0026 verbatim to workforce-management''s own chart and Postgres\nadapters — do not redesign, mirror the reference.\n\n1. HorizontalPodAutoscaler (autoscaling/v2) per independently-assessed\n   Deployment, replacing the previous flat single-HPA-on-api-only shape:\n   - api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU (stateless OLTP; its two Kafka caches\n     use per-process-unique consumer groups, safe at N)\n   - analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU (workforce-analytics\n     consumer group verified stable/shared, safe at N via normal Kafka\n     rebalancing; capped below api per the reference''s reasoning)\n   - analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU (stateless read-only\n     reader)\n   - frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU (static asset serving)\n   - mcp: deliberately excluded (no autoscaling.mcp block) — the MCP Go\n     SDK''s StreamableHTTPHandler keeps in-memory per-process session\n     state keyed by Mcp-Session-Id, and mcp-service.yaml has no\n     sessionAffinity, so a second replica could misroute a mid-session\n     request.\n\n   Every autoscaling.<x>.enabled defaults to false. Each Deployment''s\n   static replicas: field is now guarded with\n   `{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so the HPA never\n   fights a hardcoded replica count. Verified with helm template across\n   default (0 HPAs, all Deployments keep static replicas), all-enabled\n   (4 HPAs render, mcp still has replicas), and mixed (only api enabled)\n   combinations.\n\n2. pgxpool.Config.MaxConns + statement_timeout on all three pools,\n   matching order-management''s numbers (same shared-Postgres-instance\n   topology, same PgBouncer front end per warehouse-infra PR #43):\n   - OLTP (postgres.NewPool, cmd/workforce + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10,\n     statement_timeout=5s\n   - Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/workforce-projector):\n     MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=10s\n   - Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool,\n     cmd/workforce-reports): MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=15s\n\n   Proven against a real Postgres via testcontainers\n   (pool_limits_integration_test.go, -tags=integration): statement_timeout\n   actually cancels a pg_sleep past the configured duration (SQLSTATE\n   57014), and MaxConns actually blocks a further Acquire once the\n   ceiling is reached.\n\n3. ADR-0024 documents both, including the shared-Postgres finding, the\n   PgBouncer-already-in-front context (so this ADR''s connection-budget\n   section differs from order-management''s pre-PgBouncer one), and the\n   per-workload HPA table with the mcp exclusion reasoning verified\n   directly against this repo''s own mcp adapter code.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt, make check,\nmake arch-test, make coverage (99.3%, gate 90%), go test -tags=integration\n./... -race -count=1, helm lint, helm template (default/all-on/mixed),\nand the existing chart selector-conformance test.","tree":{"sha":"eda4b8ebf048abba608e712af0f24a95baad24f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/eda4b8ebf048abba608e712af0f24a95baad24f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/31ce9dd3a0422ab580c7674ff48ba82cff672028","verification":{"payload":"tree eda4b8ebf048abba608e712af0f24a95baad24f7\nparent aff9553ff5f5bd8da07f56f8b9249eecabca69a1\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790567986 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790567986 -0300\n\nfeat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (#107)\n\nPhase 3 (scalability) fan-out, porting order-management''s reference PR\n#110 / ADR-0026 verbatim to workforce-management''s own chart and Postgres\nadapters — do not redesign, mirror the reference.\n\n1. HorizontalPodAutoscaler (autoscaling/v2) per independently-assessed\n   Deployment, replacing the previous flat single-HPA-on-api-only shape:\n   - api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU (stateless OLTP; its two Kafka caches\n     use per-process-unique consumer groups, safe at N)\n   - analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU (workforce-analytics\n     consumer group verified stable/shared, safe at N via normal Kafka\n     rebalancing; capped below api per the reference''s reasoning)\n   - analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU (stateless read-only\n     reader)\n   - frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU (static asset serving)\n   - mcp: deliberately excluded (no autoscaling.mcp block) — the MCP Go\n     SDK''s StreamableHTTPHandler keeps in-memory per-process session\n     state keyed by Mcp-Session-Id, and mcp-service.yaml has no\n     sessionAffinity, so a second replica could misroute a mid-session\n     request.\n\n   Every autoscaling.<x>.enabled defaults to false. Each Deployment''s\n   static replicas: field is now guarded with\n   `{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so the HPA never\n   fights a hardcoded replica count. Verified with helm template across\n   default (0 HPAs, all Deployments keep static replicas), all-enabled\n   (4 HPAs render, mcp still has replicas), and mixed (only api enabled)\n   combinations.\n\n2. pgxpool.Config.MaxConns + statement_timeout on all three pools,\n   matching order-management''s numbers (same shared-Postgres-instance\n   topology, same PgBouncer front end per warehouse-infra PR #43):\n   - OLTP (postgres.NewPool, cmd/workforce + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10,\n     statement_timeout=5s\n   - Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/workforce-projector):\n     MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=10s\n   - Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool,\n     cmd/workforce-reports): MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=15s\n\n   Proven against a real Postgres via testcontainers\n   (pool_limits_integration_test.go, -tags=integration): statement_timeout\n   actually cancels a pg_sleep past the configured duration (SQLSTATE\n   57014), and MaxConns actually blocks a further Acquire once the\n   ceiling is reached.\n\n3. ADR-0024 documents both, including the shared-Postgres finding, the\n   PgBouncer-already-in-front context (so this ADR''s connection-budget\n   section differs from order-management''s pre-PgBouncer one), and the\n   per-workload HPA table with the mcp exclusion reasoning verified\n   directly against this repo''s own mcp adapter code.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt, make check,\nmake arch-test, make coverage (99.3%, gate 90%), go test -tags=integration\n./... -race -count=1, helm lint, helm template (default/all-on/mixed),\nand the existing chart selector-conformance test.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueYyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACj4QAJCFNYtHcUC5CstAh4KXeygr\nNUPpsXw/4xYyb8Sqj3J4wx1pSQy9gY9Srarw37KB+D7vDzhUkPz/4zw5LillgEDc\nGCQlQBbT2nYcM/tuZaZ5eMQQcl2OCyw5ocaV8D4fPho2sEeTBzZlDohB4HdTJ/rH\n4BmfyBQ0qTXUivWDnw0ecEGDK/7ZuNSZWcB6ivhvqbD0VHQshpJJ9appi6GlBw6A\nZvTDiPWojiLF/HVYxQU9oQkSaGiVYVeIyAeTbKQSjYVGAuw08vno37LqhX4yAA9I\npxL40cNFr7JUyY/NpHhuf0UuiKwfdOKirfw+AedPJLLb64cH76uPlauZnhGUJc1R\nNcW2MCbIvaMn3Mc0KFucdMpYJAERmVb+pdmO6eyQM8RXx3AnJO6JKpooVe4rRVfr\nlqWKhI8DcTJ4WqJHaOVK9L9ztcFKKk6ik7x6j5mxsmVxAA9dNVq24oMLwwhpUKbc\nJAZu/etXQO8OxzU3b9SrbTOt326nxEqi6Nchnc2CmGifpJjxxRzFd0p356xPqHgU\nULF8nEOd0Fsz5S0FUf+kVChKJMuV4mk5YWwWC+Iq09fGJSN8e4IbRyyU+40zrQjk\n8vb+zd3XCN4h7d6mUbVWk6Vl07qRJzF6j7nhvmK8m9tW9ujQ7LUeL82FcPWxdiz+\nvw/+DJtBhLQeH/pIQTLQ\n=3M6i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:59:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/31ce9dd3a0422ab580c7674ff48ba82cff672028","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjCLdoAKDMxY2U5ZGQzYTA0MjJhYjU4MGM3Njc0ZmY0OGJhODJjZmY2NzIwMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/aff9553ff5f5bd8da07f56f8b9249eecabca69a1","sha":"aff9553ff5f5bd8da07f56f8b9249eecabca69a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/aff9553ff5f5bd8da07f56f8b9249eecabca69a1"}],"sha":"31ce9dd3a0422ab580c7674ff48ba82cff672028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/31ce9dd3a0422ab580c7674ff48ba82cff672028"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/aff9553ff5f5bd8da07f56f8b9249eecabca69a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:01:27Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:01:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): key integration publisher by ShiftPlan aggregate id (#106)\n\nThe integration Kafka publisher (internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/\npublisher.go) published ShiftPlanCommitted to warehouse.workforce.events\nwith no message Key -- the code''s own doc comment said so explicitly:\n\"Messages carry no key\". With the topic''s original single partition this\nwas accidentally safe: one partition is one ordered log, so every\nconsumer saw every ShiftPlanCommitted message in the order the broker\nreceived it regardless of key.\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #42 scaled every business topic, including this one,\nfrom 1 to 8 partitions. Unkeyed messages are now distributed across\npartitions by the writer''s LeastBytes balancer (queue size), not by\ncontent, so the several messages one CommitShiftPlan fans out -- one per\nPathPlan line -- and any later re-commit for the same building/shift\ncould land on different partitions and be consumed out of order relative\nto each other, silently violating per-aggregate ordering for\nwes-work-planning''s LaborPlanObserved projection.\n\nThis mirrors the pattern the sibling AnalyticsPublisher already uses\n(keyed by aggregate id since ADR 0016) but the integration publisher had\nnever adopted.\n\nChanges:\n- Encode now computes key = shiftPlanKey(buildingId, shiftId) once per\n  ShiftPlanCommitted event and sets it on every PathPlan-line message\n  fanned out from that event. shiftPlanKey mirrors the ShiftPlan\n  aggregate''s real composite identity (buildingId + \"/\" + shiftId), the\n  same identity used by the postgres repo''s composite primary key.\n- Removed/replaced the now-inaccurate \"Messages carry no key\" doc comment\n  with one documenting the new keying and its ordering guarantee.\n- Unit test (encode_test.go): updated the stale \"must have no key\"\n  assertion to assert the new deterministic key.\n- New unit test (publisher_test.go):\n  TestPublish_AllMessagesForSameShiftPlanCarryIdenticalKey -- publishes a\n  multi-line commit followed by a second, later commit for the SAME\n  building/shift via a recording fake Writer, and asserts every message\n  across both commits carries the identical, non-empty key.\n- New real-Kafka integration test\n  (publisher_partition_integration_test.go, -tags=integration,\n  testcontainers confluentinc/confluent-local): creates the topic with 8\n  partitions (matching the fleet''s post-scaleup count), publishes through\n  a real segmentio.Writer with the production Hash balancer, and asserts\n  every message for the same building/shift lands on the SAME partition.\n- ADR 0023 documents the fix, referencing warehouse-infra PR #42 as the\n  change that exposed the gap, and is wired into docs/docs/adr/index.md\n  and docs/sidebars.ts (which was also missing ADR 0022''s entry --\n  folded that omission into the same sidebar edit).\n\nVerified: go build/vet clean, gofmt clean, make check (fmt-check, vet,\nbuild, lint, test -race) green, make arch-test green, go test\n-tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 green (includes the new real-Kafka\npartition test and the full pre-existing outbox integration suite,\nunchanged), make coverage at 99.3% (gate 90%), docs npm run build green.","tree":{"sha":"e290e8b67bdc743cf635b5cb65288034b48b91a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/e290e8b67bdc743cf635b5cb65288034b48b91a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/aff9553ff5f5bd8da07f56f8b9249eecabca69a1","verification":{"payload":"tree e290e8b67bdc743cf635b5cb65288034b48b91a1\nparent 6cf5ff8afed0f0c89870c048ab1aeb100b9f9919\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790564487 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790564487 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): key integration publisher by ShiftPlan aggregate id (#106)\n\nThe integration Kafka publisher (internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/\npublisher.go) published ShiftPlanCommitted to warehouse.workforce.events\nwith no message Key -- the code''s own doc comment said so explicitly:\n\"Messages carry no key\". With the topic''s original single partition this\nwas accidentally safe: one partition is one ordered log, so every\nconsumer saw every ShiftPlanCommitted message in the order the broker\nreceived it regardless of key.\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #42 scaled every business topic, including this one,\nfrom 1 to 8 partitions. Unkeyed messages are now distributed across\npartitions by the writer''s LeastBytes balancer (queue size), not by\ncontent, so the several messages one CommitShiftPlan fans out -- one per\nPathPlan line -- and any later re-commit for the same building/shift\ncould land on different partitions and be consumed out of order relative\nto each other, silently violating per-aggregate ordering for\nwes-work-planning''s LaborPlanObserved projection.\n\nThis mirrors the pattern the sibling AnalyticsPublisher already uses\n(keyed by aggregate id since ADR 0016) but the integration publisher had\nnever adopted.\n\nChanges:\n- Encode now computes key = shiftPlanKey(buildingId, shiftId) once per\n  ShiftPlanCommitted event and sets it on every PathPlan-line message\n  fanned out from that event. shiftPlanKey mirrors the ShiftPlan\n  aggregate''s real composite identity (buildingId + \"/\" + shiftId), the\n  same identity used by the postgres repo''s composite primary key.\n- Removed/replaced the now-inaccurate \"Messages carry no key\" doc comment\n  with one documenting the new keying and its ordering guarantee.\n- Unit test (encode_test.go): updated the stale \"must have no key\"\n  assertion to assert the new deterministic key.\n- New unit test (publisher_test.go):\n  TestPublish_AllMessagesForSameShiftPlanCarryIdenticalKey -- publishes a\n  multi-line commit followed by a second, later commit for the SAME\n  building/shift via a recording fake Writer, and asserts every message\n  across both commits carries the identical, non-empty key.\n- New real-Kafka integration test\n  (publisher_partition_integration_test.go, -tags=integration,\n  testcontainers confluentinc/confluent-local): creates the topic with 8\n  partitions (matching the fleet''s post-scaleup count), publishes through\n  a real segmentio.Writer with the production Hash balancer, and asserts\n  every message for the same building/shift lands on the SAME partition.\n- ADR 0023 documents the fix, referencing warehouse-infra PR #42 as the\n  change that exposed the gap, and is wired into docs/docs/adr/index.md\n  and docs/sidebars.ts (which was also missing ADR 0022''s entry --\n  folded that omission into the same sidebar edit).\n\nVerified: go build/vet clean, gofmt clean, make check (fmt-check, vet,\nbuild, lint, test -race) green, make arch-test green, go test\n-tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 green (includes the new real-Kafka\npartition test and the full pre-existing outbox integration suite,\nunchanged), make coverage at 99.3% (gate 90%), docs npm run build green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqudiHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD+kQAH1XQYLl5mbevXnNx+mEb6tv\nnJWScHbGwFX32vId04YUH1nQL8qTPevQw45hSWwOmZCkRQuUMsN3c6PBCS7E1m5f\nenk6dhZrzRU9040ov4aiRI2DCxLFVV+BR4aDiNQR4mHGPhmLWt+eyQNXz2DJDEof\nHpvIydGc7sgRSiYHCQXgybxTLji3dbXRc42cx6Eaf1SNh8KbZdMKFlMAyQ+70ycy\n1Ak0FuTGVrZkLL6TfV2qqUx1EbWBIgw+Pk2lXnxA5lZscgCwH65Q8y44GHGXDlTw\nLzmPUYsbwxa/L50eOSFgvAD0szMycgo5r52ZHJNfLGq4R1plECVLAsKlkfAxy+7h\nIja1VlvJ0bYhbM8MQOSH+1SbiJT3zKThHMVJy0DJkNhciUjr1V6jJWe8G1bNzzfd\nOLiUe4QpIvHPAhkbrdzT4c0V82ThGvRIYql8B4NGEw8HRLSXGRcGBvU1I7lokttx\nRP6Wny7DQcszRnwhpz1HJbUSVchSTK7M1qdU9A8aEJdfQYbI0Psn84c2J0Mh9QL7\ntm/gadNc0O/PKL9+aph0ik6pRZXFex4rZH3bgjeFF0bxXS6ITqrbULAtnsjDttkO\nV9orRZampNqnNv/l2wBGxNons5vhKUipXpeWBBCKNii+e+qo6Q4fX7cnhR90o2Q+\na7uPluqvOgSgldcg0WP3\n=UhAf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:01:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"http