61a68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/f9ed92dc86509250ad8f984c7f97178994ca638a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:15:49Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:15:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Outbox-lag metric, fleet-wide staffing-gap list, destinationLocationRole decode (#94)\n\n* kafkacatalog: decode destinationLocationRole from process-path-management\n\nprocess-path-management publishes destinationLocationRole on the path\ncatalog Kafka payload, but this consumer silently dropped it (git grep\nconfirmed zero hits for the field anywhere in this repo). Wiring only:\ndecode it into pathData and thread it onto the local\npathcatalog.PathDefinition, matching the exact field/casing confirmed\nagainst process-path-management''s own dto.go/server.go/kafka publisher\non origin/develop.\n\nAdds TestConsumer_DecodesDestinationLocationRole.\n\n* postgres: add workforce.outbox.lag_seconds gauge\n\nADR-0016 flagged an outbox-lag metric as a follow-up: attempts/last_error\nwere already queryable but nothing surfaced lag as a metric. Adds an\nOTel Float64ObservableGauge, workforce.outbox.lag_seconds, reporting the\nage in seconds of the oldest unpublished outbox_events row (0 when fully\ndrained) -- the lag signal this schema most naturally supports without\na new column. Registered against the global MeterProvider alongside the\noutbox relay in kafka/outbox EVENT_PUBLISHER mode, unregistered on\nshutdown.\n\nAdds outbox_metrics_test.go (unit, scripted pgx.Row.Scan via a fake row)\nand outbox_lag_integration_test.go (//go:build integration, proves the\ngauge is observed via an OTel ManualReader once an event is stuck).\n\n* staffing-gap: add fleet-wide all-paths list endpoint\n\nADR-0011 flagged a fleet-wide ''all paths, one building/shift'' list\nendpoint as an explicit deferred fast-follow: the shipped screen only\nhad GET /paths/{pathId}/staffing-gap (single path, requires pathId).\n\nFactors GetStaffingGap''s per-path computation into a shared gapForLine\ncore so Execute (single path) and the new ExecuteAll (every path in the\nbuilding+shift''s committed plan) can never drift from each other.\nExecuteAll batches every PathUnderstaffed event it raises into one\nUnitOfWork scope rather than one per line.\n\nAdds GET /buildings/{buildingId}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap, reusing\nthe single-path DTO shape as a list. Updates apis/openapi.yaml (new\npath item + reusable BuildingId/ShiftId path parameters) and\nregenerates docs/docs/api-reference/rest via docusaurus gen-api-docs.\n\nAdds use-case tests (ExecuteAll: lists every path, cross-checks against\nExecute for the same path, batches events into one scope, no-scope when\nnothing is understaffed, not-found) and HTTP handler tests.","tree":{"sha":"494e53cdc6bb4d992b008bea9e3701940ca1ac4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/494e53cdc6bb4d992b008bea9e3701940ca1ac4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/f9ed92dc86509250ad8f984c7f97178994ca638a","verification":{"payload":"tree 494e53cdc6bb4d992b008bea9e3701940ca1ac4f\nparent 9fc391a97e9bdb7595d15bd948b9ddc45caf55c9\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790432149 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790432149 -0300\n\nOutbox-lag metric, fleet-wide staffing-gap list, destinationLocationRole decode (#94)\n\n* kafkacatalog: decode destinationLocationRole from process-path-management\n\nprocess-path-management publishes destinationLocationRole on the path\ncatalog Kafka payload, but this consumer silently dropped it (git grep\nconfirmed zero hits for the field anywhere in this repo). Wiring only:\ndecode it into pathData and thread it onto the local\npathcatalog.PathDefinition, matching the exact field/casing confirmed\nagainst process-path-management''s own dto.go/server.go/kafka publisher\non origin/develop.\n\nAdds TestConsumer_DecodesDestinationLocationRole.\n\n* postgres: add workforce.outbox.lag_seconds gauge\n\nADR-0016 flagged an outbox-lag metric as a follow-up: attempts/last_error\nwere already queryable but nothing surfaced lag as a metric. Adds an\nOTel Float64ObservableGauge, workforce.outbox.lag_seconds, reporting the\nage in seconds of the oldest unpublished outbox_events row (0 when fully\ndrained) -- the lag signal this schema most naturally supports without\na new column. Registered against the global MeterProvider alongside the\noutbox relay in kafka/outbox EVENT_PUBLISHER mode, unregistered on\nshutdown.\n\nAdds outbox_metrics_test.go (unit, scripted pgx.Row.Scan via a fake row)\nand outbox_lag_integration_test.go (//go:build integration, proves the\ngauge is observed via an OTel ManualReader once an event is stuck).\n\n* staffing-gap: add fleet-wide all-paths list endpoint\n\nADR-0011 flagged a fleet-wide ''all paths, one building/shift'' list\nendpoint as an explicit deferred fast-follow: the shipped screen only\nhad GET /paths/{pathId}/staffing-gap (single path, requires pathId).\n\nFactors GetStaffingGap''s per-path computation into a shared gapForLine\ncore so Execute (single path) and the new ExecuteAll (every path in the\nbuilding+shift''s committed plan) can never drift from each other.\nExecuteAll batches every PathUnderstaffed event it raises into one\nUnitOfWork scope rather than one per line.\n\nAdds GET /buildings/{buildingId}/shifts/{shiftId}/staffing-gap, reusing\nthe single-path DTO shape as a list. Updates apis/openapi.yaml (new\npath item + reusable BuildingId/ShiftId path parameters) and\nregenerates docs/docs/api-reference/rest via docusaurus gen-api-docs.\n\nAdds use-case tests (ExecuteAll: lists every path, cross-checks against\nExecute for the same path, batches events into one scope, no-scope when\nnothing is understaffed, not-found) and HTTP handler tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt9OVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAasMQAFRBOfTeV95qxpURypYsZKAF\nvBTHKJh+CVtcAlcbABd4nVYtVCK2F1v6ZAeVJ8No4siYkt9doY1uAnmebIMBWSlt\nbqAVrly71biVYoaoYcrYYBfVARZNBLDNYzTBPmBijNTOG4KAx2RkgrIz6atAY0HE\nL38P7HvQVzoQWYuzGNh7hh4wNzym26p2mmnNf4wv37xzPnNSOCd1Ew1Q/sW9QpeX\nZ52KBGQ4EU9PkEGkrq4ohEguPE2aIx0Rz0F2JJfFMX6rJuZrLC//9SodnAJvfvFG\nAqTySuciKMRFdT/avCY8HbGf16xYAXD/vzGlLAF82nmEwUvhJQpkIb0RU88b5vfo\n4rn2PqFiaNbC9pqQ3ritvnnmKIQkQJThe29Nypvowbhz1q6sUgg8ZPNM8GRedZZy\n5n2pucfbxuB+wN6i/7tcD9fUS7mlWEXrfxd/qiypectT2rMpsd+n0rD8N0VEmu56\nSVqbIpU9MFid97LA71nTcLDCQu4YYFHx+EvQxwAd7clzxwQIy2WAXC+axwVABcxP\npskNclLcSg7hlLChR2javjugBzdBQ3UXf1DE/ezxxIenDmba5IAHej0cHfHOISuN\nJEPoko3nY0SB1bXsLfONvbFh1f+Q6vpx7KmpbcuPMFRx4ZM4eQv68+7xnCcXXeXl\nzNI+Vacsa9wYXFSSNvkl\n=imzw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T14:15:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy