\n\nDocuments 4 open Dependabot alerts (adm-zip GHSA-vwc7-r8mq-g2x9,\n@faker-js/faker GHSA-qxc2-j82w-r537, image-size GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr and\nGHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq) as blocked on upstream -- no patched version exists\nfor adm-zip/image-size, and faker''s patched major breaks npm run build\nvia postman-collection/docusaurus-plugin-openapi-docs. See PR body.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqTWpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqisQACdMWU+5iXb/Rt+qrvcD+tbm\nONTWN5EijJojClTFbrzFuB3HMxupantEoOATbhw8ACprfee6ZO7knmo17m1AqrE2\nf7solkIz6aC5um9edt36Bl4ygR2MtjJKHg6ntVXm6iKVviQ3Q1T8kx/JaBUzUYg2\nlj5lFNdnlXqIxNkSY5bW+dDXgp4gRpZOJUi+iMrmMH9hbJBrwbhU1KrIdFW9nMmH\nOGmuhUSuPDRm6egSABMHwd0lKuvaMYNIqBKrTDe4da9k4ZILXA5ZaJ5/FCkp5Q9C\n+oriHXM7460b3rwilVpkL7TpSrQaoJGqB6UTB6PpIwkYqSqIf35IfMPevFB+luu8\n4vACJmVxflfBSGzd4m6EhYJE4JLZh8M46GpFuZrtuLILCNPKeBTv/nIM5d6dsOTu\noZpFs1xoPB84l1GBGMA6BWrtiYZzs0kemVj+ilex0chkKt5Wwph2c8s2KDXpasbG\navaT2cgHVti4LR5wOVz9/6mmRE5oRh/50qIu+cFlCWWy36wtuswaSXmxTKBQsxLY\nqyl1SdGRTWVAtOQf5n7NCW0r8gmhsGeLRCkJpxZiOGoOpXz5ryTjHhsYGctYaS0y\niTmyR1/kVBGz970F6cy0++ZbnyBEfA3ivgYq4F38P0WnyLbLoQb3XnSjz6vpnjZ4\nPJQeOZ0xoSS3EIgnt052\n=hTIH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T12:10:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/156a0025e437ab3409e19dccf5de006f08f6fe78","node_id":"C_kwDOUAjCLdoAKDE1NmEwMDI1ZTQzN2FiMzQwOWUxOWRjY2Y1ZGUwMDZmMDhmNmZlNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/workforce-management/commit/d7a97da1b087af8e7a3dad26565276e13c813583","sha":"d7a97da1b087af8e7a3dad26565276e13c813583","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/d7a97da1b087af8e7a3dad26565276e13c813583"}],"sha":"156a0025e437ab3409e19dccf5de006f08f6fe78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/156a0025e437ab3409e19dccf5de006f08f6fe78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/commits/d7a97da1b087af8e7a3dad26565276e13c813583/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:47:41Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T01:47:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add weekly continuous-drift sensor (#80)\n\nAdapt inventory-storage''s advisory, non-blocking `drift` job (same gate as\nthe existing scheduled `mutation` job: `workflow_dispatch` or `schedule`,\nweekly Monday 6am UTC cron already present in `on.schedule`).\n\nThe job runs:\n- `go tool deadcode -test ./...` for dead-code detection (test helpers\n  excluded from false positives)\n- `go mod tidy -diff` for stale/unused go.mod entries\n- `npx knip --no-exit-code` in `web/` for unused frontend exports/files/deps\n- `scripts/coverage-quality.py`, cross-referencing `go tool cover -func`\n  against gremlins'' LIVED-mutant report to flag high-coverage functions\n  (>=90%) whose covered lines still have a surviving mutant — i.e. tests\n  that execute a line but assert nothing about it\n\nAll four sub-checks are advisory only (`|| true` / `--no-exit-code`); the\njob never blocks a PR. Copied `scripts/coverage-quality.py` verbatim from\ninventory-storage (already reviewed/merged there).\n\nVerified locally before pushing:\n- `go build ./...`, `go mod tidy -diff` (clean) both pass\n- `deadcode -test ./...` runs and reports two harmless unreachable-func\n  hits (outbox_relay.WithBatchSize, a test fake) — proves the sensor fires\n- `go test ./internal/domain/... -coverprofile=... -covermode=atomic` +\n  `gremlins unleash ./internal/domain --workers 1 --timeout-coefficient 30`\n  -> 35/35 mutants killed, 100% efficacy/coverage\n- `scripts/coverage-quality.py` run against that real cover.out + gremlins\n  log -> \"no high-coverage functions with surviving mutants found. clean.\"\n- `npx knip --no-exit-code` in web/ runs cleanly, exit 0\n- YAML parses (`python3 -c \"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(...)\"`)","tree":{"sha":"dc7fcd13d823befd48b18ba5eee6e394b9113e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/trees/dc7fcd13d823befd48b18ba5eee6e394b9113e3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/workforce-management/git/commits/d7a97da1b087af8e7a3dad26565276e13c813583","verification":{"payload":"tree dc7fcd13d823befd48b18ba5eee6e394b9113e3c\nparent 639805f8bf5b77ed8dfd28813993526c26289b3e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789436861 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789436861 -0300\n\nci: add weekly continuous-drift sensor (#80)\n\nAdapt inventory-storage''s advisory, non-blocking `drift` job (same gate as\nthe existing scheduled `mutation` job: `workflow_dispatch` or `schedule`,\nweekly Monday 6am UTC cron already present in `on.schedule`).\n\nThe job runs:\n- `go tool deadcode -test ./...` for dead-code detection (test helpers\n  excluded from false positives)\n- `go mod tidy -diff` for stale/unused go.mod entries\n- `npx knip --no-exit-code` in `web/` for unused frontend exports/files/deps\n- `scripts/coverage-quality.py`, cross-referencing `go tool cover -func`\n  against gremlins'' LIVED-mutant report to flag high-coverage functions\n  (>=90%) whose covered lines still have a surviving mutant — i.e. tests\n  that execute a line but assert nothing about it\n\nAll four sub-checks are advisory only (`|| true` / `--no-exit-code`); the\njob never blocks a PR. Copied `scripts/coverage-quality.py` verbatim from\ninventory-storage (already reviewed/merged there).\n\nVerified locally before pushing:\n- `go build ./...`, `go mod tidy -diff` (clean) both pass\n- `deadcode -test ./...` runs and reports two harmless unreachable-func\n  hits (outbox_relay.WithBatchSize, a test fake) — proves the sensor fires\n- `go test ./internal/domain/... -coverprofile=... -covermode=atomic` +\n  `gremlins unleash ./internal/domain --workers 1 --timeout-coefficient 30`\n  -> 35/35 mutants killed, 100% efficacy/coverage\n- `scripts/coverage-quality.py` run against that real cover.out + gremlins\n  log -> \"no high-coverage functions with surviving mutants found. clean.\"\n- `npx knip --no-exit-code` in web/ runs cleanly, exit 0\n- YAML parses (`python3 -c \"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(...)\"`)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqKO9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATyYQAKWtRhC11TdirNEtdS7lzT+c\nWyGn/hSH8dNJLTMOoxrnSeJ8IHzapYdX+rwdK3sg9UT5FYibGHrsCwhiSRHI1Uhm\npdy8o7+3B7vx+AwjCpgJV5cWj1wYcVIPMALkNHmJv04wKn1B/eDNfP8bE7zaKDkB\nHq+ITtxI+dRilQbKBhk4ZJSBwSBqckogrOZ4nJ/jm4/2yXEQkv7cYV8b6ahELQOf\n3s+Mx4htg7l8hSsHaXdjOd4QwDXhYB2cQRhT9y6fUjl40q9hWPfO+S5nZHJUf8O9\n6kbIk9++b/zezHyD2zGFd/cr7R4IKwSvwv/SBUw3tPOy1UBi5pLiXElFcztUPxIm\nAAsyGEx6o256supAKv6kEWmA2KKpqH3kBGSw2wVdC4qMSC6NtBbaaWhXcNaKJHxF\nCAsFMWgL4d9fIGCu5phlRY049RQ8Md8o+Fk/5lexTv0v74mwm74Nu/2H0iugbcfV\nXL1//JCf6SwdD4H53bAkU7fxmoqg1uwz8MqaSIx7pK04Tac4Ork5PdpADBlrjGA3\nvt2gIQF+LOo07Ef0iUJvhuHYxuBrxR1NSygmYmAsEE7IJavbs0qfi5IGo2GbPoYq\naaIHLS8xa0AznNuq+Tr9RoO0ODk6Q5kzGzRvhTa456QxJH1Tn+IIvHMVsTvehBa+\ncAED8gMxWLSK1runRwxK\n=oJ/d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T01:47:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type