eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/aa4166295ae2bd718e7a1d32756f60f2191c082d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:40:32Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:40:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp): slug-prefixed tool errors per the fleet convention; record import-key decision (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#154)\n\n* feat(mcp): slug-prefixed tool errors per the fleet convention\n\nEvery MCP tool error now reads \"<slug>: detail\", the slug being the REST\nproblem slug for the same condition; unmapped errors become\n\"internal-error: an unexpected internal error occurred\" so internals do\nnot leak. Success payloads are unchanged. A blank or missing location\ncode on estimate_travel_distance is missing-location-code.\n\nThe MCP slug table mirrors the REST error table one-for-one, enforced by\nTestSlugTableMatchesRESTOneForOne. Tool descriptions document the error\nshape. Eval scenarios pin the slugs over the real wire.\n\n* docs: ADR 0033 (slug-prefixed MCP tool errors), ADR 0034 (import key kept)\n\nADR 0033 records the fleet tool-error convention and the ecosystem check\n(warehouse-ops-agent mcpclient is the only consumer). ADR 0034 records the\n2026-10-06 decision to keep FacilityLayoutImported keyed by its CloudEvents\nid. Updates the governance charter (section 8.3), the sequence diagram''s\nerror path (section 6), the eventstorming H5 row, the domain-events note,\nthe consumer guide, the ADR index and the sidebar.","tree":{"sha":"2b49dea153b83a8f8a7cd8e701d84cecb941b963","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/2b49dea153b83a8f8a7cd8e701d84cecb941b963"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/aa4166295ae2bd718e7a1d32756f60f2191c082d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b49dea153b83a8f8a7cd8e701d84cecb941b963\nparent 90208cb38ff0446b7970ab14f7995803edf1ad2e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791330032 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791330032 -0300\n\nfeat(mcp): slug-prefixed tool errors per the fleet convention; record import-key decision (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#154)\n\n* feat(mcp): slug-prefixed tool errors per the fleet convention\n\nEvery MCP tool error now reads \"<slug>: detail\", the slug being the REST\nproblem slug for the same condition; unmapped errors become\n\"internal-error: an unexpected internal error occurred\" so internals do\nnot leak. Success payloads are unchanged. A blank or missing location\ncode on estimate_travel_distance is missing-location-code.\n\nThe MCP slug table mirrors the REST error table one-for-one, enforced by\nTestSlugTableMatchesRESTOneForOne. Tool descriptions document the error\nshape. Eval scenarios pin the slugs over the real wire.\n\n* docs: ADR 0033 (slug-prefixed MCP tool errors), ADR 0034 (import key kept)\n\nADR 0033 records the fleet tool-error convention and the ecosystem check\n(warehouse-ops-agent mcpclient is the only consumer). ADR 0034 records the\n2026-10-06 decision to keep FacilityLayoutImported keyed by its CloudEvents\nid. Updates the governance charter (section 8.3), the sequence diagram''s\nerror path (section 6), the eventstorming H5 row, the domain-events note,\nthe consumer guide, the ADR index and the sidebar.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxYbwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIUUQAKYZGNgvdD8B1giwlNkpMjHU\nuwd1OcWF8td/R7n2FvNrIdb1RWWY8s/8FO6Mipftm9w+OqyuaT