"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/5591190cc34d4135a7a565aa37f5c5bea1388b37","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDU1OTExOTBjYzM0ZDQxMzVhN2E1NjVhYTM3ZjVjNWJlYTEzODhiMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/9a17d274b717e56a89c4906067d61c88a50ede0e","sha":"9a17d274b717e56a89c4906067d61c88a50ede0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/9a17d274b717e56a89c4906067d61c88a50ede0e"}],"sha":"5591190cc34d4135a7a565aa37f5c5bea1388b37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/5591190cc34d4135a7a565aa37f5c5bea1388b37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/9a17d274b717e56a89c4906067d61c88a50ede0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:40:35Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:40:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#151)\n\n* fix(mcp): estimate_travel_distance description matches cross-zone behaviour\n\nThe tool description claimed cross-zone requests are always refused, but\nEstimateTravelDistance returns a flagged straight-line estimate when both\nslots have recorded position geometry (ADR-0017) and refuses otherwise.\nUpdate the description, the eval feature wording and the governance\ncharter note, and pin the description with an eval test.\n\n* docs(kafka): correct publisher downstream list; asyncapi contact -> IQVO\n\npublisher.go''s package doc named workforce-management (no consumer; Separate\nWays in the context map) as a Conformist and omitted warehouse-planning, which\nconsumes LocationSlotRegistered/Decommissioned. Correct the list.\n\napis/asyncapi.yaml info.contact.url pointed at the old claudioed org; use\nIQVO.\n\n* fix(kafka): key geometry, structure and cross-aisle events by aggregate id\n\nLocationGeometryUpdated, AisleGeometryUpdated, FixedStructureRegistered and\nCrossAisleRegistered fell through aggregateKey to the event-type string, so\nwith the Hash balancer every occurrence of a type shared one partition (skew,\nand no ordering against the aggregate''s registration events). Key them by\ntheir aggregate identity (locationCode / aisleId / structureId / composite\ncross-aisle id), equal to their CloudEvents subject.\n\nFacilityLayoutImported is a batch outcome with no aggregate (its payload has\nno site/zone): key it by its CloudEvents id so batches spread over partitions\nand an outbox redelivery stays on the same partition. Its subject is unchanged.\n\nConsumers checked first (inventory-storage facilitycache, warehouse-planning\nstorage-capacity consumer, own analytics consumer, e2e-tests): none reads the\nfour geometry types or depends on import ordering. Wire format, type, subject,\ndataschema and topics are unchanged.\n\nProof: golden key assertions + a keys-are-not-event-type unit test (red on the\nold code), and a testcontainers Kafka test on an 8-partition topic (red on the\nold code: all geometry events on one partition). ADR-0032 records the decision;\nasyncapi.yaml, domain-events, consuming-this-service and eventstorming (H5\nresolved) updated.","tree":{"sha":"a68f6b94f1af02ba43a55171ef377fc7a663eec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/a68f6b94f1af02ba43a55171ef377fc7a663eec8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/9a17d274b717e56a89c4906067d61c88a50ede0e","verification":{"payload":"tree a68f6b94f1af02ba43a55171ef377fc7a663eec8\nparent d75cca4fbb7c822fbacd28a5dbc855b9160328af\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791297635 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791297635 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#151)\n\n* fix(mcp): estimate_travel_distance description matches cross-zone behaviour\n\nThe tool description claimed cross-zone requests are always refused, but\nEstimateTravelDistance returns a flagged straight-line estimate when both\nslots have recorded position geometry (ADR-0017) and refuses otherwise.\nUpdate the description, the eval feature wording and the governance\ncharter note, and pin the description with an eval test.\n\n* docs(kafka): correct publisher downstream list; asyncapi contact -> IQVO\n\npublisher.go''s package doc named workforce-management (no consumer; Separate\nWays in the context map) as a Conformist and omitted warehouse-planning, which\nconsumes LocationSlotRegistered/Decommissioned. Correct the list.\n\napis/asyncapi.yaml info.contact.url pointed at the old claudioed org; use\nIQVO.\n\n* fix(kafka): key geometry, structure and cross-aisle events by aggregate id\n\nLocationGeometryUpdated, AisleGeometryUpdated, FixedStructureRegistered and\nCrossAisleRegistered fell through aggregateKey to the event-type string, so\nwith the Hash balancer every occurrence of a type shared one partition (skew,\nand no ordering against the aggregate''s registration events). Key them by\ntheir aggregate identity (locationCode / aisleId / structureId / composite\ncross-aisle id), equal to their CloudEvents subject.\n\nFacilityLayoutImported is a batch outcome with no aggregate (its payload has\nno site/zone): key it by its CloudEvents id so batches spread over partitions\nand an outbox redelivery stays on the same partition. Its subject is unchanged.\n\nConsumers checked first (inventory-storage facilitycache, warehouse-planning\nstorage-capacity consumer, own analytics consumer, e2e-tests): none reads the\nfour geometry types or depends on import ordering. Wire format, type, subject,\ndataschema and topics are unchanged.\n\nProof: golden key assertions + a keys-are-not-event-type unit test (red on the\nold code), and a testcontainers Kafka test on an 8-partition topic (red on the\nold code: all geometry events on one partition). ADR-0032 records the decision;\nasyncapi.yaml, domain-events, consuming-this-service and eventstorming (H5\nresolved) updated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQhjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuWgQAFcHpy9jJwLaQZHfutnRkanO\nQDxSijkzLUJg+clk3qbo5J8tTyF2Uk73oaEvGQqxXwBAVXX1/OpCTgOLtQG1gat+\ndnYWYrBhofOLlh6iM68Yhin91YWb3H39/mlnhf85txx/xNMp5jTlre5G3F0o8LYR\nphoWxdQnB8bQVT/blzwncUS6OsZ995cbBoBh0XzV7JXFfxRZRrV08EdsKEZw3uoA\nZiKVnwCECC+rz3HK1b4iMkUr82fDd1NHFWVTmI07VAs4Z53n1ca9qCqBDNOE7iTR\nUPE6rpHc5mpjNJ03OHy4y9xkw+kAthMsIHIpI1a9+YB0HA+qJIuF6JQtZupDcpht\n4gJ6Cw/xP69n4g/0CkSu+0EgCYEaZVAvy/JXZ7cXg5VGlD21RUsggnaDZJU+CV1M\ncQtveR04PTrDW/67+M1hvgKbLt3sOHwoh5u1DnOm6yOm/L/uYVaELqQAwt3QUpuY\nViGCPE5fTwicgPt07JYJ3cQzSHKuVofAVfqW39bzVXPu/fQr6rf5sFvzZB1eoCLD\ngFzFxf0Xj+o+hdZzkk6oIfmMqjIjKr