/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/b1c5d2dd0463e298acc4be0623ed771ce8df55d0","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKGIxYzVkMmRkMDQ2M2UyOThhY2M0YmUwNjIzZWQ3NzFjZThkZjU1ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/f3b732a854f74a047a8a9e5ca203035c8b5f4652","sha":"f3b732a854f74a047a8a9e5ca203035c8b5f4652","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/f3b732a854f74a047a8a9e5ca203035c8b5f4652"}],"sha":"b1c5d2dd0463e298acc4be0623ed771ce8df55d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/b1c5d2dd0463e298acc4be0623ed771ce8df55d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/f3b732a854f74a047a8a9e5ca203035c8b5f4652/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:58:00Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:58:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#146)\n\n* docs: WIP part A refresh (agent interrupted by rate limit)\n\nUnreviewed partial refresh of existing pages, committed to preserve work.\nTo be verified and completed by the resume run.\n\n* docs: add ddd-crew pack index, core domain chart, canvases; refresh ADR index\n\nPart B: ddd-artifacts index, Core Domain Chart (Generic, bottom-right),\nBounded Context Canvas v5, Aggregate Design Canvas v1.1 for the eight\naggregate roots. Wire them under a DDD artifacts (ddd-crew) sidebar\ncategory.\n\nPart A: ADR index statuses for 0005/0010/0017/0025 match the ADR bodies;\noverview, subdomain classification and ADR index now list\nwarehouse-planning and warehouse-ops-agent as live consumers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add domain message flow, EventStorming, UML, ER and sequence diagrams\n\nPart B pages derived from internal/domain, the use cases, adapters and\nmigrations: Domain Message Flow (4 scenarios), design-level EventStorming\n(4 processes + legend, hotspots from real gaps), UML class diagrams (3 +\nhexagonal view), ER diagrams for the OLTP and analytics schemas, and UML\nsequence diagrams for every command use case plus the relay/projector and\nread models. Ubiquitous language gains a code-identifier column and a\nname-mismatch table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: refresh README, conventions, aggregates and agent rules against code\n\n- README: warehouse-planning listed as a live Kafka consumer; cross-zone\n  /distance behaviour; GET /zones/{zoneId}/cross-aisles row; drop the stale\n  geometry spec-vs-router note (spec now matches); outbox wording;\n  make check-fast; link the DDD artifact pack.\n- conventions: add the eight problem types the code emits but the\n  catalogue lacked (concurrent-modification, segment-*, missing-*,\n  invalid-layout-format, invalid-report-query, report-store-error).\n- aggregates/invariants: link the Aggregate Design Canvas; LocationSlot\n  version field; per-step unit of work inside a bulk-import row.\n- domain-vision: warehouse-planning consumer.\n- .claude/rules: 31 use cases, warehouse-planning consumer, structure/\n  and travel/ domain packages, cross-zone distance estimate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(claude): list warehouse-planning and warehouse-ops-agent as consumers\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"51f9aa9a92216e9dc6fcf00a8c1a713d654889bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/51f9aa9a92216e9dc6fcf00a8c1a713d654889bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/f3b732a854f74a047a8a9e5ca203035c8b5f4652","verification":{"payload":"tree 51f9aa9a92216e9dc6fcf00a8c1a713d654889bc\nparent f0ad6644a076d57b092e5e5f0076f5b8c8068943\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791269880 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791269880 -0300\n\ndocs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#146)\n\n* docs: WIP part A refresh (agent interrupted by rate limit)\n\nUnreviewed partial refresh of existing pages, committed to preserve work.\nTo be verified and completed by the resume run.\n\n* docs: add ddd-crew pack index, core domain chart, canvases; refresh ADR index\n\nPart B: ddd-artifacts index, Core Domain Chart (Generic, bottom-right),\nBounded Context Canvas v5, Aggregate Design Canvas v1.1 for the eight\naggregate roots. Wire them under a DDD artifacts (ddd-crew) sidebar\ncategory.\n\nPart A: ADR index statuses for 0005/0010/0017/0025 match the ADR bodies;\noverview, subdomain classification and ADR index now list\nwarehouse-planning and warehouse-ops-agent as live consumers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add domain message flow, EventStorming, UML, ER and sequence diagrams\n\nPart B pages derived from internal/domain, the use cases, adapters and\nmigrations: Domain Message Flow (4 scenarios), design-level EventStorming\n(4 processes + legend, hotspots from real gaps), UML class diagrams (3 +\nhexagonal view), ER diagrams for the OLTP and analytics schemas, and UML\nsequence diagrams for every command use case plus the relay/projector and\nread models. Ubiquitous language gains a code-identifier column and a\nname-mismatch table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: refresh README, conventions, aggregates and agent rules against code\n\n- README: warehouse-planning listed as a live Kafka consumer; cross-zone\n  /distance behaviour; GET /zones/{zoneId}/cross-aisles row; drop the stale\n  geometry spec-vs-router note (spec now matches); outbox wording;\n  make check-fast; link the DDD artifact pack.\n- conventions: add the eight problem types the code emits but the\n  catalogue lacked (concurrent-modification, segment-*, missing-*,\n  invalid-layout-format, invalid-report-query, report-store-error).\n- aggregates/invariants: link the Aggregate Design Canvas; LocationSlot\n  version field; per-step unit of work inside a bulk-import row.\n- domain-vision: warehouse-planning consumer.\n- .claude/rules: 31 use cases, warehouse-planning consumer, structure/\n  and travel/ domain packages, cross-zone distance estimate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(claude): list warehouse-planning and warehouse-ops-agent as consumers\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by