ttps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/31f33499495e110b001fe62300dcfd2af63e4c46","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDMxZjMzNDk5NDk1ZTExMGIwMDFmZTYyMzAwZGNmZDJhZjYzZTRjNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/1ed47a1e8d59acc31e7b165f16bc70c0d2fee672","sha":"1ed47a1e8d59acc31e7b165f16bc70c0d2fee672","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/1ed47a1e8d59acc31e7b165f16bc70c0d2fee672"}],"sha":"31f33499495e110b001fe62300dcfd2af63e4c46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/31f33499495e110b001fe62300dcfd2af63e4c46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/1ed47a1e8d59acc31e7b165f16bc70c0d2fee672/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T03:47:16Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T03:47:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ADR-conformance fixes: idempotency/CORS, DLQ durability, OCC, telemetry, ADR-0017 travel reads, trace-context, sweeper, ADRs 0025-0031 (#140)\n\n* fix(idempotency+dlq): allow Idempotency-Key in CORS preflight, send it from the console, durable DLQ writer\n\nItem 1 (ADR-0019/0011): CORS AllowedHeaders gains Idempotency-Key (a\npreflight that omits it makes the browser drop the key, so every console\ncreate form got 400 idempotency-key-required against a Postgres-backed\nAPI); web/src/api.ts mints a per-submit crypto.randomUUID key on every\nPOST; openapi.yaml documents the header + 400 idempotency-key-required /\n422 idempotency-key-reused on all 8 protected operations (required:false,\nno minLength, description says clients must always send a non-empty key).\n\nItem 2 (ADR-0020 durability): outbound/kafka exports NewDeadLetterWriter\n(RequireAll + Hash + 10ms, mirroring fulfillment-execution); the projector\ninjects it via the new WithDLQWriter option (inbound cannot import\noutbound per arch rules) and the inbound fallback writer re-states the\nsame pinned config; test pins the full fleet config.\n\n* feat(occ): version column on location_slots, 409 concurrent-modification, ADR-0025\n\nLocationSlot gains an inert version field (fresh=1, Rehydrate carries the\nloaded row''s version); migration 0007 adds location_slots.version NOT NULL\nDEFAULT 1; SlotRepo.Save is a version-guarded upsert returning\nports.ErrConcurrentModification on a stale write; errors.go maps it to 409\nconcurrent-modification. Closes the audit race where a concurrent\nSetLocationGeometry wrote status=Active back over a decommission.\n\nSites/zones/aisles deliberately not versioned (no genuine multi-writer);\nreasoning recorded in ADR-0025, referenced from ADR-0005 and ADR-0019.\nProven against testcontainers Postgres: stale-save rejected,\ncurrent-save increments, two-goroutine race yields exactly one winner.\n\n* feat(telemetry): otelchi + otelchimetric on the reports router and the projector admin server\n\nADR-0012 gap from the audit: both HTTP surfaces served without tracing or\nHTTP metrics even though the chart injects OTEL_* env into those pods.\nNewReportsRouter now mirrors the main router''s middleware order (RequestID,\notelchi, request-duration + active-requests metrics, RequestLogger,\nRecoverer); the projector''s admin mux is rebuilt on chi with the same\nmiddleware; both analytics composition roots call telemetry.Setup and log\nthrough telemetry.NewLogger under their own OTEL_SERVICE_NAME. Tests pin\nthe instrumented routers still serve and flip readiness (ADR-0020).\n\n* feat(roles): per-slot role in the zone grid + role monogram/stroke in the SVG floor plan\n\nADR-0016 gaps: gridPositionResponse (and openapi GridPosition) gains role,\nmatching what the site layout already exposed; the SVG floor plan draws a\ntwo-letter monogram (DK, WC, ST...) and a darker outline on every\nfunctional location, with the role also in the tooltip; Storage stays\nunmarked. Tests cover the JSON contract and the rendered SVG.\n\n* feat(travel): zone pitch API + cross-aisle read model + geometry-backed cross-zone estimate (ADR-0017)\n\n* docs: remove stale bearer-key residue (NOTES.txt, ADR-0007/0011/0014 statuses, index rows)\n\n* feat(telemetry+kafka): inject W3C trace context into Kafka headers, first-class OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL, fix stale outbox docs\n\n* docs(kafka): analytics channel in AsyncAPI, replace stale no-OTel comments\n\n* docs(adr-0004): record the errorCategories table shape\n\n* feat(housekeeping): idempotency-key TTL + published-outbox retention sweeper, ADR-0026\n\n* docs(drift): 0001/0013 amendments, GET /readyz in openapi, ADRs 0027-0031 for undocumented features\n\n* style: gofmt\n\n* style: satisfy funlen/gocognit (extract startBackground, startConsumer, setupTelemetry; split trace-header tests)\n\n* fix(cmd): treat typed-nil sweeper as no worker in startBackground\n\nIn-memory mode (no DATABASE_URL) returned a typed-nil *postgres.Sweeper\nfrom memoryAdapters; boxing it into startBackground''s interface parameter\nmade worker != nil, so Run was called on a nil receiver and SIGSEGV-\npanicked the process ~5ms after boot. The contract job boots the service\nexactly this way, so Schemathesis lost its server before the first probe.\n\nNormalize the typed nil before the nil check. Regression tests cover\nboth the typed-nil sweeper and the positive path.\n\n* docs(api): fix spectral errors in openapi.yaml and regenerate docs\n\n- Add the now-required bayPitchM/levelPitchM to all four Zone response\n  examples (registerZone 201, listZones 200 [both items], getZone 200,\n  getZoneGrid 200 example.zone).\n- Replace all 27 deep $refs into components.responses.<X>/content/\n  application~1problem+json/example with inline example objects; spectral\n  resolves them as media-type objects, not Examples (''content property\n  must exist'').\n- Remove the now-unused components.responses.IdempotencyKeyRequired\n  (oas3-unused-component); its 400 example lives inline at every use\n  site (the ADR 0019 semantics are preserved in the descriptions).\n- Regenerate docusaurus API docs (clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs).\n\n* test(contract): exclude registerZone from Schemathesis\n\nADR-0017 makes bayPitchM/levelPitchM both-or-neither with null meaning\n''not sent'' — a ternary cross-field rule OpenAPI 3.0.3 cannot encode, so\nSchemathesis generates schema-valid one-sided pitches the API must\ncorrectly reject with 422 invalid-pitch. Same documented-exclusion\nconvention as registerLocationType & friends; the constraint is tested\nby ''422s on a one-sided pitch'' in travel_read_test.go. Zone response\nconformance is still covered by listZones/getZone/getZoneGrid.\n\nFull local run: 2130/2130 passed, all four phases green.","tree":{"sha":"daa0ad000254bdf0fc79e1d9e52c2182e67943da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/daa0ad000254bdf0fc79e1d9e52c2182e67943da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/1ed47a1e8d59acc31e7b165f16bc70c0d2fee672","verification":{"payload":"tree daa0ad000254bdf0fc79e1d9e52c2182e67943da\nparent 9ee9118caffd7412bd2892868dfdff2879cc4609\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791172036 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791172036 -0300\n\nADR-conformance fixes: idempotency/CORS, DLQ durability, OCC, telemetry, ADR-0017 travel reads, trace-context, sweeper, ADRs 0025-0031 (#140)\n\n* fix(idempotency+dlq): allow Idempotency-Key in CORS preflight, send it from the console, durable DLQ writer\n\nItem 1 (ADR-0019/0011): CORS AllowedHeaders gains Idempotency-Key (a\npreflight that omits it makes the browser drop the key, so every console\ncreate form got 400 idempotency-key-required against a Postgres-backed\nAPI); web/src/api.ts mints a per-submit crypto.randomUUID key on every\nPOST; openapi.yaml documents the header + 400 idempotency-key-required /\n422 idempotency-key-reused on all 8 protected operations (required:false,\nno minLength, description says clients must always send a non-empty key).\n\nItem 2 (ADR-0020 durability): outbound/kafka exports NewDeadLetterWriter\n(RequireAll + Hash + 10ms, mirroring fulfillment-execution); the projector\ninjects it via the new WithDLQWriter option (inbound cannot import\noutbound per arch rules) and the inbound fallback writer re-states the\nsame pinned config; test pins the full fleet config.\n\n* feat(occ): version column on location_slots, 409 concurrent-modification, ADR-0025\n\nLocationSlot gains an inert version field (fresh=1, Rehydrate carries the\nloaded row''s version); migration 0007 adds location_slots.version NOT NULL\nDEFAULT 1; SlotRepo.Save is a version-guarded upsert returning\nports.ErrConcurrentModification on a stale write; errors.go maps it to 409\nconcurrent-modification. Closes the audit race where a concurrent\nSetLocationGeometry wrote status=Active back over a decommission.\n\nSites/zones/aisles deliberately not versioned (no genuine multi-writer);\nreasoning recorded in ADR-0025, referenced from ADR-0005 and ADR-0019.\nProven against testcontainers Postgres: stale-save rejected,\ncurrent-save increments, two-goroutine race yields exactly one winner.\n\n* feat(telemetry): otelchi + otelchimetric on the reports router and the projector admin server\n\nADR-0012 gap from the audit: both HTTP surfaces served without tracing or\nHTTP metrics even though the chart injects OTEL_* env into those pods.\nNewReportsRouter now mirrors the main router''s middleware order (RequestID,\notelchi, request-duration + active-requests metrics, RequestLogger,\nRecoverer); the projector''s admin mux is rebuilt on chi with the same\nmiddleware; both analytics composition roots call telemetry.Setup and log\nthrough telemetry.NewLogger under their own OTEL_SERVICE_NAME. Tests pin\nthe instrumented routers still serve and flip readiness (ADR-0020).\n\n* feat(roles): per-slot role in the zone grid + role monogram/stroke in the SVG floor plan\n\nADR-0016 gaps: gridPositionResponse (and openapi GridPosition) gains role,\nmatching what the site layout already exposed; the SVG floor plan draws a\ntwo-letter monogram (DK, WC, ST...) and a darker outline on every\nfunctional location, with the role also in the tooltip; Storage stays\nunmarked. Tests cover the JSON contract and the rendered SVG.\n\n* feat(travel): zone pitch API + cross-aisle read model + geometry-backed cross-zone estimate (ADR-0017)\n\n* docs: remove stale bearer-key residue (NOTES.txt, ADR-0007/0011/0014 statuses, index rows)\n\n* feat(telemetry+kafka): inject W3C trace context into Kafka headers, first-class OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL, fix stale outbox docs\n\n* docs(kafka): analytics channel in AsyncAPI, replace stale no-OTel comments\n\n* docs(adr-0004): record the errorCategories table shape\n\n* feat(housekeeping): idempotency-key TTL + published-outbox retention sweeper, ADR-0026\n\n* docs(drift): 0001/0013 amendments, GET /readyz in openapi, ADRs 0027-0031 for undocumented features\n\n* style: gofmt\n\n* style: satisfy funlen/gocognit (extract startBackground, startConsumer, setupTelemetry; split trace-header tests)\n\n* fix(cmd): treat typed-nil sweeper as no worker in startBackground\n\nIn-memory mode (no DATABASE_URL) returned a typed-nil *postgres.Sweeper\nfrom memoryAdapters; boxing it into startBackground''s interface parameter\nmade worker != nil, so Run was called on a nil receiver and SIGSEGV-\npanicked the process ~5ms after boot. The contract job boots the service\nexactly this way, so Schemathesis lost its server before the first probe.\n\nNormalize the typed nil before the nil check. Regression tests cover\nboth the typed-nil sweeper and the positive path.\n\n* docs(api): fix spectral errors in openapi.yaml and regenerate docs\n\n- Add the now-required bayPitchM/levelPitchM to all four Zone response\n  examples (registerZone 201, listZones 200 [both items], getZone 200,\n  getZoneGrid 200 example.zone).\n- Replace all 27 deep $refs into components.responses.<X>/content/\n  application~1problem+json/example with inline example objects; spectral\n  resolves them as media-type objects, not Examples (''content property\n  must exist'').\n- Remove the now-unused components.responses.IdempotencyKeyRequired\n  (oas3-unused-component); its 400 example lives inline at every use\n  site (the ADR 0019 semantics are preserved in the descriptions).\n- Regenerate docusaurus API docs (clean-api-docs + gen-api-docs).\n\n* test(contract): exclude registerZone from Schemathesis\n\nADR-0017 makes bayPitchM/levelPitchM both-or-neither with null meaning\n''not sent'' — a ternary cross-field rule OpenAPI 3.0.3 cannot encode, so\nSchemathesis generates schema-valid one-sided pitches the API must\ncorrectly reject with 422 invalid-pitch. Same documented-exclusion\nconvention as registerLocationType & friends; the constraint is tested\nby ''422s on a one-sided pitch'' in travel_read_test.go. Zone response\nconformance is still covered by listZones/getZone/getZoneGrid.\n\nFull local run: 2130/2130 passed, all four phases green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwx3ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAju0QAAEAosw+9ZrokbVyEvh4aqo5\nX02cMWeN6rCGqVofqBN98+2T/QdI4XgGtfm4kF0IkwUduMzNwZvq6vrmtaKTy2ik\nXQvUSq89a31p/J4Tv/xJwrjjEepoyy2nyE+lHyzhgX5MksUKJ8d3eBDh8u0WIbh8\nQUTvjvLJQIcdTHdJuY6+EUu1T98bxxksNUmycY7zs9vhLjGfoXYGb4RcQz0/wJ4Y\nN88x+peDyYmmHja85Af6LSh2ct2kdTotreuiqRjX+hfv5jcOeO40Me5VWadqtnJu\nnZDZIhBclQsxvWRp9JMOB00RYqkszeTrHVad03u6lOiJvmjGzUhdczypM0yWW85t\nHwBLbQGqYkEM1Kvvbgo0o4UokOF7os/ZjxblgBEbXKUr9lvQE8N9wbUxqDECjdzq\nUG0AXz9Rpw54oMfgbt4Rw1PxN2ZVpDm3Y6z6fv5kOiuEuUQaURLZ+/vTqsiQ4MPe\nTMCP0RoClwMJpdmv/4KBMscgVQi1MKA0O/HksGr806VKdeksnq3UuWUrFEIRql/v\nQoFmV1zvZg+va89hCEe+1+jVQHsQ9ZOZn+ordjXQwD168MFjPvmB7fChpMLhhimR\nrneVwjLsqP60T64PLaVRG9dCCUHVQAHx8wLnGp1LZzn5yFA2iDYpLP7mHQCIqLp4\nK42FcIW/tkBvqrgPQ6Sv\n=k3Gw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T03:47:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.co