rl":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/678adc1ff88a9b4ed6b7d0e1e97481936dd086dc","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDY3OGFkYzFmZjg4YTliNGVkNmI3ZDBlMWU5NzQ4MTkzNmRkMDg2ZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/77e9c4dc23dc05e3ed1cdde3e51ebcc2854de758","sha":"77e9c4dc23dc05e3ed1cdde3e51ebcc2854de758","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/77e9c4dc23dc05e3ed1cdde3e51ebcc2854de758"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/48e026b717ab762954c69f513ecb4ddd488bd7eb","sha":"48e026b717ab762954c69f513ecb4ddd488bd7eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/48e026b717ab762954c69f513ecb4ddd488bd7eb"}],"sha":"678adc1ff88a9b4ed6b7d0e1e97481936dd086dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/678adc1ff88a9b4ed6b7d0e1e97481936dd086dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/77e9c4dc23dc05e3ed1cdde3e51ebcc2854de758/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:12Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#115 port) (#115)\n\nFleet-wide bug fix (Phase 4 cleanup), ported from order-management''s\nreference implementation PR #115 / ADR-0029. golang-migrate''s postgres\ndriver takes a session-scoped pg_advisory_lock to serialize concurrent\nmigration runs at boot, but DATABASE_URL (warehouse-infra PR #43,\nPgBouncer rollout) points facility-layout at PgBouncer in\ntransaction-pooling mode, which does not preserve session state across\nstatements. Two or more facility-layout replicas (cmd/facility or\ncmd/mcp) starting concurrently — an HPA scale-out (ADR-0022''s api HPA),\nor an ordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1 — would crash-loop with\n`pq: unnamed prepared statement does not exist` for ~1-2 minutes until\none wins the advisory-lock race.\n\ncmd/facility/main.go (publisherConfigFromEnv/dialPostgres) and\ncmd/mcp/main.go (buildAdapters) now read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nenv var for the migration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when\nunset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\ndatabaseURL unchanged — every request this service serves keeps going\nthrough PgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local dev, CI\nintegration tests, and any environment that doesn''t provision the split\nworking byte-identically to before this change.\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL as a\nnew secret key alongside DATABASE_URL for all 9 OLTP services,\nincluding facility-layout — no further warehouse-infra work needed.\n\nAdds:\n- cmd/facility/main_test.go: TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback,\n  TestPublisherConfigFromEnv_ThreadsMigrationsDatabaseURL,\n  TestDialPostgres_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations.\n- cmd/mcp/migrations_test.go: the same fallback + wiring proofs for\n  cmd/mcp''s buildAdapters.\n- ADR-0023: mirrors order-management''s ADR-0029, cross-references\n  warehouse-infra PR #43 (PgBouncer rollout) and PR #44 (secret\n  provisioning).\n- charts/facility-layout: a new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey\n  value (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders a\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var, sourced from the same existingSecret,\n  in both the api and mcp Deployments (optional: true on the\n  secretKeyRef so a secret that predates this key still starts the pod).\n\nhelm lint and helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL both\nverified locally.\n\nmake check, make check-all (30/30 BDD scenarios, arch-test, coverage\ngate) and make integration (real Postgres via docker) all pass.","tree":{"sha":"64f2d0b8a3143fc9cc5087198675d3d8d222ed42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/64f2d0b8a3143fc9cc5087198675d3d8d222ed42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/77e9c4dc23dc05e3ed1cdde3e51ebcc2854de758","verification":{"payload":"tree 64f2d0b8a3143fc9cc5087198675d3d8d222ed42\nparent 954c1c7ecf7331ca59e162f962023a96ca52237b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790601732 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790601732 -0300\n\nfix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#115 port) (#115)\n\nFleet-wide bug fix (Phase 4 cleanup), ported from order-management''s\nreference implementation PR #115 / ADR-0029. golang-migrate''s postgres\ndriver takes a session-scoped pg_advisory_lock to serialize concurrent\nmigration runs at boot, but DATABASE_URL (warehouse-infra PR #43,\nPgBouncer rollout) points facility-layout at PgBouncer in\ntransaction-pooling mode, which does not preserve session state across\nstatements. Two or more facility-layout replicas (cmd/facility or\ncmd/mcp) starting concurrently — an HPA scale-out (ADR-0022''s api HPA),\nor an ordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1 — would crash-loop with\n`pq: unnamed prepared statement does not exist` for ~1-2 minutes until\none wins the advisory-lock race.\n\ncmd/facility/main.go (publisherConfigFromEnv/dialPostgres) and\ncmd/mcp/main.go (buildAdapters) now read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nenv var for the migration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when\nunset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\ndatabaseURL unchanged — every request this service serves keeps going\nthrough PgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local dev, CI\nintegration tests, and any environment that doesn''t provision the split\nworking byte-identically to before this change.\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL as a\nnew secret key alongside DATABASE_URL for all 9 OLTP services,\nincluding facility-layout — no further warehouse-infra work needed.\n\nAdds:\n- cmd/facility/main_test.go: TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback,\n  TestPublisherConfigFromEnv_ThreadsMigrationsDatabaseURL,\n  TestDialPostgres_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations.\n- cmd/mcp/migrations_test.go: the same fallback + wiring proofs for\n  cmd/mcp''s buildAdapters.\n- ADR-0023: mirrors order-management''s ADR-0029, cross-references\n  warehouse-infra PR #43 (PgBouncer rollout) and PR #44 (secret\n  provisioning).\n- charts/facility-layout: a new database.migrationsExistingSecretKey\n  value (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders a\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var, sourced from the same existingSecret,\n  in both the api and mcp Deployments (optional: true on the\n  secretKeyRef so a secret that predates this key still starts the pod).\n\nhelm lint and helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL both\nverified locally.\n\nmake check, make check-all (30/30 BDD scenarios, arch-test, coverage\ngate) and make integration (real Postgres via docker) all pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumoECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEo0QAHEH6n+EIhDzBI8IBKu2iIqY\nL9pVtIXpUnLWYV1rCFaP0123oFvg8heTaiLTm/DMKpU/XE4TRA0BhBJ/SdIR8G4B\nfuqIqk6GUbAltDZTK2O1DnZk8gsJ6QDEtrheyvNPcIFe3iWB9l0rD6Xfb22eAD6v\nvrH/R9n8UnNhj6Dttevsuq+KYjJXWyKiDt9zOjfaX/uv/0IGbP3/kll8oE5C77ZE\nwqF4ry326eSHbPr03oYm0xUqrPHU5Dr3svjcTy+VaTuCEsi4bdy7nWztoEOEzSAr\nMqoHOscnVidXFw9Dm2LnZcjmbnU9j6AD0nTOKaIIjM7YarpfSzmj1Lr/E+Z7cBBM\n6mOg0d5+GghknuEkimk0Dek0Ny080IzEGJIa6dwtHVbEU8gXVC+rIb8CaMZJBuEh\n+XMe4l6HOaT3mF3jjfsZrllXlDCofSHx8PwqfSllxINd5HxGjB2mJWDlPvQ5zuOu\nIQ+lCAGQUMGGgRgfhXZHtue4MYVPH24iKiJoAg3GTjXJbjFHqG2DJF3RUl4zU7P0\n4cPVazbw/dNsUm3Ub7uyE3n0MNjlR5AI4IrTjMFaH6XHArUPHoZtvFoTJG++usrb\nWY/9dInZFrA+NdTgv/UYYFyigvmcH/Eeda0t1NfqOIDP57JfnVIwDh6OMpnC6g57\nC+oE07j1RTYDSfZE32Cp\n=IyWY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T13:22:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/recei