ther_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/3876065eec9e11f3b5f7bd550a4fbf4c9369770c","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDM4NzYwNjVlZWM5ZTExZjNiNWY3YmQ1NTBhNGZiZjRjOTM2OTc3MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b","sha":"70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b"}],"sha":"3876065eec9e11f3b5f7bd550a4fbf4c9369770c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/3876065eec9e11f3b5f7bd550a4fbf4c9369770c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:04Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0022) (#112)\n\nPhase 3 (scalability) for facility-layout, ported from order-management\nPR #110 / ADR 0026, the fleet''s reference implementation for this phase.\n\nHorizontalPodAutoscaler (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed\nworkload, every block default-disabled via values.yaml so this PR\nchanges nothing on merge:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. cmd/facility has no inbound Kafka\n  consumer at all (outbound-publisher-only Open Host Service), so it is\n  unconditionally safe to run N independent copies of.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU, capped below api''s\n  ceiling. Its Kafka consumer group (\"facility-analytics\") is stable\n  and shared, and every projection write is idempotent on event_id, so\n  N replicas share partitions safely via normal rebalancing.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Stateless read-only REST\n  reader over its own read-only pgxpool, same treatment as api.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving.\n- mcp: deliberately excluded, not just disabled. Its StreamableHTTPHandler\n  keeps per-process in-memory session state keyed by Mcp-Session-Id, and\n  mcp-service.yaml has no session affinity, so a second replica could\n  receive a mid-session request its own process never created.\n\nEvery Deployment template guards its spec.replicas with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so an enabled HPA is the\nsole owner of .spec.replicas -- no replicas-vs-HPA fight on reconcile.\nVerified with helm template with autoscaling on and off (see ADR 0022).\n\npgxpool tuning, both MaxConns and statement_timeout via AfterConnect:\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool, cmd/facility + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10,\n  statement_timeout=5s. This DSN is already re-pointed at PgBouncer in\n  transaction-pooling mode (warehouse-infra PR #43, merged) so this\n  bounds each process''s demand on PgBouncer''s client pool, not a direct\n  Postgres slot.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/facility-projector):\n  MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=10s. Direct to Postgres per PR #43''s\n  documented reasoning (low QPS, single consumer connection).\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool, cmd/facility-reports):\n  ReportsMaxConns=5, ReportsStatementTimeout=15s. Direct to Postgres.\n\nBoth pools now expose a *WithLimits constructor so a test can drive a\nmuch shorter timeout without waiting out the production value.\n\nAdded internal/adapters/outbound/postgres/pool_limits_integration_test.go\n(testcontainers, real postgres:16-alpine, -tags=integration):\nTestNewPool_AppliesStatementTimeoutToNewConnections proves a pg_sleep(2)\nis actually cancelled by Postgres (SQLSTATE 57014) at a 200ms configured\ntimeout, and that the pool survives the cancellation.\nTestNewPool_AppliesMaxConns proves MaxConns=2 is a real enforced\nceiling: a third Acquire blocks to context.DeadlineExceeded.\n\nAdded ADR 0022 (docs/docs/adr/0022-horizontal-autoscaling-and-pgxpool-tuning.md)\nreferencing order-management PR #110 / ADR 0026 and warehouse-infra PR #43,\nwith facility-layout''s own connection-budget accounting (smaller\ndirect-Postgres footprint than order-management''s since PgBouncer\nalready fronts this service''s OLTP DSN).\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt, make check,\nmake arch-test, make coverage (98.5%, gate 90%), go test -tags=integration\n./... -race -count=1 (all green, including the two new pool_limits\ntests against a real testcontainers Postgres), helm lint, helm template\nwith autoscaling.*.enabled=true and =false (0 HPAs / static replicas by\ndefault, 4 HPAs / no replicas field on those 4 Deployments when enabled,\nmcp always keeps its static replicas).","tree":{"sha":"75f81b94ed7395adedd9dcf6c585229306cc556e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/75f81b94ed7395adedd9dcf6c585229306cc556e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b","verification":{"payload":"tree 75f81b94ed7395adedd9dcf6c585229306cc556e\nparent 7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790567944 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790567944 -0300\n\nfeat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0022) (#112)\n\nPhase 3 (scalability) for facility-layout, ported from order-management\nPR #110 / ADR 0026, the fleet''s reference implementation for this phase.\n\nHorizontalPodAutoscaler (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed\nworkload, every block default-disabled via values.yaml so this PR\nchanges nothing on merge:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. cmd/facility has no inbound Kafka\n  consumer at all (outbound-publisher-only Open Host Service), so it is\n  unconditionally safe to run N independent copies of.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / 70% CPU, capped below api''s\n  ceiling. Its Kafka consumer group (\"facility-analytics\") is stable\n  and shared, and every projection write is idempotent on event_id, so\n  N replicas share partitions safely via normal rebalancing.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Stateless read-only REST\n  reader over its own read-only pgxpool, same treatment as api.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving.\n- mcp: deliberately excluded, not just disabled. Its StreamableHTTPHandler\n  keeps per-process in-memory session state keyed by Mcp-Session-Id, and\n  mcp-service.yaml has no session affinity, so a second replica could\n  receive a mid-session request its own process never created.\n\nEvery Deployment template guards its spec.replicas with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so an enabled HPA is the\nsole owner of .spec.replicas -- no replicas-vs-HPA fight on reconcile.\nVerified with helm template with autoscaling on and off (see ADR 0022).\n\npgxpool tuning, both MaxConns and statement_timeout via AfterConnect:\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool, cmd/facility + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10,\n  statement_timeout=5s. This DSN is already re-pointed at PgBouncer in\n  transaction-pooling mode (warehouse-infra PR #43, merged) so this\n  bounds each process''s demand on PgBouncer''s client pool, not a direct\n  Postgres slot.\n- Analytics writer (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/facility-projector):\n  MaxConns=5, statement_timeout=10s. Direct to Postgres per PR #43''s\n  documented reasoning (low QPS, single consumer connection).\n- Analytics reader (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool, cmd/facility-reports):\n  ReportsMaxConns=5, ReportsStatementTimeout=15s. Direct to Postgres.\n\nBoth pools now expose a *WithLimits constructor so a test can drive a\nmuch shorter timeout without waiting out the production value.\n\nAdded internal/adapters/outbound/postgres/pool_limits_integration_test.go\n(testcontainers, real postgres:16-alpine, -tags=integration):\nTestNewPool_AppliesStatementTimeoutToNewConnections proves a pg_sleep(2)\nis actually cancelled by Postgres (SQLSTATE 57014) at a 200ms configured\ntimeout, and that the pool survives the cancellation.\nTestNewPool_AppliesMaxConns proves MaxConns=2 is a real enforced\nceiling: a third Acquire blocks to context.DeadlineExceeded.\n\nAdded ADR 0022 (docs/docs/adr/0022-horizontal-autoscaling-and-pgxpool-tuning.md)\nreferencing order-management PR #110 / ADR 0026 and warehouse-infra PR #43,\nwith facility-layout''s own connection-budget accounting (smaller\ndirect-Postgres footprint than order-management''s since PgBouncer\nalready fronts this service''s OLTP DSN).\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt, make check,\nmake arch-test, make coverage (98.5%, gate 90%), go test -tags=integration\n./... -race -count=1 (all green, including the two new pool_limits\ntests against a real testcontainers Postgres), helm lint, helm template\nwith autoscaling.*.enabled=true and =false (0 HPAs / static replicas by\ndefault, 4 HPAs / no replicas field on those 4 Deployments when enabled,\nmcp always keeps its static replicas).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueYICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU84QAC/NowSYv1UzrObM4UT5MJlQ\ndAaMDGJM34sHvGJKOLSyTaytV/g/WX7nviiYDkGI5j9O1hz5fwH4HWBbkIN0bLvs\n0mi2Sp+mHqClYQzfmndtdQZuOw2pONRbAYPbQalg8q/nI4AxBvHFudBGmE6kAALe\n9nFuLrzIfnXhr29IVrUq3t5lSGA8IBDciSIYVvx9vcdF+zMHtYBiX5lcJ1O+neX5\nMwkOqNwTr/kpRz2eirSmPfifFyiMkNiE785hohZWfYmsSJuCfX+PCNLAeE8iyfU1\nwFYriEtYDjMJbH/hn5RzweYmu+00HjyhlxPtzCPNh+BtXr1WBY5rEnv4PwIOAHji\nnOqQOFRUgYAAdzPqxMREpf6ceztsHQZBMsPiMb+faeN7ft5rSGV9/p+TGPs7f0nK\nB0nGbVjIboCclvG5+FMQr7U+8gedQze4VSyRh8gghOBuB0OEP/u1ZrPX/hfmHOiI\n3HkyBJHa73EB5xB8AfFRkrRXvwGTC+DaIry4q2sqYqzNd95cMlJR3rPI1RGWazER\nmdUESaX5w6wc5pA8RObiItfqakB9dNxWPEOeqVlf/8C6XACCfmJDXXK+L46d5ITy\nmD+OeZACM5fHrnh9KNtv0QrSbTs0IljwcTpiSNEJ7jR8aPsJ+yB3n0xBPlMQTUhb\nguMmjU1B+ns6EMEMVcdu\n=Mulo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:59:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDcwYTkwYWRhMTViMjQxNjNiYWQzZTU4MGIwMzNmMDg1YzY1OTUxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf","sha":"7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf"}],"sha":"70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/70a90ada15b24163bad3e580b033f085c659515b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:51Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): switch writer Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0021) (#111)\n\nA fleet-wide code audit following order-management''s, inventory-storage''s,\nand workforce-management''s Kafka partition-key fixes (PRs #111, #102,\n#106, all merged into develop) found this repo carrying the same latent\nbug those three had just fixed: kafka-go''s LeastBytes balancer completely\nignores Message.Key when choosing a partition. LeastBytes.Balance picks\nwhichever partition currently has the least cumulative bytes written,\nreading len(msg.Key) + len(msg.Value) only to update that running total\n-- it never hashes or otherwise routes on the key''s content.\n\nThis repo''s own Message.Key logic was already correct (verified against\norigin/develop:internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher.go before\ntouching anything): every event Publisher, AnalyticsPublisher, and the\noutbox relay''s RelaySink forward already carries a non-nil, per-aggregate\nkey via aggregateKey. But all three of this package''s *kafkago.Writer\nliterals used Balancer: &kafkago.LeastBytes{}, so the correct key was\ncomputed and set, then silently discarded for partition-placement\npurposes by the writer itself. This was invisible while this service''s\ntopics ran at 1 partition; warehouse-infra PR #42''s Phase 3 scaleup took\nevery business topic, including both of this service''s, to 8 partitions,\nwhich can now let a consumer observe events for one aggregate out of\norder across partitions even though nothing on the publish side raced.\n\nFix:\n- Switched every kafkago.Writer''s Balancer in\n  internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/{publisher.go,analytics_publisher.go,\n  relay_sink.go} from &kafkago.LeastBytes{} to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a\n  over Message.Key). Message.Key/Encoded.Key construction is untouched --\n  it was already correct.\n- Added a real-Kafka Testcontainers integration test\n  (publisher_partition_integration_test.go,\n  TestPublisherKeysMessagesForSameAggregateOntoTheSamePartition) against\n  an 8-partition topic, proving all 3 events published for one aggregate\n  land on the same partition while a different aggregate''s event is free\n  to land elsewhere. Verified by temporarily reverting the test''s writer\n  to LeastBytes: it failed (1 of 3 on the right partition); it passes (3\n  of 3) with Hash. A fake-writer unit test alone would not have caught\n  this, since it only proves the key is set, not that the balancer routes\n  on it.\n- Adds ADR 0021 documenting the fix, referencing order-management PR\n  #111 / ADR 0027 (the reference fix for the identical bug) and the\n  original partition-scaleup audit, warehouse-infra PR #42.\n\nVerified: go build/vet, gofmt, make check, make arch-test,\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1, make coverage (98.5%,\ngate 90%).","tree":{"sha":"ec8ab224f4b1e1e33ab2983ec527ff814f812b88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/ec8ab224f4b1e1e33ab2983ec527ff814f812b88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf","verification":{"payload":"tree ec8ab224f4b1e1e33ab2983ec527ff814f812b88\nparent 14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790566491 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790566491 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): switch writer Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0021) (#111)\n\nA fleet-wide code audit following order-management''s, inventory-storage''s,\nand workforce-management''s Kafka partition-key fixes (PRs #111, #102,\n#106, all merged into develop) found this repo carrying the same latent\nbug those three had just fixed: kafka-go''s LeastBytes balancer completely\nignores Message.Key when choosing a partition. LeastBytes.Balance picks\nwhichever partition currently has the least cumulative bytes written,\nreading len(msg.Key) + len(msg.Value) only to update that running total\n-- it never hashes or otherwise routes on the key''s content.\n\nThis repo''s own Message.Key logic was already correct (verified against\norigin/develop:internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher.go before\ntouching anything): every event Publisher, AnalyticsPublisher, and the\noutbox relay''s RelaySink forward already carries a non-nil, per-aggregate\nkey via aggregateKey. But all three of this package''s *kafkago.Writer\nliterals used Balancer: &kafkago.LeastBytes{}, so the correct key was\ncomputed and set, then silently discarded for partition-placement\npurposes by the writer itself. This was invisible while this service''s\ntopics ran at 1 partition; warehouse-infra PR #42''s Phase 3 scaleup took\nevery business topic, including both of this service''s, to 8 partitions,\nwhich can now let a consumer observe events for one aggregate out of\norder across partitions even though nothing on the publish side raced.\n\nFix:\n- Switched every kafkago.Writer''s Balancer in\n  internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/{publisher.go,analytics_publisher.go,\n  relay_sink.go} from &kafkago.LeastBytes{} to &kafkago.Hash{} (FNV-1a\n  over Message.Key). Message.Key/Encoded.Key construction is untouched --\n  it was already correct.\n- Added a real-Kafka Testcontainers integration test\n  (publisher_partition_integration_test.go,\n  TestPublisherKeysMessagesForSameAggregateOntoTheSamePartition) against\n  an 8-partition topic, proving all 3 events published for one aggregate\n  land on the same partition while a different aggregate''s event is free\n  to land elsewhere. Verified by temporarily reverting the test''s writer\n  to LeastBytes: it failed (1 of 3 on the right partition); it passes (3\n  of 3) with Hash. A fake-writer unit test alone would not have caught\n  this, since it only proves the key is set, not that the balancer routes\n  on it.\n- Adds ADR 0021 documenting the fix, referencing order-management PR\n  #111 / ADR 0027 (the reference fix for the identical bug) and the\n  original partition-scaleup audit, warehouse-infra PR #42.\n\nVerified: go build/vet, gofmt, make check, make arch-test,\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1, make coverage (98.5%,\ngate 90%).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueBbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXTYQAIn6o4hZArJUb1RTkBntQYBb\nSeOTkg7tsKFJGfZiDutmqre0v3ujHzruX6RmGbbeJjbMhEjsraUzYDBAyoJHSN1e\ndBcdTd5PkU/yWIsY7lsSN0CdebRDq7Y1z7PnIS+4xvVDitk14FzjAYJ4xExr8wO5\nl2dd9a3Kkva4UWHTY8fIqu8s22/gap/u/Rkt1oNliZNpmYwk1rMxkJnfxAlUxTP7\n6XogysPSTUBKT1j9Nv4uJJnKCYd1zo6yPZfW0kh2JHge4h9uHB7GqVSM+iCbAFqa\nKINcWczoBFyN29IANvRfoss4ySlpylkCNSTgSDBSuejytjuB15TCSBqZOLTCqaJF\n/CHpgiuMqy9mxqUAdQexsO44SAZ+iGAK08IJSKR/n9SAAqjsXHkvbMbVPDGKYXKv\nauXRHudjQ+6/gaZziyv6imcEKN3HqIekk56P3qSdmirVbCxX3Li3iyDU6ACQmpj4\n6U9tiZFddaWYpS0VXCrWjSt1MP/fwNFHp2mEoJtK9kHRC5EmMx8Om/De+Ynr62fI\nC6aQA0P2pY7Jj3P6/6u/8ZvA1Vj1ee7dA4Sut5Z4l48Zg9dUa0z3idDzNgvK5873\n+awVUuN0L0PwJXjgqI+nrAE7KUNBbr0xILNDcdsjnKB9UC08+CK9AJae6EQiBGZJ\nppZKpoON/D1ETrnXZsLC\n=zaPr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:34:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDcyNjlmNmYyODkzZjAyNjEzZDJhZTJiODIzOTk1YWEyMmY2ZDFhZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7","sha":"14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7"}],"sha":"7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/7269f6f2893f02613d2ae2b823995aa22f6d1adf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:39:43Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:39:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(complexity): enforce gocyclo/gocognit/cyclop/funlen/nestif gate, refactor all violations (#110)\n\n* chore: ignore local tool-run artifacts (.schemathesis, tooling node_modules)\n\n* ci(complexity): enforce gocyclo/gocognit/cyclop/funlen/nestif gate, refactor all violations\n\nEnable the five complexity linters in .golangci.yml (gocyclo 15, gocognit 20,\ncyclop 15 / package-average 10, funlen 80 lines/50 statements, nestif 5;\n_test.go exempt from funlen/gocyclo, web/ exempt from all five) and add a\ndedicated `complexity` CI job (golangci-lint --enable-only + gocyclo report\nin the step summary, gated into docker-publish). Refactor every\npre-existing violation with zero behavior change: table-driven problem\ncatalogs, split wiring/relay/policy functions, named test helpers instead\nof t.Run closures. golangci-lint, go build/vet, go test ./... all green.\n\n* ci(complexity): gocyclo report needs filesystem paths (go list -f {{.Dir}}), dedup + web filter on output","tree":{"sha":"901fb6552acb14c3b1d10124ab2ebe6e2883b694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/901fb6552acb14c3b1d10124ab2ebe6e2883b694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 901fb6552acb14c3b1d10124ab2ebe6e2883b694\nparent 99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790559583 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 179055958