/api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDE0ZmM3MGYzOWEzMTExM2ZiY2RmODkwOGQ5NjJlNTQ3MGE1MzIyZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463","sha":"99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463"}],"sha":"14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/14fc70f39a31113fbcdf8908d962e5470a5322e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T23:00:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T23:00:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add Kafka consumer DLQ and graceful shutdown hardening (ADR-0020) (#109)\n\nPhase 2 fan-out (resilience) for facility-layout, copying the DLQ and\ngraceful-shutdown pieces of order-management''s PR #107 / ADR 0025 ONLY.\nNo circuit breaker is introduced: facility-layout has no synchronous\noutbound HTTP calls to sibling bounded contexts to wrap (Kafka-producer-\nonly plus its own REST API), confirmed from the actual code before\nwriting anything.\n\nDead-letter queue (analytics Kafka consumer):\n- AnalyticsConsumer.handleMessage retries HandleMessage in-process via\n  cenkalti/backoff/v4 (jittered, 100ms-2s, max 3 attempts). Once\n  exhausted, the raw message plus x-dlq-* error-context headers is\n  published to <source-topic>.dlq and the offset is committed anyway,\n  so one poison message can never block its partition.\n- Fixed a pre-existing idempotency-ordering bug found while adding the\n  retry: HandleMessage claimed the event id (MarkProcessed) BEFORE\n  applying the projection. Combined with the new retry, that silently\n  defeated the DLQ entirely -- a failed Apply on attempt 1 left the\n  event already claimed, so attempt 2 returned nil without retrying,\n  and the poison message would never actually reach the DLQ. Fixed by\n  adding a read-only ProcessedEvents.IsProcessed pre-check and moving\n  MarkProcessed to run only after Apply* succeeds. Caught by running\n  the new integration test against a real testcontainers Kafka broker\n  and observing the poison message being silently acknowledged instead\n  of dead-lettered before the fix.\n- Proven end to end in analytics_dlq_integration_test.go against a\n  real testcontainers Kafka: poison message lands on .dlq after 3\n  attempts with headers intact; a well-formed message on the same\n  topic is still processed without delay.\n\nGraceful shutdown (all three binaries: cmd/facility, cmd/facility-\nprojector, cmd/facility-reports):\n1. Flip readiness to not-ready first -- new GET /readyz (backed by\n   inboundhttp.Readiness, atomic/thread-safe), distinct from the\n   existing GET /healthz liveness endpoint, which is never flipped.\n2. Drain in-flight HTTP/admin requests, bounded by a shutdown deadline.\n3. Stop the outbox relay (cmd/facility) / analytics consumer loop\n   (cmd/facility-projector) cleanly: cancel context, wait bounded for\n   the goroutine to actually finish (including its offset commit or\n   DLQ publish).\n4. Close the Kafka producer/consumer, then the pgx pool LAST (deferred\n   near the top of run(), so LIFO order runs closePool after every\n   consumer/relay has stopped touching it).\n\ncharts/facility-layout: readinessProbe now points at /readyz (was\n/healthz) on all three deployments; livenessProbe/startupProbe stay on\n/healthz. Added terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30 (previously unset).\n\ngo.mod: cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted from indirect to direct (already\npinned at v4.3.0, matching order-management).\n\nVerification: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\nmake check (0 lint issues), make arch-test (all hexagonal fitness\ntests pass, including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers), go\ntest -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (including a real\ntestcontainers Kafka broker), make coverage (98.5%, gate 90%), helm\nlint + helm template dry-run on all three deployment templates.\n\nADR: docs/docs/adr/0020-resilience-kafka-dlq-graceful-shutdown.md","tree":{"sha":"c5e4e81c7a28736fe5341e20613edab5a16aac45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/c5e4e81c7a28736fe5341e20613edab5a16aac45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463","verification":{"payload":"tree c5e4e81c7a28736fe5341e20613edab5a16aac45\nparent 1e21d9220f1ca909f52f30598468159b3eadc9cf\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790550031 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790550031 -0300\n\nAdd Kafka consumer DLQ and graceful shutdown hardening (ADR-0020) (#109)\n\nPhase 2 fan-out (resilience) for facility-layout, copying the DLQ and\ngraceful-shutdown pieces of order-management''s PR #107 / ADR 0025 ONLY.\nNo circuit breaker is introduced: facility-layout has no synchronous\noutbound HTTP calls to sibling bounded contexts to wrap (Kafka-producer-\nonly plus its own REST API), confirmed from the actual code before\nwriting anything.\n\nDead-letter queue (analytics Kafka consumer):\n- AnalyticsConsumer.handleMessage retries HandleMessage in-process via\n  cenkalti/backoff/v4 (jittered, 100ms-2s, max 3 attempts). Once\n  exhausted, the raw message plus x-dlq-* error-context headers is\n  published to <source-topic>.dlq and the offset is committed anyway,\n  so one poison message can never block its partition.\n- Fixed a pre-existing idempotency-ordering bug found while adding the\n  retry: HandleMessage claimed the event id (MarkProcessed) BEFORE\n  applying the projection. Combined with the new retry, that silently\n  defeated the DLQ entirely -- a failed Apply on attempt 1 left the\n  event already claimed, so attempt 2 returned nil without retrying,\n  and the poison message would never actually reach the DLQ. Fixed by\n  adding a read-only ProcessedEvents.IsProcessed pre-check and moving\n  MarkProcessed to run only after Apply* succeeds. Caught by running\n  the new integration test against a real testcontainers Kafka broker\n  and observing the poison message being silently acknowledged instead\n  of dead-lettered before the fix.\n- Proven end to end in analytics_dlq_integration_test.go against a\n  real testcontainers Kafka: poison message lands on .dlq after 3\n  attempts with headers intact; a well-formed message on the same\n  topic is still processed without delay.\n\nGraceful shutdown (all three binaries: cmd/facility, cmd/facility-\nprojector, cmd/facility-reports):\n1. Flip readiness to not-ready first -- new GET /readyz (backed by\n   inboundhttp.Readiness, atomic/thread-safe), distinct from the\n   existing GET /healthz liveness endpoint, which is never flipped.\n2. Drain in-flight HTTP/admin requests, bounded by a shutdown deadline.\n3. Stop the outbox relay (cmd/facility) / analytics consumer loop\n   (cmd/facility-projector) cleanly: cancel context, wait bounded for\n   the goroutine to actually finish (including its offset commit or\n   DLQ publish).\n4. Close the Kafka producer/consumer, then the pgx pool LAST (deferred\n   near the top of run(), so LIFO order runs closePool after every\n   consumer/relay has stopped touching it).\n\ncharts/facility-layout: readinessProbe now points at /readyz (was\n/healthz) on all three deployments; livenessProbe/startupProbe stay on\n/healthz. Added terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30 (previously unset).\n\ngo.mod: cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted from indirect to direct (already\npinned at v4.3.0, matching order-management).\n\nVerification: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt clean,\nmake check (0 lint issues), make arch-test (all hexagonal fitness\ntests pass, including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers), go\ntest -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (including a real\ntestcontainers Kafka broker), make coverage (98.5%, gate 90%), helm\nlint + helm template dry-run on all three deployment templates.\n\nADR: docs/docs/adr/0020-resilience-kafka-dlq-graceful-shutdown.md","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquaAPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9sIQAJI6RtcE7xmsZpaK+KYYH4zX\nETp1hdTtbynBDjHmKKnSmRTGFzApxsyNAn0MX0RwnOxqECh7ES8CbgRZu6X9ZOxP\nhwBWjfgjnWHxrdwecc+a4HfXSU47I/072xrjVDm3lj65qvwQoTQMzZsYuYSD4PsZ\nWblQ9uLC46GVGBwaTkF3mIf/dM+OEsnSk0LnZ+1W/Mxp7oc6NOakGqnClR0IL1Vg\nnP0UtZEwFEMK8mj6iB/uKZsSe4sShS1S8LJv6gU3avRq1uKisuuRDGPWN6QZrao1\nN2e+NDz4tixwBUn08ywTlExhYlgnAox8mazyanqWL+AafOsvSvUQBp25BhKsF+3w\n9pP9IwIIolxS2NlaLUNF+aZxklZpz14z8inZagTEYgwpbLxsSZnmHUCL7z/6t4Iw\nm0FNK730FsaZyWhbtvdodeV3Y/etrbu4KRQEwTxrsGWXCwz5/FBJF23+ozi37yKg\nMtCjekD8eiFR4DjYyPw++xIR4kd1lSLV/wJTzfkyVkGSi10fmoM1+Fb2fte97+DK\nnGCl6e8HQBc7meg9XMEJFun5S43uim5w6XUIXUBVy5hlCbLVKzGBqrPmBQCGzCJe\nNy4Hd6oipUVZ281y+UjHL5mYGpRnfmgyJkzOiBw1H2PBPo3mxgOPvWx8zDUJxrAF\n1i/H2ma3KskpVjNNsY25\n=hDPA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T23:00:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDk5YTE2MmJjMDZlMDQ4MGJmOGQ2NTI5MDc2MjUyNTNkNjU4YjQ0NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/1e21d9220f1ca909f52f30598468159b3eadc9cf","sha":"1e21d9220f1ca909f52f30598468159b3eadc9cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/1e21d9220f1ca909f52f30598468159b3eadc9cf"}],"sha":"99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/99a162bc06e0480bf8d652907625253d658b4463"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/1e21d9220f1ca909f52f30598468159b3eadc9cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:11:42Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:11:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(http): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for resource-creation POSTs (ADR-0019) (#108)\n\nAdds a route-scoped, transactional Idempotency-Key middleware to every\ntrue resource-creation POST this service exposes: /sites,\n/sites/{siteCode}/zones, /sites/{siteCode}/structures,\n/zones/{zoneId}/aisles, /zones/{zoneId}/cross-aisles, /location-types,\n/placement-rules, /locations. POST /locations/import (bulk import,\npartial-success semantics) and POST /locations/{locationCode}/decommission\n(acts on an existing resource) are deliberately excluded — see ADR-0019\nfor the reasoning.\n\nPorts order-management''s reference implementation (PR #105, ADR 0023):\n\n- internal/pgtx: the tx-in-context key/WithTx/TxFrom mechanism, extracted\n  out of the outbound postgres package''s unit_of_work.go into its own\n  dependency-free package so the inbound HTTP middleware can bind a\n  transaction into the same context slot UnitOfWork.Execute reads,\n  without either adapter package importing the other (the hexagonal\n  fitness tests forbid that in both directions). unit_of_work.go''s own\n  withTx/txFrom are now one-line aliases over pgtx.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go: RequireIdempotencyKey,\n  identical design to the reference — a required Idempotency-Key header,\n  request-body hashing, an INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING race decided\n  by Postgres'' own unique-index lock, an httptest.ResponseRecorder used to\n  capture the wrapped handler''s outcome before committing it (so a\n  committed idempotency_keys row can never have a NULL status_code), and\n  a panic path that rolls back and re-panics without ever caching the\n  panic''s outcome.\n- migrations/0006_idempotency_keys: the idempotency_keys table, same\n  schema as the reference.\n- server.go: a small idempotent(r chi.Router) helper wraps\n  r.With(RequireIdempotencyKey(pool)) on each of the eight protected\n  POST route registrations individually (never r.Use on the whole\n  router); a nil Server.IdempotencyPool (in-memory dev/test config) is a\n  no-op passthrough, mirroring this codebase''s existing convention for\n  every other optional Postgres-backed capability.\n- cmd/facility/main.go: threads the same pgxpool.Pool the Postgres\n  adapters use into Server.IdempotencyPool whenever Postgres is\n  configured (with or without Kafka/the outbox wired).\n\nConfirmed all eight protected use cases already wrap their aggregate\nSave + Events.Publish in atomically()/UnitOfWork from the transactional\noutbox rollout (ADR-0018, PR #106) — no use case needed new wiring to\njoin the middleware''s outer transaction.\n\nTesting: the full a-f scenario matrix (fresh key, replay, mismatched\nbody, missing header, real concurrency, cached business-error response)\nruns against real testcontainers Postgres through the real chi router\nfor POST /sites (simplest) and POST /locations (deepest — chain-of-\ncustody resolution, PlacementRule evaluation, metrics recording). The\nremaining six protected endpoints each get a smoke test (fresh key\ncreates, replay does not duplicate), proving the wiring is live on\nevery route. See ADR-0019''s \"Test coverage strategy\" section for the\nfull rationale.\n\nVerified locally: go build/vet (plain and -tags=integration), gofmt\nclean, make check (fmt-check vet build lint test), make arch-test (all\nten hexagonal fitness checks, including the pgtx-extraction-sensitive\nones), go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all new and\nexisting tests green), make coverage 98.5% (gate 90%).","tree":{"sha":"619fb4518140ab8577cf680536e4c268ba0f9417","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/619fb4518140ab8577cf680536e4c268ba0f9417"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/1e21d9220f1ca909f52f30598468159b3eadc9cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 619fb4518140ab8577cf680536e4c268ba0f9417\nparent 57ae916c4e1367a66b3a6cf08537ec913729b299\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790514702 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <no