 r.Use on the whole\n  router); a nil Server.IdempotencyPool (in-memory dev/test config) is a\n  no-op passthrough, mirroring this codebase''s existing convention for\n  every other optional Postgres-backed capability.\n- cmd/facility/main.go: threads the same pgxpool.Pool the Postgres\n  adapters use into Server.IdempotencyPool whenever Postgres is\n  configured (with or without Kafka/the outbox wired).\n\nConfirmed all eight protected use cases already wrap their aggregate\nSave + Events.Publish in atomically()/UnitOfWork from the transactional\noutbox rollout (ADR-0018, PR #106) — no use case needed new wiring to\njoin the middleware''s outer transaction.\n\nTesting: the full a-f scenario matrix (fresh key, replay, mismatched\nbody, missing header, real concurrency, cached business-error response)\nruns against real testcontainers Postgres through the real chi router\nfor POST /sites (simplest) and POST /locations (deepest — chain-of-\ncustody resolution, PlacementRule evaluation, metrics recording). The\nremaining six protected endpoints each get a smoke test (fresh key\ncreates, replay does not duplicate), proving the wiring is live on\nevery route. See ADR-0019''s \"Test coverage strategy\" section for the\nfull rationale.\n\nVerified locally: go build/vet (plain and -tags=integration), gofmt\nclean, make check (fmt-check vet build lint test), make arch-test (all\nten hexagonal fitness checks, including the pgtx-extraction-sensitive\nones), go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all new and\nexisting tests green), make coverage 98.5% (gate 90%).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRYOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANikQADteStwZzQo/QgkzVYt1zl3E\n1apNoubDh3qJ7nR9SfE546lsA+Dw0Mo1dgYEkeWZJGsysvQWWA7nMU8565SCCbFE\nv3zkmdmVbg8wO7Duc4byyRdlOcE8nI8ZxHStkgnL/Ef83ni6YRS95HREIWxfH/Q/\nk/0upuvqlOi74+AUFSiLU6KlIi3K2NjJ5RwAzH0CBIpuWh9PsSHlyFq0nIckhs4i\nLXXPd/PuysuvJ7xa18qMUsaIIg8br7xV2Jf2boYOxb0Hi+500P3IRUnbsGb/mdRQ\nj2r1G+GpHXE92d+3Kbt