ted evals-tests job for the MCP eval gate (#105)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRHpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArowQABxoZwLogZ41uEqi7t6hSoSW\nUTaTePEwaLGX9dg0CpBrSXuT6L60I0qnmyP/eOZjLJ5+IBksv/ruTw7aixeVwvHU\nOsUMZGOwF5iGwvrOlmNuOzSVhNQScor6UHn6EW9gX7Ju8TY7sXhHHPYmGSdOm1ZG\npzjiGKz9BQxlX7zV5ccDEGa7li2Kiu8eHbGWQdGfuZdBfAX2p5r+jjiKViS/m+B3\ny0xJwhRnKXtBjiocV3FKz2aVT+MbYfTMb0O01xTL+kWpRjYXFsXO+g5Xdcc0tNR/\npVi93hK6DfVeo8MuAXuYDcJDEE8VsqMpsQUytjwbZIOKkZGWiJtjka/7nHjEe6XR\nIu8ceLG+lEgjj5eSBtufp8QcBzUq4s6bFv0S08Kq9PbOja7XM7qJCKEhOcqooh/H\nH7+GVYTgdzxT8cesdJ4rKNS5UrwoRDFqQOPnJO/Nyz/Xmay39kvwFDvgSXJKR7xn\nnkENqGR4P4gVSZmrylPOweADvvRKRIMgYgoBRYsApiiBo9P/EfzhJAc+zE1qyNpf\nq/GrpnOrv2xcDpV1oKlIegM/RvKKznyasCsetGAsSzVYZAlkEksBC5FCmDxIAS3o\n5Qpp7pTZqsq40XTzM5h2KJbkkRGf8kbZpSAfDjOVIDorDntofHwawHm4mThp58XZ\nFEO7bfz1OjvC0tsMzkkX\n=jDG/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T12:54:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/57ae916c4e1367a66b3a6cf08537ec913729b299","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDU3YWU5MTZjNGUxMzY3YTY2YjNhNmNmMDg1MzdlYzkxMzcyOWIyOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/01fef3cf88866c9fa2df441e10451cf0a7979417","sha":"01fef3cf88866c9fa2df441e10451cf0a7979417","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/01fef3cf88866c9fa2df441e10451cf0a7979417"}],"sha":"57ae916c4e1367a66b3a6cf08537ec913729b299","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/57ae916c4e1367a66b3a6cf08537ec913729b299"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/01fef3cf88866c9fa2df441e10451cf0a7979417/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T01:21:20Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T01:21:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(outbox): transactional outbox + relay for atomic event publishing (ADR-0018) (#106)\n\nAggregate saves and their domain event publishes now commit atomically in\none Postgres transaction, closing the dual-write gap ADR-0009 reopened\nwhen it moved facility-layout from a never-drained outbox to direct Kafka\npublishing.\n\n- Add ports.UnitOfWork (Execute wraps a use case''s Save + Publish calls in\n  one transaction); every publishing use case takes an optional\n  UnitOfWork field and routes through a new atomically() helper that\n  falls back to running the wrapped function directly when nil, so\n  in-memory-adapter callers are unaffected.\n- Add postgres.UnitOfWork/querier/querierFrom/withTx: every postgres repo\n  now issues its SQL through the querier resolved from ctx, joining the\n  outer transaction when one is present.\n- Replace the dead postgres/event_publisher.go (the ADR-0009-era outbox\n  that nothing ever drained) with outbox_events (migration 0005),\n  postgres.OutboxPublisher, and postgres.OutboxRelay. One row is written\n  per (event x topic): OutboxPublisher enqueues both the integration and\n  analytics topic in the same transaction as the aggregate write, so the\n  two streams can never diverge.\n- Split Encode from Send in both kafka.Publisher and\n  kafka.AnalyticsPublisher via a shared kafka.Encoder interface, so\n  OutboxPublisher and the direct-publish path share one encoding\n  implementation. Add kafka.RelaySink, a topic-less writer that routes\n  each message off its own Encoded.Topic for the relay''s dual-topic drain.\n- Wire cmd/facility/main.go: with DATABASE_URL and EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka\n  both set, EventPublisher becomes the outbox and a relay goroutine runs\n  alongside the HTTP server sharing its shutdown signal\n  (OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL tunes the poll interval). Every other\n  DATABASE_URL/EVENT_PUBLISHER combination keeps ADR-0009/0010''s direct\n  fan-out unchanged. Composes cleanly with the recently-merged bootretry\n  boot-time dial retry (#100).\n- New outbox_integration_test.go (testcontainers-only Postgres, no\n  DATABASE_URL skip) covers: aggregate+outbox commit together, a\n  publish-time failure rolls back the aggregate save, the relay drains\n  in order and marks rows published, and a sink failure stops at the\n  failed row and is retried on the next pass without reordering.\n- docs/docs/adr/0018-transactional-outbox.md records the decision and its\n  relationship to ADR-0009''s reversal; README env var table and ADR\n  index/sidebar updated.\n\nTests: make check-all passes locally (fmt/vet/build/lint/unit test/\ncoverage/arch-test/bdd); full integration suite (go test -tags=integration\n./... -race) passes against a real Postgres via docker-compose, including\nthe new outbox_integration_test.go against testcontainers. Coverage over\ninternal/domain/... and internal/application/... unchanged at 98.5%\n(gate 90%).","tree":{"sha":"722d050edec09e388df2d6151f0356407fd335ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/722d050edec09e388df2d6151f0356407fd335ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/01fef3cf88866c9fa2df441e10451cf0a7979417","verification":{"payload":"tree 722d050edec09e388df2d6151f0356407fd335ab\nparent 6e645a3531e5eb21cee84d953025d61fa96b9482\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790472080 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790472080 -0300\n\nfeat(outbox): transactional outbox + relay for atomic event publishing (ADR-0018) (#106)\n\nAggregate saves and their domain event publishes now commit atomically in\none Postgres transaction, closing the dual-write gap ADR-0009 reopened\nwhen it moved facility-layout from a never-drained outbox to direct Kafka\npublishing.\n\n- Add ports.UnitOfWork (Execute wraps a use case''s Save + Publish calls in\n  one transaction); every publishing use case takes an optional\n  UnitOfWork field and routes through a new atomically() helper that\n  falls back to running the wrapped function directly when nil, so\n  in-memory-adapter callers are unaffected.\n- Add postgres.UnitOfWork/querier/querierFrom/withTx: every postgres repo\n  now issues its SQL through the querier resolved from ctx, joining the\n  outer transaction when one is present.\n- Replace the dead postgres/event_publisher.go (the ADR-0009-era outbox\n  that nothing ever drained) with outbox_events (migration 0005),\n  postgres.OutboxPublisher, and postgres.OutboxRelay. One row is written\n  per (event x topic): OutboxPublisher enqueues both the integration and\n  analytics topic in the same transaction as the aggregate write, so the\n  two streams can never diverge.\n- Split Encode from Send in both kafka.Publisher and\n  kafka.AnalyticsPublisher via a shared kafka.Encoder interface, so\n  OutboxPublisher and the direct-publish path share one encoding\n  implementation. Add kafka.RelaySink, a topic-less writer that routes\n  each message off its own Encoded.Topic for the relay''s dual-topic drain.\n- Wire cmd/facility/main.go: with DATABASE_URL and EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka\n  both set, EventPublisher becomes the outbox and a relay goroutine runs\n  alongside the HTTP server sharing its shutdown signal\n  (OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL tunes the poll interval). Every other\n  DATABASE_URL/EVENT_PUBLISHER combination keeps ADR-0009/0010''s direct\n  fan-out unchanged. Composes cleanly with the recently-merged bootretry\n  boot-time dial retry (#100).\n- New outbox_integration_test.go (testcontainers-only Postgres, no\n  DATABASE_URL skip) covers: aggregate+outbox commit together, a\n  publish-time failure rolls back the aggregate save, the relay drains\n  in order and marks rows published, and a sink failure stops at the\n  failed row and is retried on the next pass without reordering.\n- docs/docs/adr/0018-transactional-outbox.md records the decision and its\n  relationship to ADR-0009''s reversal; README env var table and ADR\n  index/sidebar updated.\n\nTests: make check-all passes locally (fmt/vet/build/lint/unit test/\ncoverage/arch-test/bdd); full integration suite (go test -tags=integration\n./... -race) passes against a real Postgres via docker-compose, including\nthe new outbox_integration_test.go against testcontainers. Coverage over\ninternal/domain/... and internal/application/... unchanged at 98.5%\n(gate 90%).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquG+QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAfAQACEw7X1RP+3bw1YM2r7oMeXm\nqidKgdKUeeptWggW297SOYzMZ3tj8vFJXteyJ3ctVaTHf4+e42AxDTJsqDzJq1hL\nRT7wq0NEPzsLI0Azlp5n2vGKaOqRxJzGDQ20nOkOkXKpIPOScpsYIxiFZ6IPnF3H\nO3/Hv6yQvyVnlgAThyfBvXUecGBHBfE+Jzlwe5Z/wMenFQMcd+LC1i46/BmV3YRG\nIiSGBXr5CvlHQpuMMox3bzNWRGbZXrYbGtoXCnijjYEU8T4eIRm1l6WTqHBMDog0\nC6HZKcuFjkvFm9WK7Ly7ATXnXgPts49a/g53y9LkGbqdj/LG+HjQ3pzVmeONxKNR\nEsw9HQLk0ZAq0bU29R9MBqqagBYGzIHo21zrU8JG0JuPmvbKuQVKgu7U5hA4bTg1\n3B7hxlhhSTaZPjfhCD0EiciJJQfnnwdcNEhA5iXkaHMeSXSSot/lbyew9cB2+CS/\nTArllQQmSP5diGZD5caoIm2qFlmtkzKAtcWX67FzVXwohU9Ar5myWXxD8J7zR3WH\nu3M70KmU964B7DIjlSFX0xYyNpSbQ6Er0WKJ8p5wJhSjaexsNIuLgHhoVvRDH2ez\n8lbH0CmXRmHIjeAlhb6NJ2oHTg8DU5x3lIVWIn4omGYUPdC2ZGy4PBflRvEbyNfo\n2jC2AopFN8yX8OsBo1W9\n=0jvE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T01:21:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"ht