ue,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T00:33:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/6e645a3531e5eb21cee84d953025d61fa96b9482","node_id":"C_kwDOUBAk6doAKDZlNjQ1YTM1MzFlNWViMjFjZWU4NGQ5NTMwMjVkNjFmYTk2Yjk0ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/facility-layout/commit/fad9e1dbb71a67fb4d9aaaababa743153b13a7bf","sha":"fad9e1dbb71a67fb4d9aaaababa743153b13a7bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/fad9e1dbb71a67fb4d9aaaababa743153b13a7bf"}],"sha":"6e645a3531e5eb21cee84d953025d61fa96b9482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/6e645a3531e5eb21cee84d953025d61fa96b9482"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/commits/fad9e1dbb71a67fb4d9aaaababa743153b13a7bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:23:57Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:23:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: retry first boot-time Postgres dial and add Helm startupProbe (#100)\n\nEvery injected pod''s FIRST outbound TCP dial (Postgres) in this cluster\nfails with `read: connection reset by peer` ~10s after the app starts\n(Istio 1.30 native sidecars; holdApplicationUntilProxyStarts is a no-op\nfor them). Every one of this repo''s four fail-fast binaries treated that\nas permanent and exited 1, so kubelet crash-loops every pod once on\nrollout.\n\n- Add internal/adapters/outbound/bootretry: a single reusable\n  Retry/RetryWithDelay pair (bootRetries=5, bootRetryDelay=1s,\n  exponential backoff, ~31s total) shared by every composition root\n  instead of reimplementing it four times. Mirrors the shipped, tested\n  reference in network-fulfillment''s cmd/netfulfil/main.go, including\n  its four test cases (survives first failure, no sleep on a healthy\n  start, gives up and reports the last real error, stops on context\n  cancellation) plus a fifth asserting the budget outlasts the ~10s\n  reset arithmetically.\n- Wire it into cmd/facility (RunMigrations + pool.Ping), cmd/mcp\n  (RunMigrations + pool.Ping), cmd/facility-projector (RunMigrations +\n  pool.Ping) and cmd/facility-reports (pool.Ping; it runs no\n  migrations). The retry does not weaken the fail-closed rule: once the\n  budget is exhausted every binary still refuses to boot and reports\n  the real underlying error.\n- charts/facility-layout: add a startupProbe (httpGet /healthz,\n  periodSeconds 2, failureThreshold 30 -> 60s of startup grace) to\n  values.yaml and wire it into every Deployment template that runs a\n  DB-backed binary (deployment.yaml, mcp-deployment.yaml,\n  projector-deployment.yaml, reports-deployment.yaml), mirroring\n  network-fulfillment''s chart. This suspends liveness/readiness checks\n  until /healthz answers, so a pod retrying its first dial is never\n  killed mid-retry.\n\nVerified: go build/vet/test -race, go build/vet -tags=integration,\nmake check (fmt-check vet build lint test), charts/facility-layout''s\nown render_test.sh and test_service_selectors.py.","tree":{"sha":"ce34cd0d5b8c55d9f4e96d5cefed6887f8350b78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/trees/ce34cd0d5b8c55d9f4e96d5cefed6887f8350b78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/facility-layout/git/commits/fad9e1dbb71a67fb4d9aaaababa743153b13a7bf","verification":{"payload":"tree ce34cd0d5b8c55d9f4e96d5cefed6887f8350b78\nparent 287784e5c0a4d8b276b8aa864d09d52e49e1b20e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790465037 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790465037 -0300\n\nfix: retry first boot-time Postgres dial and add Helm startupProbe (#100)\n\nEvery injected pod''s FIRST outbound TCP dial (Postgres) in this cluster\nfails with `read: connection reset by peer` ~10s after the app starts\n(Istio 1.30 native sidecars; holdApplicationUntilProxyStarts is a no-op\nfor them). Every one of this repo''s four fail-fast binaries treated that\nas permanent and exited 1, so kubelet crash-loops every pod once on\nrollout.\n\n- Add internal/adapters/outbound/bootretry: a single reusable\n  Retry/RetryWithDelay pair (bootRetries=5, bootRetryDelay=1s,\n  exponential backoff, ~31s total) shared by every composition root\n  instead of reimplementing it four times. Mirrors the shipped, tested\n  reference in network-fulfillment''s cmd/netfulfil/main.go, including\n  its four test cases (survives first failure, no sleep on a healthy\n  start, gives up and reports the last real error, stops on context\n  cancellation) plus a fifth asserting the budget outlasts the ~10s\n  reset arithmetically.\n- Wire it into cmd/facility (RunMigrations + pool.Ping), cmd/mcp\n  (RunMigrations + pool.Ping), cmd/facility-projector (RunMigrations +\n  pool.Ping) and cmd/facility-reports (pool.Ping; it runs no\n  migrations). The retry does not weaken the fail-closed rule: once the\n  budget is exhausted every binary still refuses to boot and reports\n  the real underlying error.\n- charts/facility-layout: add a startupProbe (httpGet /healthz,\n  periodSeconds 2, failureThreshold 30 -> 60s of startup grace) to\n  values.yaml and wire it into every Deployment template that runs a\n  DB-backed binary (deployment.yaml, mcp-deployment.yaml,\n  projector-deployment.yaml, reports-deployment.yaml), mirroring\n  network-fulfillment''s chart. This suspends liveness/readiness checks\n  until /healthz answers, so a pod retrying its first dial is never\n  killed mid-retry.\n\nVerified: go build/vet/test -race, go build/vet -tags=integration,\nmake check (fmt-check vet build lint test), charts/facility-layout''s\nown render_test.sh and test_service_selectors.py.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquFQNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdBgQAJEKZSZYFqTcNH1OaOhQk4Yd\nyxIca7ajfTDvyFO2w75PY3/5YKMs0nMYcY1MTOEs0QlX8jxa8KAVSi+hNSpCwBWi\nhvfHgFljYP0BikOA/kfEoW393D8WbsqE+/YcNtg9H9f0YJgGeojPowNDdUEKk+xe\nHFteEI3qveKHmSdULzO2HrC14CBSUpqi9w1OyzraGuJn7eSPH/HK4fmDEFryTGD5\nyYNHh4rkOF2j8KJ+tIaTehNdcn5vU65KdN7+rswwgjzy5ow