/users/vulko99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/58952db4ed763445e3d001ecdc59e24c3cf7b15e","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDU4OTUyZGI0ZWQ3NjM0NDVlM2QwMDFlY2RjNTllMjRjM2NmN2IxNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747","sha":"b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030","sha":"c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030"}],"sha":"58952db4ed763445e3d001ecdc59e24c3cf7b15e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/58952db4ed763445e3d001ecdc59e24c3cf7b15e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194582360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99","id":194582360,"login":"vulko99","node_id":"U_kgDOC5kXWA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:00:28Z","email":"vulkoshishkov87@gmail.com","name":"Veyra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:00:28Z","email":"vulkoshishkov87@gmail.com","name":"Veyra"},"message":"feat(amount): manual numeric input + slider, single source of truth (Part 1)\n\nAdd a combined numeric-input + slider to the amount step, always synchronised,\nkeeping the existing Veyra visual language. The stored value stays numeric\n(never the formatted string); display uses grouped thousands.\n\n- frontend/lib/amount.ts: single source of truth for EUR bounds (min/max/step/\n  default, overridable via NEXT_PUBLIC_AMOUNT_*), plus validateAmount/snapToStep/\n  formatting helpers mirrored by the backend.\n- Amount step: editable figure + slider + presets, all synced; inline\n  min/max/step validation blocks advancing; numeric inputMode for mobile.\n- Backend: settings.AMOUNT_MIN/MAX/STEP_EUR and independent serializer\n  validation (validate_requested_amount) so a value bypassing the UI is still\n  rejected with the same rules. Matching is unchanged — both inputs produce the\n  same numeric application amount.\n- Tests: backend amount-validation suite; updated two matching-exclusion tests\n  to use amounts valid at the funnel level but outside the product range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KffmA1kzYNwRxH6iUnodE2","tree":{"sha":"57f5ffcc1f08e002a807b0640776086730dd251b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/57f5ffcc1f08e002a807b0640776086730dd251b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747","verification":{"payload":"tree 57f5ffcc1f08e002a807b0640776086730dd251b\nparent 16e5088d5bb2f6e877f34a2e98339a31a50172e7\nauthor Veyra <vulkoshishkov87@gmail.com> 1788364828 +0000\ncommitter Veyra <vulkoshishkov87@gmail.com> 1788364828 +0000\n\nfeat(amount): manual numeric input + slider, single source of truth (Part 1)\n\nAdd a combined numeric-input + slider to the amount step, always synchronised,\nkeeping the existing Veyra visual language. The stored value stays numeric\n(never the formatted string); display uses grouped thousands.\n\n- frontend/lib/amount.ts: single source of truth for EUR bounds (min/max/step/\n  default, overridable via NEXT_PUBLIC_AMOUNT_*), plus validateAmount/snapToStep/\n  formatting helpers mirrored by the backend.\n- Amount step: editable figure + slider + presets, all synced; inline\n  min/max/step validation blocks advancing; numeric inputMode for mobile.\n- Backend: settings.AMOUNT_MIN/MAX/STEP_EUR and independent serializer\n  validation (validate_requested_amount) so a value bypassing the UI is still\n  rejected with the same rules. Matching is unchanged — both inputs produce the\n  same numeric application amount.\n- Tests: backend amount-validation suite; updated two matching-exclusion tests\n  to use amounts valid at the funnel level but outside the product range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KffmA1kzYNwRxH6iUnodE2\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHEhwrZ5\nZiRlT2LV2IdHi5TgC5IczAuPnrHcwPN061Tqwc+7349h170VPcB/Zem4WIBF6gbBkBmXapY8iENG\nMwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194582360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99","id":194582360,"login":"vulko99","node_id":"U_kgDOC5kXWA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vulko99","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKGI2NTYwYjNjMDNmZWM3Njg5MGVjNjEwZmU4MWFhMjc1OWVjM2M3NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/16e5088d5bb2f6e877f34a2e98339a31a50172e7","sha":"16e5088d5bb2f6e877f34a2e98339a31a50172e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/16e5088d5bb2f6e877f34a2e98339a31a50172e7"}],"sha":"b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/b6560b3c03fec76890ec610fe81aa2759ec3c747"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:37:02Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:37:02Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"chore(render): make the blueprint actually build\n\nrender.yaml predates the legal guard and was never retested against it. As it\nstood, a Render deploy would have failed at prebuild.\n\nIt sets NEXT_PUBLIC_PRELAUNCH=false to open the funnel for a partner demo, and\n4dd9e0d made an open funnel with no company EIK FATAL — refused in EVERY\nenvironment, not only where CONTEXT=production. The blueprint''s own comment\nstill claimed the guard ''does not catch it here, so on Render it warns and\nbuilds anyway'', which was true when written and is exactly the gap that commit\nclosed. Corrected, and REQUIRE_LEGAL_VALUES=false added, which is now required\nfor this service to build at all.\n\nAlso adds NEXT_PUBLIC_HIDE_UNFILLED=true. Without it the demo renders ten red\n[[TODO:*]] markers on /about alone — noise on a link sent to a partner.\nPresentation only: no figure is substituted for a missing one and check:legal\nstill reports every outstanding value.\n\nNot verified by deploying — that needs a Render account. This makes the\nblueprint internally consistent with the guard as it stands today.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c4e7e96b91578a9d5b566aeec47e08affc6e65fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/c4e7e96b91578a9d5b566aeec47e08affc6e65fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKGM0YTVjOTIzZTRmNjE3YmU4YWY3NzYyYTYyMTRkNTk3NDJlMzcwMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501","sha":"054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501"}],"sha":"c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/c4a5c923e4f617be8af7762a6214d59742e37030"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:17:39Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:17:39Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"fix(ui): stop sections staying invisible when the observer goes quiet\n\nReported as sections not animating on reload. They were not failing to\nanimate — they were staying HIDDEN. Reproduced on the home page: eight\nreveal-scroll sections at opacity 0 and blur(10px), one of them 363px inside\nthe viewport, still armed minutes after load.\n\nThe fail-safe was supposed to prevent exactly this and could not, because it\nasked the wrong question. It stands down when `observerIsLive` is set — and\nthat flag is set by the FIRST IntersectionObserver callback, which observe()\nalways delivers for every target whether it intersects or not. So it is true\nwithin a frame of arming, the timeout is cancelled permanently, and an observer\nthat delivers its initial callbacks and then stops tracking scroll leaves every\narmed section hidden for the rest of the visit. The check proved the observer\nhad been constructed, not that it was following the page.\n\nLiveness was the wrong question. Whether an element is ON SCREEN and still\nhidden needs no observer to answer, so a second net now sweeps the armed set on\na 400ms interval and reveals anything the observer should have caught. It:\n\n  - reveals rather than strips, so the entrance still plays — the visitor sees\n    the same animation, driven by the sweep instead of the observer\n  - leaves sections the visitor has not reached alone, so it does not\n    reintroduce the deadline-on-the-effect problem that made the old\n    unconditional timeout wrong\n  - stops itself once nothing is armed, costing nothing on a page read through\n  - strips the classes on a timeout rather than transitionend, since an\n    environment that is not running the transition never fires that event\n\nThe original observer path is untouched and still does the work normally.\n\nVerified on a production build, same scroll position before and after: sections\non screen but hidden went from 8 to 0, the three reported blocks now reach\nopacity 1, and five sections further down remain armed and waiting, which is\nthe correct state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ca831e704d6a9f75092ebac76aba83fb9fbb509","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/4ca831e704d6a9f75092ebac76aba83fb9fbb509"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDA1NGFkMzg1ZDI4ZjY5N2Y0MjE5MTdiNzU4NDZjODRjYjEwYjM1MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/b9a6f7866284f43fed8522c82228ed3987f27c3a","sha":"b9a6f7866284f43fed8522c82228ed3987f27c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/b9a6f7866284f43fed8522c82228ed3987f27c3a"}],"sha":"054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/054ad385d28f697f421917b75846c84cb10b3501"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/b9a6f7866284f43fed8522c82228ed3987f27c3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:11:01Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T07:11:01Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"fix(ui): give the last two static blocks an entrance\n\nReported as several areas having no blur entry animation. Auditing every\ntop-level block on the four pages for a .reveal / .reveal-load / .reveal-scroll\nancestor found only two without one:\n\n  /how-it-works  the closing ''See your options'' call to action\n  /kalkulator    the mandatory credit warning\n\nEverything else reported — the 01/02/03 cards, the four detail cards, ''How\nVeyra makes money'', the calculator card, the FAQ list, all four\nresponsible-borrowing sections — already animates, as part of a PARENT block\nrather than individually. That is why no single card appears to move on its\nown; it is a design choice, not a gap, and changing it means staggering\nchildren within a scroll reveal rather than adding classes.\n\nThe calculator''s warning had been left static deliberately, on the argument\nthat regulated copy should be readable the instant the page is. The home page\nhas always revealed the same component, so the two pages contradicted each\nother and the calculator looked unfinished. Nothing is at risk in aligning\nthem: ScrollReveal hides a block only after script has run AND found it below\nthe fold, unarms anything the observer misses, and never ships a hidden state\nin the server HTML — and this warning sits high enough that it is rarely armed\nat all. The stale comment asserting the opposite is removed rather than left to\nmislead.\n\nVerified after: every top-level block on /en/how-it-works has a reveal\nancestor (0 without), with two armed and waiting below the fold on load.\ntypecheck, lint, build 76/76 clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24ab1e0dca564fe16bf20da295fbec0eafd4160e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/24ab1e0dca564fe16bf20da295fbec0eafd4160e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/b9a6f7866284f43fed8522c82228ed3987f27c3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{