g_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/8a56ee0fd747b211a28d9ec73b70b59df64a52c6","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDhhNTZlZTBmZDc0N2IyMTFhMjhkOWVjNzNiNzBiNTlkZjY0YTUyYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/3c4d9741b211e07f466ce625047b04f49aa15d92","sha":"3c4d9741b211e07f466ce625047b04f49aa15d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/3c4d9741b211e07f466ce625047b04f49aa15d92"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624","sha":"f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624"}],"sha":"8a56ee0fd747b211a28d9ec73b70b59df64a52c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/8a56ee0fd747b211a28d9ec73b70b59df64a52c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/2428154b82a73628764bff2b894c9ef186692929/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:30:46Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:30:46Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"fix(viz): draw the connector lines that were never being painted\n\nReported against the diagram on /how-it-works: the line from the request to the\nmatching engine was missing, and the fan below it ended in mid-air.\n\nTwo separate faults, and a third instance of the first one elsewhere.\n\n1. Zero-extent bounding boxes. The gradient used the default\n   objectBoundingBox units, and a straight line has a bounding box with no\n   width (vertical) or no height (horizontal), which leaves the gradient\n   undefined. The browser then paints nothing at all -- no error, no fallback\n   colour, just an absent stroke. The two curved legs of the fan drew fine\n   because a curve has a real box, which is exactly what made this look like a\n   layout problem rather than a paint one.\n\n   Measured in Chrome rather than assumed: a vertical and a horizontal path\n   with an objectBoundingBox gradient both sample fully transparent, while the\n   same path with userSpaceOnUse, and a diagonal with either, paint normally.\n\n   This is the same fault already fixed in MatchingViz, in two copies that fix\n   did not reach:\n     - /how-it-works: the request-to-engine line and the centre leg of the fan\n     - /results: the progress line between request and matches, a horizontal\n       path whose animated dashes were invisible against the static track\n       underneath, so the strip looked deliberately plain\n\n2. The fan was drawn in a 120-unit-wide box while the options it points at are\n   a full-width three-column grid, so its outer legs stopped above the gaps\n   between the cards instead of reaching them. The connector now shares the\n   grid''s geometry -- max-w-lg, gap-3, three columns -- and derives the leg\n   endpoints from the column centres, so they land on the cards and stay\n   aligned at any width.\n\nAlso: both Connectors on the page declared the same gradient id. Duplicate ids\nare invalid and every url(#...) resolves to whichever came first; it happened to\nlook right only because the two gradients were identical. Now per-instance via\nuseId, with punctuation stripped -- useId embeds colons, which are legal in an\nid but not in a CSS selector, so the raw value works in a stroke attribute and\nbreaks the moment anything looks the gradient up from a stylesheet.\n\nVerified: all four connectors render on /how-it-works and terminate on the\noption cards; the results progress line goes from 0 painted gradient pixels to\n70; gradient ids unique and colon-free in the served HTML; 76/76 pages build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7f1cc4cefcde5b009608bd18ca9c402bae4a07c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/7f1cc4cefcde5b009608bd18ca9c402bae4a07c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/2428154b82a73628764bff2b894c9ef186692929","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/2428154b82a73628764bff2b894c9ef186692929","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDI0MjgxNTRiODJhNzM2Mjg3NjRiZmYyYjg5NGM5ZWYxODY2OTI5Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8","sha":"6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8"}],"sha":"2428154b82a73628764bff2b894c9ef186692929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/2428154b82a73628764bff2b894c9ef186692929"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:23:29Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T18:23:29Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"fix(i18n): put the locale in the URL, so no page is painted in the wrong language\n\nThe flash of Bulgarian was not a bug in the effect that swapped the language;\nit was structural. Every page was prerendered in the default locale and the\nvisitor''s choice lived in localStorage, which the server cannot read. The\ncorrection could therefore only ever run after the page had been painted. An\nearlier attempt to move it earlier, into useLayoutEffect, threw a hydration\nerror that tore down the client tree and took every other effect with it.\n\nSo the locale now lives in the URL and the server resolves it before rendering\na byte. Bulgarian keeps every URL it had -- the unprefixed slugs are the whole\nSEO surface and do not move -- and English lives under /en. Middleware rewrites\n/faq to /bg/faq internally; /bg/... is never a public address and is redirected\naway so each page has exactly one URL.\n\n  /faq     -> Bulgarian, unchanged\n  /en/faq  -> English\n\nBoth locales are prerendered: 76/76 pages static, none of this costs static\ngeneration. A visitor who picks a language gets a cookie the edge can read, so\na bookmark or a bare-domain visit lands in their language from any entry point.\nCrawlers carry no cookie and so always see Bulgarian at the unprefixed URL,\nwhich is exactly what the canonical and the hreflang alternates claim.\n\nConsequences worth reading:\n\n- The four `document.title = ...` effects are gone. They existed for the same\n  reason the flash did -- the locale was only known in the browser -- and they\n  were overwriting the SEO titles from PAGE_SEO with worse ones, after a\n  visible title flash. The server now renders the right title up front.\n\n- English SEO copy (PAGE_SEO_EN) covers the 12 translated pages. Presence in\n  that map is what makes an English page indexable, so a page whose English\n  copy has not been written yet is noindex rather than published to search\n  under a Bulgarian title.\n\n- The 12 Bulgarian-only pages (landing pages, guides) have /en twins so an\n  English reader following a link keeps English chrome, but they are noindex\n  and canonicalise to the Bulgarian URL, their prose is marked lang=\"bg\" so a\n  screen reader does not read Bulgarian with English pronunciation, and a\n  notice says the page is Bulgarian only. That set is derived from the content\n  itself, so a new landing page cannot silently claim an English twin.\n\n- robots.txt disallowed /apply and /results but would not have covered\n  /en/apply and /en/results, which carry the same personal data. Now expanded\n  across every locale.\n\n- The locale cookie is the site''s first actual cookie -- everything else was\n  localStorage -- so the cookie policy names it in both catalogues.\n\n- Landing-page CTA labels came from Bulgarian string literals, invisible while\n  those pages were Bulgarian-only. They now come from the catalogue, which also\n  fixes a latent bug: PrimaryCta ignores its label only while pre-launch is on.\n\n- lib/locale.ts (path helpers) is deliberately separate from lib/bg-only.ts\n  (which reads the landing and guide content). The helpers are reached from\n  client components, and merging them would ship every Bulgarian landing page\n  to the browser on every route. Verified absent from the client chunks.\n\nVerified on a production build: 28 routes x 2 locales all 200; server HTML and\nhydrated DOM identical in lang, title and h1 (so there is no window in which\nthe wrong language can be shown); zero console errors, in particular no\nhydration error; canonical/hreflang/noindex correct for all three page classes;\nsitemap lists no noindex twin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a82f99534cebb39796f933c0c6b28810d599a27d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/a82f99534cebb39796f933c0c6b28810d599a27d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDYwMThjYTczM2RkMGI2NTVjODRhYzY1ZTg3NDUwYTc4OTlmOWViZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624","sha":"f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624"}],"sha":"6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/6018ca733dd0b655c84ac65e87450a7899f9ebd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:42:30Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:42:30Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"fix(ui): make the hero''s load animation actually run, as a blur reveal\n\nThe hero asked for the same blur-and-rise entrance the scroll sections\nhave, but on page load rather than on scroll. Implementing it turned up\nthat the existing load animation had never run at all.\n\n`.reveal > *` declared `animation: fade-up ...`, and `fade-up` was\ndefined only in tailwind.config''s `keyframes`. Tailwind emits a themed\n@keyframes block only when a matching `animate-*` utility turns up in\nthe scanned markup; nothing used `animate-fade-up`, so no keyframes were\ngenerated. The rule pointed at a name with nothing behind it and the\nhero simply appeared. Confirmed from the CSSOM: the document carried\ndash-flow, pulse-node, menu-in and menu-out -- each either used as a\nutility or hand-written -- and no fade-up.\n\nSo the keyframes are written out here alongside menu-in/menu-out rather\nthan declared in the theme, with a comment recording why they have to\nstay. The values match .reveal-scroll (blur 10px, 26px rise) so the hero\nand the sections below share one entrance language; the existing\n0.04s-0.28s stagger is unchanged.\n\nDuration is 0.7s against the scroll version''s 0.85s. This one sits in\nfront of first paint and the hero headline is the LCP element, so\nholding it out of focus costs load metrics; 0.7s reads the same and\ngives that back.\n\nVerified by scrubbing the animation to exact timestamps rather than\nracing the clock -- at 175ms it is blur(2.6px), opacity 0.74, 6.8px\nbelow rest. Picked up by PageShell and LandingPage too. The global\nprefers-reduced-motion block already collapses it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6d70c0c031625a15fffd3b7af31f15ef451737b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/6d70c0c031625a15fffd3b7af31f15ef451737b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKGYyMGM5NjU4N2RhMGExNTQ0YWY4OTNlOGVlZWNlMGQ0NDM2NTI2MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f","sha":"7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f"}],"sha":"f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/f20c96587da0a1544af893e8eeece0d443652624"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:33:18Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:33:18Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"feat(ui): frosted chrome, scroll reveal, and typographic hierarchy\n\nA design pass over the marketing pages. Brand tokens, IA and copy are all\nunchanged; this is material, motion and hierarchy.\n\nFrosted glass. Buttons keep their exact colours and pill shape and gain the\nmaterial: a lit top edge, a darker bottom edge, blur behind the translucent\nparts. Fills stay opaque enough to hold contrast — measured at 8.78:1 for\nbtn-mint and 17.23:1 for btn-ghost. The navigation bar is frosted at all times\nrather than only once scrolled, deepening its tint as content passes beneath,\nand the menu button and language toggle share the same material.\n\nThe header itself deliberately carries no backdrop-filter. An element with one\nbecomes a backdrop root for its descendants, which meant the dropdown panel\nhad nothing left to sample and stayed see-through however high its blur went.\nThe bar''s glass is now its own layer and the panel is a sibling of it, so each\nsamples the page directly and both frost properly. The panel is also absolute,\nso opening the menu overlays the page instead of pushing it down.\n\n`under-nav` runs each page''s background up behind the bar and gives the height\nstraight back as padding, so the bar has something to refract on every page\nrather than only the home page.\n\nScroll reveal: sections rise 26px out of a 10px blur as they are scrolled to,\nvia IntersectionObserver. Deliberately fail-safe, because this site carries\nlegal disclosures and content stuck invisible would be far worse than a missing\nanimation: a section is hidden only after script has run AND found it below the\nfold, the hiding class is REMOVED rather than overridden once the transition\nends, and a 1.6s timer unarms anything the observer missed. Feature-detecting\nIntersectionObserver is not enough — it can exist and never fire.\n\nTypography: page bodies are capped at 52ch, not 65ch. The CSS `ch` unit is the\nwidth of \"0\", which is wider than this face''s average letter, so 65ch measured\nout at 87 real characters. 52ch lands at 70 in English and 63 in Bulgarian.\nSection headings step up from 1.2rem so they stop reading as bold first lines,\nintros become real leads, and page titles get a short accent rule.\n\nLayout fixes: hero CTAs sit side by side at every width down to 320px, an\norphaned grid cell on /loans and /how-it-works is given the full row, and the\nhomepage drops one eyebrow and a decorative dot.\n\nReduced motion and reduced transparency are honoured throughout, with solid\nfills where backdrop-filter is unavailable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"13f88baf96ba487595e1ac456d2ae763dea4dc9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/13f88baf96ba487595e1ac456d2ae763dea4dc9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDdjOGJhODU2N2Y5MzVhMTA3N2ViNThmZjRjYmE0MWE4ZDljMWEzN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4","sha":"8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4"}],"sha":"7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/7c8ba8567f935a1077eb58ff4cba41a8d9c1a37f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:32:58Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:32:58Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"fix(viz): draw the vertical connectors, and stop the option chips colliding\n\nTwo of the four connector lines never rendered: request-to-engine, and\nengine-to-middle-option. Both are perfectly vertical, and that is the cause.\nrouteGrad used the default objectBoundingBox units, a vertical path has a\nzero-width bounding box, and a gradient in bounding-box units is undefined\nthere, so the browser skipped painting the stroke entirely. The two curved\npaths drew fine because their boxes have width. Switching the gradient to\nuserSpaceOnUse, anchored to the viewBox, makes straight and curved paths\nbehave identically.\n\nThe three option chips also overlapped: each sized itself to its label, and\nwith centres at 19/50/81 percent they ran into each other. The right-hand one\nwrapped to a second line as a result, which read as a taller pill than its\nneighbours rather than as a matching set. The outer two now sit wider, the\nmiddle one drops further, padding is tighter and both label lines are nowrap.\n\nMeasured after: all three chips 44px tall, zero overlapping pairs, in both\nlocales, and all four connector paths resolve the gradient with real lengths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48a23973539cc258302af236d52e4dc84dc69634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/48a23973539cc258302af236d52e4dc84dc69634"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDgyMTljZWZhMzMzNzE4MDBjYjI1NzE3N2M3MmFiNzY5OTYwMTk1ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/293e128a87083659cb32018d7a2ce26b51d24ef7","sha":"293e128a87083659cb32018d7a2ce26b51d24ef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/293e128a87083659cb32018d7a2ce26b51d24ef7"}],"sha":"8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/8219cefa33371800cb257177c72ab769960195e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/293e128a87083659cb32018d7a2ce26b51d24ef7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:32:43Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:32:43Z","email":"alaahalabibusiness@gmail.com","name":"alaahlb"},"message":"feat(legal): warning in the reader''s language, and hide unfilled values locally\n\nTwo changes to how regulated values and the statutory warning present.\n\nThe credit warning now renders in the active locale rather than always in\nBulgarian. CREDIT_WARNING remains the Bulgarian statutory string and is still\nwhat ships by default; a locale that supplies legal.warningGloss shows its own\nwording instead. The owner asked for this repeatedly after seeing an\nuntranslated sentence on English pages.\n\n  RISK, STATED PLAINLY: the mandated Bulgarian wording is no longer displayed\n  in the English view. Whether that satisfies the Act is a question for the\n  operator''s ЗПК adviser, not something this change settles. Reverting is one\n  edit: render CREDIT_WARNING unconditionally.\n\nSeparately, NEXT_PUBLIC_HIDE_UNFILLED omits rows whose regulated value is still\nan unfilled [[TODO:*]] placeholder, so the site can be shown to a prospective\npartner before the company is registered without reading as a page of gaps.\nIt is opt-in, lives in .env.local (gitignored), and changes presentation only:\nno figure is substituted for a missing one, DISCLOSURES_INCOMPLETE and\nCOMPANY_INCOMPLETE are untouched, check-legal-values.mjs still reports all 16\nvalues outstanding, and a production build is still refused. The disclosures\npanel keeps a line saying the values are pending, so the block cannot read as\nfinished when it is not, and CompanyIdentity removes itself entirely rather\nthan showing a heading over nothing.\n\nTodoMark gives both call sites one rendering for a missing value so the two\ncannot drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"15746ea22b5d711d04d2524539ccf7f47da1c9f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/trees/15746ea22b5d711d04d2524539ccf7f47da1c9f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/git/commits/293e128a87083659cb32018d7a2ce26b51d24ef7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218256958?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alaahlb","id":218256958,"login":"alaahlb","node_id":"U_kgDODQJWPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alaahlb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/293e128a87083659cb32018d7a2ce26b51d24ef7","node_id":"C_kwDOUCSFDdoAKDI5M2UxMjhhODcwODM2NTljYjMyMDE4ZDdhMmNlMjZiNTFkMjRlZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vulko99/Veyra/commit/3c4d9741b211e07f466ce625047b04f49aa15d92","sha":"3c4d9741b211e07f466ce625047b04f49aa15d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commits/3c4d9741b211e07f466ce625047b04f49aa15d92"}],"sha":"293e128a87083659cb32018d7a2ce26b51d24ef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vulko99/Veyra/commi