"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/natibs/mfe-platform/commits/bc64d0a05578e8e68def8363b3ea5eefd20088b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T10:36:30Z","email":"nati.bs@gmail.com","name":"Nati Ben-Shalom"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T10:36:30Z","email":"nati.bs@gmail.com","name":"Nati Ben-Shalom"},"message":"Make the federation manifest configurable per environment\n\nAdd shell-app/env/federation.manifest.{dev,qa,preprod,prod}.json and a\nset-env script that promotes one onto a build''s output (or public/ for\nlocal dev). Since the manifest is fetched at runtime rather than baked\ninto the JS bundle, this lets a single build artifact be promoted through\nenvironments by swapping just this one file, instead of building per\nenvironment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"269eed2122c0fa244573ee35874447e94d2a15bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/natibs/mfe-platform/git/trees/269eed2122c0fa244573ee35874447e94d2a15bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/natibs/mfe-platform/git/commits/bc64d0a05578e8e68def8363b3ea5eefd20088b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10099701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natibs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.