/github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/2c02f821441670e9e04939f7f59a31bf3f5a1543/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T10:35:18Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T10:35:18Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Charts: state a flat result instead of plotting nothing\n\nTotal Blocking Time is zero on every route in both stacks, and Cumulative Layout\nShift is zero on all but one. Six rows of invisible slivers labelled 0.0000 reads\nas a broken render; one sentence reads as the finding it is — the best available\nresult, and nothing to plot.\n\nValue labels now sit clear of the whisker rather than at the bar end, so a wide\nspread no longer draws a line through its own number.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"5f33b13db2a02e260577287eb1bd775bdac51661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/5f33b13db2a02e260577287eb1bd775bdac51661"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/2c02f821441670e9e04939f7f59a31bf3f5a1543","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/2c02f821441670e9e04939f7f59a31bf3f5a1543","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDJjMDJmODIxNDQxNjcwZTllMDQ5MzlmN2Y1OWEzMWJmM2Y1YTE1NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034","sha":"3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034"}],"sha":"2c02f821441670e9e04939f7f59a31bf3f5a1543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/2c02f821441670e9e04939f7f59a31bf3f5a1543"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T10:33:39Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T10:33:39Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Report declares its own parameters, and charts the vitals\n\nTwo gaps in the generated report.\n\nIt did not say what it was measuring under. \"LCP 2.6 s\" means nothing without the\nconnection it was measured over, and \"3x faster builds\" means nothing without\nknowing both were built with the same flags. The report now carries a Parameters\nsection: the full measurement profile with its numbers (throttle rate, Kbps up\nand down, RTT, core count, heap ceiling, viewport), the toolchain versions, every\nMF_* variable in effect, the topology with ports and roles, the dependencies the\nbuild ACTUALLY shared, every budget, and every waiver with its reason.\n\nAll of it is read from the objects that shaped the run — the profile module, the\nbudget objects the checks use, the manifests the build emitted, each suite''s own\nreport. A hand-maintained list would drift from the run it claims to describe,\nwhich is worse than no list.\n\nAnd it printed Core Web Vitals as numbers only. Eight charts now: LCP, FCP, CLS,\nINP, TBT and TTFB against Google''s \"good\" thresholds drawn as lines, plus\nmain-thread time, script time, JS heap and the DOM-element conformance check.\nInline SVG, no library — the page is self-contained under a strict content\npolicy, and a charting library would outweigh the charts.\n\nEvery bar carries a whisker for its min and max across runs. A Core Web Vital is\nthree things at once — a value, a threshold, and a spread — and a chart showing\nonly the first invites the error this repo already made once, where a single\nsample was read as a result.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"54fe7ea93ed288cf90cbe222257055e66aae603e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/54fe7ea93ed288cf90cbe222257055e66aae603e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDNiYWEzODAyNTA5MmM0ZjhkMTA0ZGFiNzZiNzc2ZWZjMGZmNWQwMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133","sha":"1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133"}],"sha":"3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/3baa38025092c4f8d104dab76b776efc0ff5d034"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:54:29Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:54:29Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Measure under a device profile, not on the machine running the bench\n\nThe first research dataset had a hole in it that only network throttling could\nshow: on localhost bytes are free. One stack transferred 31.6% more on its\nheaviest page than the other and both reported the same LCP to the millisecond,\nbecause a difference in transfer size is never paid for when there is no\nconnection to pay it over.\n\nMF_PROFILE now selects the conditions and every archived run records which\nproduced its numbers. `constrained` is the default — Lighthouse mobile at the\nreference viewport: 4x CPU, Slow 4G (1.6 Mbps down, 750 Kbps up, 150 ms RTT),\nfour cores, 512 MB heap cap. LCP across the storefront moves from a uniform\n~144 ms to a range of 832 ms to 2.6 s.\n\n`constrained` and `mobile` are separate on purpose. A phone viewport changes\nwhich markup renders — the header search is `hidden lg:block`, so at 412 px it is\nabsent rather than smaller — and folding that into one profile would mean the\nDOM-conformance check was comparing two different documents.\n\nTime budgets now scale with the CPU factor and byte budgets do not. The\nfederation-runtime ceiling was set at 60 ms unthrottled and measured 76.6 ms at\n4x; the runtime had not changed, the machine had. `longTaskMs` stays at 50 ms\nbecause that is the specification''s definition, not a local judgement.\n\nThe aggregator refuses to average runs from different profiles: a mean across a\nthrottled and an unthrottled run describes no device anyone owns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"417e29e7de41c4044cd897e2df6d4db845d30a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/417e29e7de41c4044cd897e2df6d4db845d30a30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDFmZWVmMDcxZDdkNDE1YTQ1ZWM5ZWQxY2E2ODlmZTk1M2E1NDIxMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2","sha":"8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2"}],"sha":"1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/1feef071d7d415a45ec9ed1ca689fe953a542133"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:36:19Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:36:19Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"README: replace the throughput note with what n=3 actually settled\n\nThe previous entry recorded the retraction, which was itself under-evidenced.\nThree controlled runs resolve it: Svelte is faster by 6.6-10.0% at 0.4-3.8%\nvariance. The lesson worth keeping is not about throughput but about the harness\n— the middle pair of runs was most likely contaminated by a server that outlived\nits stack, which the harness now refuses to measure through.\n\nAdds the crash-versus-failure finding alongside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"10b6ab1942df613d35fda4b5c746ead7ca7514e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/10b6ab1942df613d35fda4b5c746ead7ca7514e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDhlZDQ5MTc3MzdhNzk4MzAxMTU4NzdjODhjN2FlMDNmNTZiNTQyYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583","sha":"b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583"}],"sha":"8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/8ed4917737a79830115877c88c7ae03f56b542a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:35:46Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:35:46Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Record the definitive n=3 research dataset and report\n\nThree runs of each stack, 368/368 checks every run, 251 metrics, 114 resolvable\ndifferences. Both stacks measured on the same machine, from the same commit,\nagainst the same catalog, through a harness that verifies the right stack is\nserving before it measures anything.\n\nDOM conformance is exact: all five document routes render the identical body\nelement count on both stacks, at 0.0% variance. The two implementations are the\nsame application, which is the precondition every other number here depends on.\n\nAnd it settles a question I got wrong twice. SSR throughput favours Svelte by\n6.6-10.0% across four routes, with coefficients of variation between 0.4% and\n3.8% — resolvable, not noise. I first claimed it from a single run, then\nretracted it as noise on the strength of two uncontrolled ones. The retraction\nwas as under-evidenced as the claim; the likeliest explanation for that middle\npair is the stale-server condition found later and now guarded against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"60007c634e9b1896a61ab5ec261adeb31f52952d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/60007c634e9b1896a61ab5ec261adeb31f52952d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGI4MGEzODNkMWMyZTEwYzJiNmMwYmU4ODA1NTVhNTk2Y2MxYTU1ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa","sha":"3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa"}],"sha":"b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/b80a383d1c2e10c2b6c0be880555a596cc1a5583"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:00:03Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:00:03Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Fix the flake that killed two research runs, and tell a crash from a failure\n\nThe behaviours suite has twice ended a 45-minute research run, and both times it\nlooked like a hang: two sections of output, no verdict, and a summary line saying\n\"scroll up for the failing checks\" with no failing check to find.\n\nIt was not failing. It was dying. `route.fetch()` inside a Playwright route\nhandler raised `socket hang up`, and an unhandled rejection in a route handler\nends the process — Node reports it from node:internal/process/promises with no\nsuite name attached. The fetch can legitimately fail: the page may navigate or\nclose mid-flight, and this suite runs after one that has just loaded every route.\nBoth handlers in the bench are now guarded, and a failed fetch degrades that one\nmeasurement rather than the run.\n\nThe runner now streams output AND captures it, so it can tell the two apart. A\nsuite that reached its own verdict prints \"N/M passed\"; one that did not, crashed\n— and the summary says CRSH, prints the last six lines, and states plainly that a\ncrash is a bug in the suite or the environment rather than a regression in the\napplication. Those need different responses, and the tooling was giving them the\nsame one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"b87a729f5cf334ab712538e5247860c3148c477a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/b87a729f5cf334ab712538e5247860c3148c477a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDNlM2FiZTZlMDEyZWNjNGQ4YjZlMjFhN2ExM2E0MmYwNWM4MGE0ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d","sha":"ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d"}],"sha":"3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/3e3abe6e012ecc4d8b6e21a7a13a42f05c80a4fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T07:45:21Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T07:45:21Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Make the DOM conformance metric measure conformance\n\n`domElements` counted the whole document, so stylesheet and preload links sat in\na structural metric. The entire remaining difference between the two stacks — one\nelement, on two routes — turned out to be a single `<link>`: chunking, not\nstructure.\n\nIt now counts BODY elements only, and `headLinks` is reported separately, because\nthat difference is real and worth seeing; it just is not a structural one.\n\nSecond refinement this metric has forced on itself. It began as CDP''s `Nodes`,\nwhich counts text and comment nodes, and reported /cart as 456 against 259 —\na 76% apparent divergence on a page whose element counts differ by one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"4c850495f8fd1520297c8c6020987aaadede74a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/4c850495f8fd1520297c8c6020987aaadede74a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGVmNTJiZWVlNTc0OGRjOWYyYTEzYmQ0MmUwOGY5ZDM1MTlhOTBhNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9","sha":"eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9"}],"sha":"ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/ef52beee5748dc9f2a13bd42e08f9d3519a90a4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T07:07:23Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T07:07:23Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Refuse to measure a stack that is not the stack being served\n\nA transient failure during the first full research run — `CHROME is not defined`,\ntwice, in the React stack''s verify suite — did not reproduce in a targeted re-run.\nRather than shrug at it, the harness now checks the condition that would explain\nit, because this repo has been bitten by that condition twice before.\n\nA health probe cannot catch a server that outlived its stack and went on\nanswering on the same port with a previous build: something IS listening, probes\npass, pages render, and the numbers are quietly wrong. The manifest can catch it.\nIt names the package that built it and lists the exposes that build produced, so\ncomparing the served manifest to the one on disk is the difference between \"a\nserver answered\" and \"the server I built is answering\".\n\nverifyServing() now runs before every measured run, restarts once on mismatch,\nand refuses to measure rather than producing a number nobody can trust. Verified\nby negative control: with the Svelte stack running and React under test it names\nall four remotes, the port, and both build identities.\n\nThe first version of the guard had the exact bug it exists to catch. It resolved\neach remote''s on-disk path through the topology''s `dir`, which reads MF_STACK at\nimport time — and this runner is a parent looping over several stacks, so it\ncompared every remote against whichever stack the parent happened to default to\nand reported a correct stack as entirely mismatched. Paths are now resolved from\nthe stack being measured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"1ab4839abe386d07ffbbb76684e03891d8be7cb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/1ab4839abe386d07ffbbb76684e03891d8be7cb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGVhYWNiMWY5MzQyNGUwNTZiM2Q2MzcxZDQ0YjkxNzBhY2E1YWIzYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0","sha":"6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0"}],"sha":"eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/eaacb1f93424e056b3d6371d44b9170aca5ab3c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:49:28Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:49:28Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Add the per-section comparison to the HTML report\n\nEach results section now carries its own comparison table with the resolvability\nverdict stated per row, rather than leaving a reader to infer it from two means\nand a standard deviation. A row that cannot be separated at this sample size says\n\"within noise\" in the same chip style as an unstable metric, so it reads as a\nresult rather than as a missing one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"c7a2429b0e88a9448834a75ad5ccd33cc6938ee3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/c7a2429b0e88a9448834a75ad5ccd33cc6938ee3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDZjOTQ1YWM5MjgzNTk0MmMzZmJmZDI1ODIxNGU4NDdhZGEyYTJmYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39","sha":"62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39"}],"sha":"6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/6c945ac92835942c3fbfd258214e847ada2a2fa0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:48:39Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:48:39Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Publish the research report as a page as well as markdown\n\nSame dataset, same statistics, two renderings. The markdown is the archival\nrecord — it lives in git and reviews cleanly. The HTML is what gets sent to\nsomeone who has to make a decision from it.\n\nThe design carries one idea: no number appears without its dispersion and its\nstability class, and the class is a visual chip rather than a column a reader has\nto look up. Someone skimming should be unable to mistake an unstable metric for a\nsettled one. Every metric family carries its instrument card — what the figure\nis, which tool produced it, what it excludes — beside the table rather than in a\nfootnote.\n\nThe repo''s own no-raw-color rule fired on the report stylesheet, correctly for\napp code and wrongly here: a generated report has no design system to draw from,\nand pointing it at var(--color-brand-700) would produce a page that renders\nunstyled everywhere except inside the application it reports on. Exempted in the\nshared config with that reasoning rather than disabled inline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"51df9d40f4c528501206bc7f36158a7efbf9043b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/51df9d40f4c528501206bc7f36158a7efbf9043b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDYyZGFkM2Q1M2ZjN2RhNGZhNDA0NDhkNjA2YTZmOWU3NmNmYzdiMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189","sha":"efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189"}],"sha":"62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/62dad3d53fc7da4fa40448d606a6f9e76cfc7b39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:45:13Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:45:13Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"One command, three runs, a report that states its own confidence\n\n`MF_RUNS=3 pnpm research` builds every stack, restarts it, runs all sixteen\nsuites, repeats, and produces a research report from the aggregate. Everything a\nperson had to remember to do three times is now done by the command, because\nanything remembered three times is done twice and then compared.\n\nEvery one of the 239 metrics is reported with all of its samples, a standard\ndeviation, a coefficient of variation and a stability class computed from the\ndata — deterministic, stable, variable or unstable. A stack-to-stack difference\nis called resolvable only when the gap between means exceeds twice the average\nspread; everything else is reported as \"within noise\", which is a result too.\n\nThis format exists because of the error it prevents, and the report says so in\nits own introduction: a single run reported 7-11% higher throughput for one\nstack, and a second run of identical builds gave -11% to -14%. Both numbers were\nright. Printing a mean without its dispersion was not.\n\nNew: packages/bench/src/lib/stats.mjs (summary statistics and resolvability),\nlib/dictionary.mjs (what each metric IS, which instrument produced it, and what\nit excludes — so no figure appears without its provenance), research.mjs (the\nloop) and report.mjs (formatting, deliberately separate so a report can be\nregenerated from a dataset without re-measuring). docs/methodology.md covers the\nwhole method.\n\nThe dry run immediately earned it. `domNodes` showed /cart at 456 for Svelte\nagainst 259 for React — a 76% apparent DOM divergence on an application whose\nspec freezes DOM structure. The element counts were 137 and 136; the rest was\nSvelte''s anchor comments, which CDP''s `Nodes` counts. Added `domElements` as the\nconformance metric and documented `domNodes` as a real cost that says nothing\nabout structure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"b7b2724e19b2db238abf5066d1e7efc9c9ee282d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/b7b2724e19b2db238abf5066d1e7efc9c9ee282d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGVmZWQxODg2OGY2NzJlZDA3NzhkMDVjMTE0NjNlZjMzYzc4ZTgxODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9","sha":"a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9"}],"sha":"efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/efed18868f672ed0778d05c11463ef33c78e8189"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:52:40Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:52:40Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Measure browser CPU, and correct an SSR throughput claim that was noise\n\nTwo gaps in what was reported, one of them a real error.\n\nBrowser CPU was collected and never surfaced. Chrome''s own counters — script,\nlayout and style duration at 4x throttling — were in the raw vitals report but\nabsent from the archived headline and from the comparison. Total main-thread busy\ntime (TaskDuration) and JS heap were not captured at all, though the CDP call\nalready returned them.\n\nAll of it is now recorded and BUDGETED rather than merely printed, because it is\nthe one client-side difference the Core Web Vitals cannot show: both stacks hold\nTBT at zero on every route while doing measurably different amounts of work. On\nthe two pages that mount something, Svelte does 20-29% less script work (58.2 ms\nagainst 41.3 on /cart) and holds 8-11% less JS heap on every route. A comparison\nthat stopped at the vitals would have called the two identical on the client.\n\nThe correction: an earlier version reported Svelte serving 7-11% more requests\nper second. That was one run. A second run on the same builds gave +2.3%, -10.9%\nand -14.0% on the same routes. SSR throughput and CPU per request are\nindistinguishable between these stacks at this sample size, and reporting the\nfirst run as a difference was wrong. Byte counts and main-thread times reproduce;\nthroughput does not.\n\nResident memory is the one server-side figure that does move consistently:\nSvelte''s hosts hold 25-60% more RSS across all four routes in both runs.\n\nBoth stacks re-run and re-archived: 368/368 each, same spec, same catalog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"b9ed2dd033a1cbdd342a3cfc03e70f80a444138f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/b9ed2dd033a1cbdd342a3cfc03e70f80a444138f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGE2Y2MzMGFjNmJlOGE4OTk5ZDI4ZDFhNThjYzI0ZGRlMDYwYTQ3YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68","sha":"5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68"}],"sha":"a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/a6cc30ac6be8a8999d28d1a58cc24dde060a47a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:28:48Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:28:48Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Record the React/Svelte comparison in the README\n\nTwo stacks now, both green on the same 16 suites and the same frozen spec, so\nthe headline findings can be stated as measurements rather than projections.\n\nThe one worth leading with: a framework''s size is a property of how many times\nyou pay for it. Svelte''s runtime is 3.3x smaller and cannot be shared between\nremotes; React''s is larger and is shared once. Content pages tie, a page with one\ninteractive remote is ~36 kB lighter in Svelte, and the page composing three\nteams'' widgets is 67.8 kB heavier — with each contributing remote roughly\ndoubling while the host shrinks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"6eab382d488e4ab53c459c8def2a29295f0fe695","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/6eab382d488e4ab53c459c8def2a29295f0fe695"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDVmOWU2MzllNjU5Mzc0MTMyYzlhMGYyNWE3MTE1YWZkNjM1MjdmNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422","sha":"e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422"}],"sha":"5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/5f9e639e659374132c9a0f25a7115afd63527f68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:25:23Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:25:23Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"rspack-svelte passes all 16 suites — a real comparison exists\n\n366/366 checks green against the Svelte stack, and the React baseline re-run on\nthe same catalog so the two are comparable: same SPEC_VERSION, same catalog hash,\nsame machine.\n\nThe suites ran UNMODIFIED. That was the whole point of the portability audit, and\nit held: contract, widgets, css, contamination, vitals, a11y, audit and ssr all\npassed first time against an implementation in a different framework. Only two\nsuites failed on the first run, and they were the two docs/porting-a-stack.md\npredicts.\n\nbudget failed because budgets are per-app measurements, not constants. The Svelte\nbudgets are now measured for this stack rather than copied, and their SHAPE is\nthe finding: hosts far smaller (35.4 kB own JS against React''s 97.6 — no\nframework in the host at all), remotes larger (cart 16.8 against 10.8), because\nSvelte''s runtime cannot be shared and every remote carries a private copy. CSS is\nidentical to the kilobyte, because both stacks consume the same token\nstylesheets.\n\ndx failed because the suite itself hardcoded `src/List.tsx` and `StockPanel.tsx`\n— React filenames — which made it unrunnable against any other stack. Fixed in\nthe SUITE, per this repo''s rule that a stack-specific assumption in the\nmeasurement is a bug in the measurement. It now discovers the largest source file\nto touch, and finds the file to edit by the text it renders rather than by name.\n\nsvelte-check was silently absent from one package and reported nothing; with it\ninstalled it found four real type errors, including two missing CSS-module\ndeclarations. My earlier \"typecheck clean\" greps for `error TS` had been missing\nsvelte-check output entirely — worth recording, because a check that reports\nnothing looks identical to a check that passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"d993871cba76d5080315b67c36ffea1f6176395d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/d993871cba76d5080315b67c36ffea1f6176395d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGU3NzgwOTI5YmZjOTRkOTEzODNkNmExZDE2NDJkZDI4NmQyOGU0MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0","sha":"a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0"}],"sha":"e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/e7780929bfc94d91383d6a1d1642dd286d28e422"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:02:42Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:02:42Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"rspack-svelte: the account host, and the rule that governs a Svelte boundary\n\nAll six apps now build and run. The account SPA mounts, routes client-side, and\nrenders three teams'' widgets on one page with no console errors.\n\nGetting the widgets to render took three rounds, and each one narrowed the same\nrule until it was exact. Recording it here because it is the most useful thing\nthis stack has produced so far:\n\n1. A component object cannot cross the boundary. A Svelte 5 component closes over\n   the svelte/internal/client instance that compiled it, and that instance cannot\n   be shared — sharing it hangs the container permanently. Rendering another\n   remote''s component inside the host''s tree fails as \"Cannot read properties of\n   null (reading ''nodes'')\". Remotes now expose a MOUNT FUNCTION; only a DOM node\n   and plain data cross.\n\n2. Sharing `svelte` — the public entry — is worse than useless. It re-exports\n   `mount`, which closes over the sharer''s runtime, so a remote mounting its own\n   component called the HOST''s mount against its own compiled output. Same error,\n   now thrown from inside the remote''s chunk.\n\n3. Sharing @mf-eval/svelte-contracts fails one layer up. It calls setContext, so\n   a shared copy runs Svelte''s lifecycle against the sharer''s runtime and throws\n   lifecycle_outside_component in a remote that is very much inside a component.\n\nThe rule: in the Svelte stack, ONLY plain data and DOM nodes cross a federation\nboundary. Anything touching the framework — a component, a context, a lifecycle\ncall, a rune — belongs to exactly one side.\n\nNote the exact inversion. The React binding MUST be a shared singleton, because a\nReact context object has identity and two copies break useCart. The Svelte\nbinding must NOT be shared, for the same architectural reason pointing the other\nway. That asymmetry is a result, not a workaround.\n\nConsequence, and it is the number the comparison turns on: every Svelte remote\ncarries a complete private runtime. Cross-remote state travels through\n@mf-eval/contracts and a cookie — framework-agnostic, and the reason that store\nwas written that way before either stack existed.\n\nStorefront routes all still 200; lint and typecheck clean across both stacks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"5b06f413d4ad915ce1c3d950595f7d93d4f29257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/5b06f413d4ad915ce1c3d950595f7d93d4f29257"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGExYzliZDBhZGFlM2RlYzdmZjMwM2U5NGU0YjY3OGYzY2E0NTZlZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80","sha":"d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80"}],"sha":"a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/a1c9bd0adae3dec7ff303e94e4b678f3ca456ef0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:30:36Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:30:36Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"rspack-svelte: the storefront renders, end to end\n\nAll five storefront routes serve 200 with the correct test ids: /, /faq,\n/faq/contact, /product, /product/p-0001, /cart. Chrome comes from the chrome\nremote, pages from faq/product/cart, both behaviours are declared in the markup,\nand the cart drawer placeholder reserves its box on the detail page.\n\nThe CSS Module experiment reproduces exactly: .cart-panel-V0TX and\n.product-panel-V0TX render on /product/p-0001 in this stack too. Same class\nnames, same hashes, two applications, no coordination — the isolation is a\nproperty of the build config, not of the framework.\n\nTwo fixes it took to get there, both in the shared layer and both benefiting\neither stack:\n\nloadChrome now accepts a named OR default export. A React component is\n`export function Header`; a .svelte file has exactly one export and it is the\ndefault. shell-kit resolves chrome for every stack, so forcing one framework''s\nconvention on the other was the bug. It failed as \"Cannot read properties of\nundefined\" from inside the renderer, naming neither the remote nor the export.\n\nThe shell needed __MF_REGISTRY_URL__, which the React shell passes and I had\nomitted. Without it shell-kit threw during module init, so every later call saw\nan undefined module — the error pointed at a minified property name, three layers\nfrom the cause.\n\nWorth recording: two of the three debugging rounds here were chasing a stale\nserver process holding the port and serving an older build. That is exactly the\nfailure scripts/stack.mjs stop was written to prevent, and I hit it by starting\nservers by hand and bypassing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"362e9aea5a8944d841d31187d88d550d5dc1b99a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/362e9aea5a8944d841d31187d88d550d5dc1b99a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGQ1MzM0NmI3N2RhYmJjMDQwZDE0ODY3Nzc0YWEyMWQ5Mjk2YWJhODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597","sha":"6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597"}],"sha":"d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/d53346b77dabbc040d14867774aa21d9296aba80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:26:24Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:26:24Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"rspack-svelte: the storefront host\n\nServer render, route matching, slot registry, behaviour scanning, preload\nplanning and island mounting — the same rules as the React shell, with three\nplaces where Svelte forces a different shape:\n\nContext can only be established inside a component, so the React stack''s\n<SlotProvider> wrapper becomes App.svelte with the registry as props. Chrome is\nstill rendered as SIBLINGS of the content rather than as a wrapper: a wrapper\nwould put every host''s page content inside [data-owner=\"chrome\"] and chrome''s\nscoped stylesheet would match other teams'' markup.\n\nIslands cannot be mounted directly for the same reason, so Island.svelte carries\nthe cart and slot contexts around whatever is being mounted. The server rendered\na placeholder into that box, so the island REPLACES it rather than hydrating it —\nthe two markups are deliberately different, one reserves space and the other\nshows data.\n\nsvelte/server''s render() returns head and body separately, and the head content\nis now emitted into the document. JSX has nowhere to put it, so the React stack\nhas no equivalent; without this the two documents would differ for a reason that\nhas nothing to do with either framework''s cost.\n\nThe Svelte client runtime is behind the same dynamic import react-dom is in the\nother stack, so a page with no island never downloads it. That matters MORE here,\nnot less: the runtime is 17.3 kB against React''s 56.3 kB but cannot be shared\nbetween remotes, so it is paid per remote rather than once.\n\nAlso puts the Svelte apps on the SAME ports as their React counterparts. The\ntopology is shared and only one stack runs at a time — MF_STACK picks the\ndirectory. Per-stack ports would mean the registry, the edge and every bench\nsuite needed a per-stack map too.\n\nFive of six apps now build clean, both environments; lint and typecheck clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"4442420da41094cdefcd1d6a3c7e972a7dee2a55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/4442420da41094cdefcd1d6a3c7e972a7dee2a55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDZiMDA1ZWJiNjZlZjY3OTFkZGVlNGQyZWQ1NjMzMDkyNmM0N2M1OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed","sha":"ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed"}],"sha":"6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/6b005ebb66ef6791ddee4d2ed56330926c47c597"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:21:26Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:21:26Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"rspack-svelte: the product remote, and two Svelte 5 reactivity bugs\n\nproduct: the faceted catalogue and the detail page — server-side filtering, sort\nand pagination as URL state, the gallery, the spec and document tables, the\nStockPanel CSS Module, and the account-overview widget. The loader lives in\nlist-data.ts so both the route module and the components can import it without a\ncycle.\n\nSvelte''s compiler caught two real bugs the React stack cannot have:\n\n`const v = variantOf(id)` in ProductThumb and `const Filled = slots[name]` in\nSlot capture only the FIRST value of a prop. Invisible in a single server render\nand wrong the moment the prop changes on the client — which the cart slots do.\nBoth are now $derived.\n\nThe fix for the second one was initially wrong in a way worth recording: moving\n`onUse?.(name)` into `$effect.pre` silenced the warning and would have broken\nper-route CSS injection, because $effect does not run during server rendering and\nonUse exists precisely so the SERVER can know which remote components rendered.\nIt is called during render again, which is safe — a server render is one\nsynchronous pass, and onUse is undefined on the client.\n\nAll four Svelte remotes build clean, both environments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"9132292724379564598ac4a8ca5f60c28a0e0f6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/9132292724379564598ac4a8ca5f60c28a0e0f6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGFiNWIzNTViYzc4ZDUzZjYxOTM1MDhjZTRkZmVmYjcxMGY2ZjgxZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a","sha":"85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a"}],"sha":"ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/ab5b355bc78d53f6193508ce4dfefb710f6f81ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:18:31Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:18:31Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"rspack-svelte: the faq and cart remotes\n\nfaq: the support centre and contact form, both server-rendered and never\nhydrated, plus the account-overview widget. Route modules are split into a\n`.route.ts` (loader + component re-export) beside the `.svelte` file, because a\nSvelte component file has exactly one default export and the loader cannot live\nin it. The shell sees no difference — RouteDescriptor.lazy is typed\nPromise<unknown> precisely so a stack can shape this how its framework requires.\n\ncart: all nine exposes, including the drawer, the cart page, both placeholders\nand the account widget. This is the app that proves the architecture was shaped\ncorrectly: cart state lives in @mf-eval/contracts as a framework-agnostic store\nwith a cookie behind it, so it crosses a boundary that Svelte''s own reactivity\ncannot — every Svelte remote has its own reactive graph.\n\nThe MiniCart placeholder keeps its CSS Module and emits identifiers identical to\nthe React stack''s (.cart-panel-V0TX), because localIdentName carries the app name\nand the stylesheet is the same. Two stacks, same class names, no coordination.\n\nMF''s DTS plugin is now off for Svelte apps: it cannot generate declarations from\na .svelte file, so it failed on every build and trained everyone to scroll past a\nred line. That is a genuine gap this stack has and the React one does not, and it\nbelongs in the porting guide rather than hidden behind a warning.\n\nAlso removes sass-embedded from the catalog: the pinned 1.95.0 does not exist on\nnpm and nothing referenced it — @rsbuild/plugin-sass brings its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"84d1d00bf46175555d1e835fd70dbd88f3dc02fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/84d1d00bf46175555d1e835fd70dbd88f3dc02fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDg1MTIwYmYyMjdiODEyMzQ0YjcyMjk0MThmY2Y4M2Q5Njk1NWI0NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253","sha":"d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253"}],"sha":"85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/85120bf227b812344b7229418fcf83d96955b44a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:33:27Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:33:27Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Fix three type errors in the framework-parameterised preset\n\nAll three were real, and one is worth recording: @rsbuild/plugin-svelte Omits\n`generate` from its compilerOptions type, on the assumption that the plugin picks\nthe target itself. It does not — there is one plugin per environment here and the\nnode one must compile for the server, which it does correctly at runtime. The\ncast says \"deliberately\" at the narrowest possible point.\n\nThe other two are exactOptionalPropertyTypes: an explicit `undefined` is not the\nsame as an absent key, so the node shared map is built by branch rather than by\nassigning a possibly-undefined value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"e7567b42f8eb9a5ffa27db57325f4db844d4338c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/e7567b42f8eb9a5ffa27db57325f4db844d4338c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGQ3ZDQyZDc0YjdhNDJhZTZkN2I5NTQ3OGIyMGE0YjMzMzliYjYyNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b","sha":"30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b"}],"sha":"d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/d7d42d74b7a42ae6d7b95478b20a4b3339bb6253"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:32:10Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:32:10Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"rspack-svelte: the chrome remote, and two Svelte/Rspack traps encoded in the preset\n\nFirst app of the second stack. Header and Footer, server-rendered and never\nhydrated, exposed to both hosts — same DOM, same class names, same test ids as\nthe React chrome.\n\nTwo traps are now impossible to hit rather than documented:\n\nThe Svelte plugin is wired PER ENVIRONMENT by the preset, with `generate:\n''server''` on the node build. Declaring it once at the root with a node-level\noverride produces a bundle containing BOTH compilations and a server render that\nreturns an empty string, with no error at build time or run time. No app can\nexpress the wrong shape because no app declares it at all.\n\nThe node build does not share `svelte` and externalises it. Sharing buys nothing\nserver-side — SSR is in-process, there is no share scope to deduplicate across —\nand keeping it shared makes MF bundle Svelte into the server build, which fails:\nSvelte ships SOURCE rather than compiled output, and Rspack''s optimizer mangles\nthe static private method in `internal/server/renderer.js` into something it\ncannot re-parse. The error names a line in Svelte''s own dist and nothing in this\nrepo. The browser build still bundles and shares it, which is where Svelte''s size\nis actually measured.\n\nVerified server-compiled rather than assumed: the exposed node module is\n`function Header($$renderer, $$props)` — Svelte 5''s server signature, not the\nclient''s `(anchor, props)` — and it references svelte/internal/server.\n\nReact stack untouched: typecheck and full build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"22b7f4da40e50e0c982c62e9b5f715116c420ae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/22b7f4da40e50e0c982c62e9b5f715116c420ae8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDMwYTk2N2JlNmMyNzAyMWFkYmZjNjFiZTU3Yjk0YWUzZjU1MjBiMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c","sha":"e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c"}],"sha":"30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/30a967be6c27021adbfc61be57b94ae3f5520b0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:26:30Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:26:30Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Foundation for a second stack: make the shared layer framework-agnostic\n\nGroundwork for stacks/rspack-svelte implementing the full reference app, so the\ntwo can be compared on the same 16 suites rather than on a spike.\n\nThe shared layer is now genuinely shared rather than React''s:\n\n- rsbuild-preset takes `framework: ''react'' | ''svelte''`. ONE preset, not one per\n  stack: the MF wiring, CSS scoping, asset prefixes, ESM output and cache digest\n  must be identical between stacks for the byte comparison to mean anything, and\n  two copies of that file would drift within a week.\n- shell-kit no longer imports React. It used `ComponentType` purely as a type\n  while resolving remotes it never renders; slots are now opaque and `loadChrome`\n  is generic over the caller''s component type, so each stack names it once at the\n  boundary instead of asserting at every JSX site.\n- SlotName moved to @mf-eval/contracts/slots. Both bindings must agree on the\n  names, and shell-kit resolves slots without knowing which framework renders\n  them — a second copy per binding would be the drift the test-id contract exists\n  to prevent.\n\nNew packages:\n\n- @mf-eval/svelte-contracts — the Svelte binding: cart context via a CartView\n  that bridges the framework-agnostic store''s React-shaped subscribe to a rune,\n  plus the Slot component. Shared as a singleton for the same identity reason as\n  the React one.\n- @mf-eval/design-svelte — 25 components, same DOM, same class names, same test\n  ids. Tokens are NOT duplicated: colours, sizes, spacing and the utility layer\n  stay in @mf-eval/design as plain CSS consumed unchanged by both stacks, which\n  is the only way the visual comparison holds.\n\nReact stack unchanged in behaviour: typecheck, lint and build clean, and the\nhosts, verify, contract and widgets suites stay green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"63684da75c7ac87d8e003154c7ba36ebfff919ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/63684da75c7ac87d8e003154c7ba36ebfff919ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKGU2Njc4MWRkODc3YzhlYWIwMmRiM2EyNTRmNDAwNzQyZGJkZTlmMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d","sha":"387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d"}],"sha":"e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/e66781dd877c8eab02db3a254f400742dbde9f2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:07:01Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:07:01Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Spike: is Module Federation possible with Svelte? Yes, with one real caveat\n\nEverything published on this question is a blog post, a forum thread with no\nerror message in it, or a demo that does not run. This repo''s premise is that a\nclaim without a check is marketing, so the question is answered by building it.\n\nWorks, verified by running it: a Svelte 5 remote exposing a component, a host\nloading it at runtime with no build-time dependency, $state and $derived still\nreactive after crossing the boundary, scoped component styles intact, and real\nSSR through svelte/server with props applied and hydration markers present.\n\nThe caveat is the finding no article states: you cannot share the Svelte runtime.\nSharing `svelte` works and is nearly worthless — it is the public API surface,\nnot where Svelte 5''s reactivity lives. Compiled components import\n`svelte/internal/client`, and sharing THAT leaves the container''s init promise\npermanently unsettled: every chunk 200s, no console error, no pageerror, no\nrejection, and the dynamic import simply never resolves. A crash would at least\nname a file.\n\nSo every Svelte remote carries a private 17.3 kB gzip runtime, and each copy is\nits own reactive graph — cross-remote reactive state is not inefficient, it is\nunavailable. Measured cost: a 0.96 kB component delivered by ~50 kB of\nmachinery. MF''s runtime-core alone is about the size of Svelte itself.\n\nThree further traps, all of which fail silently: exposes must be split per\nenvironment (svelte/server reaches node:async_hooks), the server build needs\ngenerate: ''server'', and the Svelte plugin must be declared per environment rather\nthan overridden — a root plugin plus a node override produced a bundle with BOTH\ncompilations and render() returned {} with no error anywhere.\n\nRecorded in docs/svelte-federation.md with the sharing matrix, the byte costs and\nwhat it would mean for a rspack-svelte stack — where the three-team widget page\nbecomes a much harsher test, and arguably the most valuable result this repo\ncould produce about Svelte.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"6e22e4de82b1a62976c574623ac0272904420436","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/6e22e4de82b1a62976c574623ac0272904420436"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/commits/387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d","node_id":"C_kwDOUClf-doAKDM4N2RjNDM3YmYyYzRkZTU4OTRjNzdmMDI1OGZiYjhlMzJkODY0NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commit/5a28007068e17c8b7691617f2849e830980ee547","sha":"5a28007068e17c8b7691617f2849e830980ee547","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/5a28007068e17c8b7691617f2849e830980ee547"}],"sha":"387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/387dc437bf2c4de5894c77f0258fbb8e32d8644d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287664814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sesa767979","id":287664814,"login":"sesa767979","node_id":"U_kgDOESVqrg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sesa767979","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/commits/5a28007068e17c8b7691617f2849e830980ee547/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T12:55:41Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T12:55:41Z","email":"SESA767979@se.com","name":"Tirth Bodawala"},"message":"Exclude results/ from the provenance dirty check\n\nThe run writes results/, so a bench in progress is always dirty there. Every\nrecord therefore claimed a dirty working tree even when the source it measured\nwas clean — which is worse than not reporting the flag at all, because it trains\nthe reader to ignore it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LtjvJvVNhKG5N1T121daxV","tree":{"sha":"94ea95261d15f85ec43bd1b7e61eb76eeb6fc024","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Atyantik/mfe-benchmarking/git/trees/94ea95261d15f85ec43bd1b7e61eb